{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghPkAXVNdqBBWLBPCNiX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01X2gR3pXrZibMazX2LAxjCB","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/PLAN.md","offset":500,"limit":500},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":15931,"cache_read_input_tokens":23986,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":15931},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf","uuid":"ed636e71-f1a5-4c6e-a604-b948a4aca178","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:11:59.555Z","request_id":"req_011CghPkAK65TMFV8V8ywbv1","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01X2gR3pXrZibMazX2LAxjCB":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/PLAN.md","offset":500,"limit":500}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X2gR3pXrZibMazX2LAxjCB","type":"tool_result","content":"500\t`M.now()` in seconds: `game.time` locally, or `AIHub.time() / 1000` in a hub session.\n501\t\n502\t**Closed form.** With τ = t − t0, e = exp(−kτ), k ≥ 1e-4:\n503\t\n504\t```\n505\tx = x0 + vx(1−e)/k\n506\ty = y0 + vy(1−e)/k + ay(τ/k − (1−e)/k²) + wobble(τ)            wobble = a·sin(wτ + ph)·min(1, τ/0.3)  (float serves)\n507\tz = z0 + (vz + g/k)(1−e)/k − gτ/k\n508\tvelocity: (vx·e,  vy·e + ay(1−e)/k,  (vz + g/k)e − g/k)\n509\t```\n510\t\n511\t- `ball.at(t)` and `ball.vel(t)` are sampled every step for drawing. There is no integration drift, and every machine\n512\t  agrees, which the online play relies on.\n513\t- **Aiming** (`aim(from, to, T)`): given a flight time T,\n514\t  - vx = (xT − x0)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)), and vy the same way (subtract the wind term when `ay` ≠ 0);\n515\t  - vz = ((zT − z0) + gT/k)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)) − g/k.\n516\t- **Flight times by kind:**\n517\t\n518\t| Kind | T |\n519\t| --- | --- |\n520\t| pass | `T.passT` (1.05 s) |\n521\t| set | `T.setT` (1.1 s); quick set .75 |\n522\t| float serve | `T.serveT` (1.3 s) |\n523\t| jump serve | `T.jumpServeT` (.85 s) |\n524\t| spike | from speed: horizontal distance / (spikeSpeed · cos 15°) |\n525\t| shot | `T.shotT` (.95 s) |\n526\t| free ball | 1.2 s |\n527\t| setter dump | .6 s |\n528\t\n529\t- **Precomputed events.** Each new launch computes these once:\n530\t  - `tNet`, when x crosses NET_X (x is monotonic). At that moment:\n531\t    - **clear** if z − r > NET_H;\n532\t    - **tape** (net cord) if z + r ≥ NET_H − 3. A new launch starts from the crossing point: with probability\n533\t      `T.netCordOver` it keeps going (vx·.35, vz 60 ± 20, from the `match` rng), otherwise it drops back (vx·−.3);\n534\t    - **net** if lower: it bounces back (vx·−.25, vy·.5, vz·.3), and the team still has its touches;\n535\t    - **antenna/outside** if |y − CY| > 64 + r: a fault on the team that hit it.\n536\t  - `tLand`, when z = r. Use bisection on the descending branch to 1e-4 s. The ball is **in** when\n537\t    X0 − r ≤ x ≤ X1 + r and Y0 − r ≤ y ≤ Y1 + r (touching the line is in).\n538\t  - `timeAtHeight(h)` (descending branch) and `posAt(t)`, for contact planning.\n539\t- **The ball itself:** radius r = 3.5; a 10-px sprite (white with blue and yellow panels) whose rotation follows its\n540\t  speed; a ground shadow `r.shadow(x, y, 4 − min(2, z·.03), .4)`. The shadow is essential for reading depth.\n541\t- **Landing:** dust (`particles.dust`), `sfx('sand')`, and a ball-mark decal for 2.5 s. The ball rolls about 6 units\n542\t  for show after the point is decided.\n543\t- Players may chase and play the ball outside the court lines, but never past the net plane.\n544\t\n545\t**Default feel** (all of these are sliders): g 330, k .12, r 3.5. With these numbers:\n546\t\n547\t| Shot | Path | Apex / timing |\n548\t| --- | --- | --- |\n549\t| pass | from z 18 to set height 40 | apex ≈ 75 |\n550\t| set | from 40 to the spike contact ≈ 62 | apex ≈ 100 |\n551\t| float serve | from 52 to the floor in 1.3 s | apex ≈ 98; clears the net by ≈ 40 |\n552\t| spike from 20 behind the net, 330 u/s | to 100 beyond the net | lands in ≈ .38 s; clears the tape by ≈ 7 |\n553\t\n554\tA spike hit from far behind the net with a short, sharp target hits the net. Errors come out of the physics.\n555\t\n556\t### 4.5 Rules and referee (`21-rules.js`)\n557\t\n558\t- **Scoring:** rally scoring; one set to `pointsToWin` (vacation 7, final 11, exhibition 7/11/15/21, hub 7); win by 2;\n559\t  hard cap at pointsToWin + 4 (to 7, the first to 11 wins even at 11–10). Exhibition can play best of 3 sets of the\n560\t  same length.\n561\t- **Touches:** at most 3 a side. A block counts as a touch (the beach rule). The same player may not touch twice in a\n562\t  row, except straight after her own block.\n563\t- **Faults** (point to the other team):\n564\t  - the ball lands out after the team's last touch;\n565\t  - a 4th touch;\n566\t  - a double touch;\n567\t  - the ball crosses outside the antennae or under the net;\n568\t  - a **net touch**: an airborne player's hands or body pass NET_X ± 2 while the ball is live within 40 units (rare;\n569\t    mostly from early, fast blocks);\n570\t  - a **serve fault**: into the net, out, or no hit within 1.2 s of the toss.\n571\t- **Serve rotation:** on a side-out the receiving team serves, and its server is the player who did not serve last time\n572\t  for that team. The first serve goes by coin toss: the player's team, unless an event says otherwise.\n573\t- **After a point:** `dead` (1.0 s: the ball settles) → `point` (1.6 s: celebrations) → optional replay → `serveSetup`.\n574\t- **Calls:** big banners with a whistle: \"IN!\", \"OUT!\", \"NET!\", \"4 TOUCHES\", \"DOUBLE TOUCH\", \"ANTENNA\", \"ACE!\", \"KILL!\",\n575\t  \"BLOCK!\", \"NET TOUCH\". Each is text plus an icon, never color alone.\n576\t- **Stats:**\n577\t\n578\t| Scope | Counted |\n579\t| --- | --- |\n580\t| per player | serves, aces, serve faults, digs, perfect passes, sets, kills, attack errors, blocks, points |\n581\t| per match | rallies, longest rally |\n582\t\n583\t### 4.6 Players, actions and the timing judge (`22-players.js`)\n584\t\n585\t**The player entity:** `{ id, side: 0 | 1, slot: 0 | 1, cast, rig, x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, facing, act, input | null, ai,\n586\tcall: 'auto' | 'mine' | 'yours', lockT, stats }`.\n587\t\n588\t**Movement.**\n589\t\n590\t- Speed is `T.runSpeed × (0.86 + 0.03 × SPD)`, default 96, with acceleration 900 u/s². Players face the ball while it\n591\t  is live.\n592\t- They can't cross NET_X (clamp at ±6). They can leave the court, but not the map.\n593\t- **Auto-run** (`T.autoMove`, Settings): while a human's stick is neutral and she is assigned the next contact, she\n594\t  steers toward the contact point at `autoMove ×` her speed.\n595\t\n596\t**Contact planning.** `planContacts(side)` runs whenever a launch heads to a side and after each touch on that side.\n597\tFor each player on that side it computes:\n598\t\n599\t- **kind**, by touch number: 0 = receive/dig, 1 = set, 2 = attack. A ball arriving from the other side is always\n600\t  touch 0.\n601\t- **contact height h:** bump 18; set 40; attack = that player's reach, about `50·size/1.25` plus her jump apex\n602\t  `12 + 1.2·JMP` (≈ 58–66). If the ball is too low to set or attack, fall back to bump height.\n603\t- **t\\*** = `timeAtHeight(h)`. If the ball never comes down to h, use tLand − .05 and the ball's height then: a dig.\n604\t- **P\\*** = `posAt(t*)` on the ground, and her travel time to it.\n605\t\n606\t**Assignment.**\n607\t\n608\t- A human's call wins: Mine gives her the ball and Yours gives it to the partner, provided that player can reach P* by\n609\t  t* + .1 s.\n610\t- Otherwise the faster arrival takes it; on a tie, whoever didn't make the previous touch.\n611\t- The partner **covers** a ball assigned to the human only when the human is more than 40 units from P* at t* − .4 s.\n612\t\n613\t**Timing ring.** A ground ring at P* (decal) shrinks from radius 22 to the reach radius over the last .8 s. It turns\n614\tfrom white to gold inside the PERFECT window, and a \"!\" pip appears over the head .35 s before t*. Settings can turn it\n615\toff, and the final's Golden Glare hides it (§4.8.6).\n616\t\n617\t**The judge.**\n618\t\n619\t- The **first** `play` press in [t* − .6, t* + okWin] counts; other presses do nothing. err = tPress − t*.\n620\t- PERFECT if |err| ≤ `T.perfectWin` (.05 s), GREAT if ≤ `T.greatWin` (.10), OK if ≤ `T.okWin` (.16); otherwise MISS:\n621\t  a whiff animation and a .45 s lock.\n622\t- **Reach check:** horizontal distance from the player to P* ≤ `T.reach` (14 + .4·TEC) keeps the judged quality; up to\n623\t  8 more gives a **stretch** (one quality lower); beyond that, a whiff.\n624\t- **Timing assist** multiplies the windows: Tight × .8, Normal × 1, Generous × 1.6.\n625\t- **Auto-receive** (Settings; forced on for the tutorial's first 2 receives): with no press by t*, a receive (not a set\n626\t  or spike) happens at OK quality.\n627\t- No press means the ball passes her. If it lands, the point is lost, unless the partner covered it (see Assignment\n628\t  above).\n629\t\n630\t**What each quality does:**\n631\t\n632\t| Quality | Accuracy radius around the intended target | Speed |\n633\t| --- | --- | --- |\n634\t| PERFECT | 4 | × 1.12 |\n635\t| GREAT | 10 | × 1.0 |\n636\t| OK | 20 | × .85 |\n637\t| stretch | 30 | × .8 |\n638\t\n639\t**Actions:**\n640\t\n641\t| Action | Input | What happens |\n642\t| --- | --- | --- |\n643\t| **Receive / dig** (touch 0) | Play | Bump to the **pass target** (NET_X ∓ 40, the partner's y) in passT; the stick biases the target ±24. Holding **Shot** instead sends a free ball over the net to the deepest open zone. |\n644\t| **Set** (touch 1) | Play | Set to the **attack spot** (NET_X ∓ 22, the hitter's y) in setT. Stick neutral = high set; toward the net = quick set (T .75, lower apex); away = back set. **Shot** = setter dump (a tip to the nearest open short zone, T .6). |\n645\t| **Attack** (touch 2) | Play = spike, Shot = cut/roll shot | She approaches and jumps on her own: the jump starts at t* − jumpTime(JMP) so her hand meets the ball at t*. The press at t* swings. Spike speed is `T.spikeSpeed × (0.85 + .035·POW) × quality`; a shot takes shotT and peaks just over the block. If she wasn't in reach (a bad set), the press makes a high, soft free ball. |\n646\t| **Aim** | Stick at contact, or mouse | Pad and keyboard pick one of 9 zones on the opponents' half: neutral = deep centre, up/down on screen = line or cross-court, toward the net = short angle, away = deep. With the mouse as the last device, the reticle's ground point is the target, clamped 6 inside the lines. Quality then scatters by the radius above, which can push it out. |\n647\t| **Spike assist** | difficulty | If the aimed spike can't clear the net from the contact point, raise the arc just enough: always on Easy; on Normal only when the miss would be under 4 units; never on Hard or Pro, where it goes into the net. |\n648\t| **Serve** | Play (float) or Shot (jump serve) to toss; the same button again at the top of the toss | Before the toss she walks along the baseline with the stick. The hit's timing is judged against the toss apex with the same windows. Aim with the stick or mouse; a target marker shows during the toss. Jump serves are faster and scatter × 1.5. No second press within 1.2 s is a serve fault. AI serves after 1.2–2.5 s; a human gets an automatic float serve after 10 s. |\n649\t| **Block** | Shot, within 20 of the net while the opponents attack | She jumps; her hands reach the top `T.blockRise` (.28 s) after the press and stay up .18 s. When the spike crosses the net plane, it is blocked if abs(y_ball − y_blocker) ≤ 9 + .6·JMP and NET_H ≤ z_ball ≤ handTop(t). Timing error = (tPress + blockRise) − tNet. PERFECT or GREAT is a **stuff** (back down on the attacker's side: v = (−.35vx, .3vy ± 20, −60)). OK is a **soft block**: it pops up on her side as a touch. Cut shots arc over the block unless she has JMP 9 and timed it PERFECT. |\n650\t| **Dive** | Dive | Lunge toward the stick (or toward P* when neutral) at 190 u/s for .22 s, slide .3 s, down .45 s. Reach is +`T.diveReach` (16) during the lunge. A judged Play press during it is a **dig**: accuracy radius × 1.6 and a higher apex. A dive with no ball is just the lunge and recovery. |\n651\t| **Call** | Call | Cycles mine → yours → auto. A speech bubble (\"MINE!\" / \"YOURS!\") appears with a gibberish shout. AI teammates call too (\"MINE!\" when they take a ball). |\n652\t\n653\tEvery action sets the rig state `{ act, phase, u }` for animation (§4.26).\n654\t\n655\t### 4.7 AI (`23-ai.js`)\n656\t\n657\t**Skill.** Each AI player, for each touch, has\n658\t`skill = clamp((base × T.aiSkillMul + difficulty) × (0.8 + 0.05 × stat) × chem, 0, 1)`:\n659\t\n660\t- `base` is the day's value (§5.6);\n661\t- `difficulty` is the setting's offset: Easy −.2, Normal 0, Hard +.12, Pro +.22;\n662\t- `stat` is the stat the touch uses: TEC for passes, digs and sets; POW for attacks and serves; JMP for blocks. SPD\n663\t  scales movement speed instead (§4.6).\n664\t- `chem` is 1 for opponents. For the player's AI partner it is `(1 − T.chemistry/2) + T.chemistry × affinity/100`; the\n665\t  default `T.chemistry` .3 gives .85–1.15.\n666\t\n667\t**Reaction.** She starts toward P* `T.aiReaction × (1.2 − skill)` s after a launch, and moves at speed × `T.aiSpeedMul`.\n668\t\n669\t**Errors per touch.** Roll on the `match` rng:\n670\t\n671\t| Outcome | Probability |\n672\t| --- | --- |\n673\t| PERFECT | .10 + .45·skill |\n674\t| GREAT | .30 |\n675\t| MISS | max(.02, .16·(1 − skill)): a shank in a random direction, or no touch |\n676\t| OK | the rest |\n677\t\n678\t**Formation by phase:**\n679\t\n680\t| Phase | Positions |\n681\t| --- | --- |\n682\t| receiving serve | split the court in y, 40% deep |\n683\t| own attack | the setter under the pass target; the hitter backs off for her approach |\n684\t| defending an attack | if the set is near the net and a skill roll passes, one blocks in line with the attacker; the other defends deep cross-court |\n685\t| free ball | both back |\n686\t\n687\t**Decisions.**\n688\t\n689\t- **Attack target:** of the 9 zones, the one with the largest \"distance to the nearest defender's predicted spot minus\n690\t  her reach\", minus 8·(1 − skill) for zones within 10 of a line.\n691\t- **Shot or spike:** a shot when a blocker is up and in line, plus 20% at random for variety.\n692\t- **Serve:** float 70% and jump 30% (50% jump when POW ≥ 8), aimed at the deep corners or the seam between receivers.\n693\t- **Setter dump:** 8% when the opponents' front court is empty.\n694\t\n695\t**AI with a human teammate.** Beach pattern: whoever passes, attacks. When the human passes, the AI sets back to her;\n696\twhen the AI passes, the human sets and the AI attacks.\n697\t\n698\t**Spectacle mode** (attract only): perfect skill until the rally reaches a random 3–9 touches, then the attacking side's\n699\tspike goes into the biggest gap, a guaranteed kill.\n700\t\n701\t**Determinism.** Every roll comes from `G.rng('match')`, so the same seed and inputs give the same score (tested).\n702\t\n703\t### 4.8 Match flow and presentation (`24-match.js`)\n704\t\n705\t**4.8.1 Phases.** `intro` → `coin` → `serveSetup` → `toss` → `rally` → `dead` → `point` → [`replay`] → … →\n706\t`matchPoint` sting → `end`.\n707\t\n708\t- `intro`: walk-on, Sonny's PA line, the teams line up at the net; 3 s, skippable.\n709\t- `coin`: who serves; 1 s.\n710\t\n711\t**4.8.2 Cameras.**\n712\t\n713\t- **Broadcast:** `cam.frame([ball, ...players, netTop], { margin: 28, zoom: [.78, 1] })` with `cam.smooth` .22. During\n714\t  `serveSetup` it frames the server and the receivers.\n715\t- **Serve Cam:** follows the ball's x with a lead, fixed at the court's centre y, zoom .9.\n716\t- `view` (V / R3) toggles them; Settings has \"Match camera\". The scene's `camera: { zoom: [.85, 1.25] }` lets the\n717\t  player nudge the zoom.\n718\t\n719\t**4.8.3 HUD** (pixel art, anchored to the screen):\n720\t\n721\t| Where | What |\n722\t| --- | --- |\n723\t| top left | TV score bug: per team two small portraits, names, score, a serve ball icon, set count, and a MATCH POINT tag |\n724\t| top right | ClockBadge (vacation) or the hub clock |\n725\t| bottom left | partner card: portrait, name, hearts = chemistry, mood |\n726\t| bottom centre | context prompts (at most 3, e.g. \"✕ BUMP · ○ DIVE · △ CALL\") |\n727\t| at players | judgement popups (PERFECT! gold, GREAT cyan, OK white, MISS grey) and call bubbles |\n728\t| bottom right | commentary box: `E.Dialog` with `modal: false, auto: 2.2`, Sonny's portrait, his voice |\n729\t\n730\t**4.8.4 Crowd and set dressing.**\n731\t\n732\t- 24 spectators on the far-side bleachers and towels, drawn as small pixel sprites like the sports kit's crowd, plus 4\n733\t  HD rigs at size .9 drawn `every: 2`. They sway, jump and cheer on points (more for the home side) and groan at errors.\n734\t- Sonny reacts at his DJ booth.\n735\t- Pepper sits at the scorer's table beside a flip scoreboard shape whose cards change with the score.\n736\t- Night matches add floodlights (lights) and tiki torches.\n737\t\n738\t**4.8.5 Celebrations.**\n739\t\n740\t| Moment | Animation |\n741\t| --- | --- |\n742\t| point won | the partners high-five (§4.26), plus a fist pump |\n743\t| ace, kill or block | the scorer's signature celebration |\n744\t| point lost | a shrug, an encouraging pat or a facepalm (short) |\n745\t| match won | both cheer, then the MVP's signature move |\n746\t| match lost | kneel and sigh |\n747\t\n748\tAll of these fit inside the `point` phase.\n749\t\n750\t**4.8.6 Specials in the final against Sonny & Pepper (\"The House\").** Each is telegraphed in Pepper's Day 4 letter and\n751\tby the commentary.\n752\t\n753\t- **Golden Glare:** half of Sonny's serves. His sunglasses flash (a .6 s telegraph: glint particle, `sfx('glare')`), and\n754\t  the receiving human's timing ring is hidden for that serve (\"DAZZLED!\"). A receiver wearing **any sunglasses**\n755\t  accessory is immune (\"SHADES ON!\").\n756\t- **House Edge:** once per set Pepper hits a precise line shot. The AI partner covers it only at chemistry Good Friend\n757\t  or better (\"I've got line!\").\n758\t- **Lucky Seven:** the first time The House reaches game point, Sonny's next attack clips the tape and is guaranteed to\n759\t  dribble over.\n760\t\n761\t**4.8.7 Highlight replay.**\n762\t\n763\t- Keep a ring buffer of the last 6 s at 60 Hz: rig states, launches and camera.\n764\t- After an ace, a stuff block, a spike over 400 u/s, or a rally of 8+ touches (at most once every 3 points), replay the\n765\t  last 3 s at .4× from the other camera with a \"REPLAY\" letterbox. Any button skips.\n766\t- Off in hub sessions.\n767\t\n768\t**4.8.8 Results.**\n769\t\n770\t- The winners pose.\n771\t- Three big stat cards: points, kills, longest rally. The MVP (most points) gets a portrait and her signature move.\n772\t- Vacation: prize money counts up, the partner's affinity change animates as hearts, then **Continue**.\n773\t- Beach Match: Rematch / Change setup / Title.\n774\t\n775\t**4.8.9 Sound.**\n776\t\n777\t- The match song `spike` has a named drum layer `rally` that comes in on long rallies (`audio.layer`). At match point\n778\t  the tempo goes up by 6 (`audio.tempo`) with a sting.\n779\t- Ball sounds per kind, the whistle, crowd swells, and Sonny's PA voice.\n780\t\n781\t### 4.9 Beach Match: exhibition and local multiplayer (`52-exhibition.js`)\n782\t\n783\t**The setup screen.** Four columns, one per slot (Left 1, Left 2, Right 1, Right 2). Each shows a fighter on a pedestal\n784\tand who controls it: CPU or P1–P4.\n785\t\n786\t- **Joining:** `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`. Start or ✕ on a free pad, or 2 on the keyboard (the split halves).\n787\t- **Each joined player:** left/right moves her badge between slots; up/down picks the fighter; □ picks the outfit\n788\t  (signature suits, plus suits ever owned in a vacation, or every suit once a vacation is finished); ✕ is ready.\n789\t- **Options row:** points (7/11/15/21), sets (1/3), difficulty, court time (Morning/Sunset/Night), camera.\n790\t- The match starts when every joined player is ready.\n791\t\n792\t**Any mix works:** 1P with a CPU partner vs CPU; 2P co-op vs CPU; 1v1 with CPU partners; 2v2; 3 players (2 vs 1 + CPU).\n793\t\n794\tEach player's prompts use her own device (`p.input.label`, per-player glyph style). Results offer Rematch / Change setup\n795\t/ Title.\n796\t\n797\t### 4.10 Calendar, slots, weather, schedules, moods (`30-vacation.js`)\n798\t\n799\t**Days and slots.** `DAYS = 5` (data). Slots are Morning (06–12), Afternoon (12–18) and Night (18–24). The ClockBadge\n800\tshows \"Day 2 · Afternoon\" with weather.\n801\t\n802\t**What uses up a slot:** finishing a match; finishing Pool Hop; leaving a location you entered (the confirm says\n803\t\"Leaving ends the Morning.\"); leaving the casino at night; Rest in the villa. Talking, gifting, shopping and changing\n804\tclothes inside a location don't.\n805\t\n806\t**At night** only the Villa, the Casino and story events are open. The map shows the rest as closed.\n807\t\n808\t**Day start** (seeded from `world`):\n809\t\n810\t- roll moods, form NPC teams, place NPCs by schedule, pick each shop's 2 daily deals, and add any items whose day has\n811\t  come (§4.12);\n812\t- set the weather from the table: D1 sunny; D2 sunny or cloudy; D3 cloudy morning, rain in the afternoon, clear night;\n813\t  D4 sunny; D5 sunny with a golden afternoon (sunset light);\n814\t- autosave.\n815\t\n816\t**Day end (sleep)** shows a summary card: money earned and spent, matches, affinity changes (arrows by each portrait),\n817\ttomorrow's weather. Then:\n818\t\n819\t- your partner leaves if you lost a match that day and her affinity is below 35;\n820\t- affinity drifts `T.affinityDecay` (2) toward its base value for every NPC you didn't talk to;\n821\t- NPC pairs \"play\" each other off-screen for that day's record: one simulated result per pair from skills on the\n822\t  `world` rng. The Match Board shows records like \"Lola & Tess 3–1\".\n823\t\n824\t**Schedules** (weights in §5.4).\n825\t\n826\t- Each NPC has weights over locations for each slot, changed by weather and mood; the `world` rng picks.\n827\t- NPC team-mates go together, to the place chosen for the first one.\n828\t- Story events override the schedule.\n829\t- Guarantee at least one NPC pair at the Beach in every daytime slot.\n830\t- Your partner isn't scheduled: she \"jogs over\" whenever you open the Match Board.\n831\t\n832\t**Moods.**\n833\t\n834\t| Mood | Icon and word |\n835\t| --- | --- |\n836\t| Happy | ☀ |\n837\t| Normal | ◐ |\n838\t| Gloomy | ☁ |\n839\t\n840\tDaily roll 35/45/20. One step up if the weather is one she likes; one step down if you beat her yesterday or the\n841\tweather is one she dislikes. Mood shifts gift thresholds and invite chances.\n842\t\n843\t### 4.11 Affinity, gifts and team-ups (`30-vacation.js`, `32-location.js`)\n844\t\n845\t**Affinity** is 0–100 between you and each NPC: one symmetric number per pair, shown as 5 hearts in half steps. Start\n846\tvalues come from the table in §5.3.\n847\t\n848\t| Stage | Affinity |\n849\t| --- | --- |\n850\t| Stranger | 0–19 |\n851\t| Acquaintance | 20–39 |\n852\t| Friend | 40–59 |\n853\t| Good Friend | 60–79 |\n854\t| Best Friend | 80–100 |\n855\t\n856\t**Changes.** Positive changes are multiplied by `T.affinityGainMul`.\n857\t\n858\t| Cause | Change |\n859\t| --- | --- |\n860\t| chat, first of the day | +2 |\n861\t| chat, later (once per slot) | +1 |\n862\t| gift loved / liked / neutral | +12 / +6 / +2 |\n863\t| gift disliked | −6 (and the gift comes back to your bag) |\n864\t| your team wins / loses | +6 / −2 (−5 if she is Gloomy) |\n865\t| you beat her team | −3 (+1 for good sports: Tess and Rin) |\n866\t| event choices | ±4 |\n867\t| winning the final, for your partner | +10 |\n868\t\n869\t**Gift acceptance.** score = taste + stage bonus + mood.\n870\t\n871\t- taste: love 3, like 2, neutral 0, dislike −3;\n872\t- stage bonus: Friend 1, Good Friend 1, Best Friend 2;\n873\t- mood: Happy +1, Normal 0, Gloomy −1.\n874\t\n875\tShe accepts if score ≥ `T.giftThreshold` (0). So neutral gifts are accepted unless she is a Gloomy stranger, and\n876\tdislikes are refused unless she is a Happy Best Friend. One gift per NPC per slot.\n877\t\n878\t**Reactions:**\n879\t\n880\t| Reaction | Animation and sound |\n881\t| --- | --- |\n882\t| love | jumps, a burst of hearts, \"I love it!\"-style line, jingle `gift_love` |\n883\t| like | smile and nod |\n884\t| neutral | polite nod |\n885\t| refuse | folded arms and a head shake (`Reject` or `Idle_FoldArms`), jingle `gift_refuse` |\n886\t\n887\t**Known likes.** The first time you see her reaction to an item, record it in `known[npc][item]`. The Villa journal's\n888\tFriends page shows what you've learned as icons.\n889\t\n890\t**Team-up.**\n891\t\n892\t- She accepts if affinity ≥ `T.inviteThreshold` (40), with the threshold −10 if she's Happy and +10 if Gloomy.\n893\t- If she's already on an NPC team she needs 20 more. Her old team-mate then goes solo and is sour with you (−4).\n894\t- You have one partner at a time. Switching asks first (\"Tess will be disappointed…\").\n895\t- Partner chemistry is her affinity, shown as hearts on the match HUD.\n896\t\n897\t**Swimsuit gifts.** A suit you give must match one of her tastes or she refuses it (\"Not really my style\"). An accepted\n898\tsuit becomes her outfit (in matches and around the island), and she keeps it.\n899\t\n900\t### 4.12 Money, shops, wardrobe, inventory (`33-shop.js`)\n901\t\n902\t**Currency:** Sonny Dollars, written S$12,500. You start with S$30,000 (`T.startMoney`).\n903\t\n904\t**Income** (match prizes × `T.prizeMul`):\n905\t\n906\t| Source | Amount |\n907\t| --- | --- |\n908\t| match win | S$ (12,000 + 3,000·day + 1,000·winning margin) |\n909\t| match loss | S$3,000 |\n910\t| tutorial | S$10,000 |\n911\t| semifinal win | S$30,000 |\n912\t| final win | S$100,000 and the \"Fortuna Gold\" suit |\n913\t| Pool Hop | S$ (2,000 + 400·perfects + 150·seconds left) |\n914\t| casino | chips cashed out at S$100 each |\n915\t\n916\t**Shops**, all on the Promenade. Each shows its whole stock from §5.2. Items marked \"Day N+\" arrive on that day and\n917\tcarry a NEW badge for it. Every day each shop also has **2 daily deals at −25%**, picked by the `world` rng. Prices ×\n918\t`T.priceMul`.\n919\t\n920\t| Shop | Keeper | Sells |\n921\t| --- | --- | --- |\n922\t| **Riptide Sports** | Coach Bo | sporty suits, sports accessories, sports gifts |\n923\t| **Coral Couture** | Odette | fashion suits and accessories, fashion gifts |\n924\t| **Sundries & Smiles** | Kai | food, goods and books gifts, the luchador mask |\n925\t\n926\t**The shop screen.**\n927\t\n928\t- Category tabs; a 3×2 card grid; a detail panel.\n929\t- For suits and accessories, a **live rig of your fighter wearing the focused item** turns on a pedestal (right stick,\n930\t  L1/R1 or a mouse drag). □ \"Try on\" switches between the item and your current outfit.\n931\t- ✕ buys. A confirm appears when the price is over 30% of your money.\n932\t- Badges show OWNED and WEARING. Items you can't afford are dimmed with the shortfall shown.\n933\t- The keeper's portrait says a short quip, with voice.\n934\t\n935\t**Wardrobe** (the Villa closet, and the changing hut at the Beach and Pool): the suits and accessories you own; ✕\n936\tequip, □ remove an accessory, the same rotating preview. A second page shows your partner and the suits she has\n937\taccepted.\n938\t\n939\t**Gift Bag:** counts per gift, sorted by category, at most 9 of each. Opened from talk menus, or with □ on the map or in\n940\ta location to browse.\n941\t\n942\t### 4.13 Island map (`31-map.js`)\n943\t\n944\t**The map:** an iso view of Isla Fortuna, a TileMap of about 48×36 tiles.\n945\t\n946\t- Sea all round (`outside` set to the sea color, animated water floor at the edges); beaches, grass, palm groves.\n947\t- A dormant volcano: stepped rock walls, 3 levels, with steam wisps.\n948\t- The lagoon pool, the courts, the Promenade, a row of villas, the casino (neon at night), the Dock with Sonny's\n949\t  seaplane, a lighthouse.\n950\t\n951\t**Pins:** Sunset Courts, Lagoon Pool, Fortuna Promenade, Your Villa, Casino Fortuna (night only), and the Dock (shown\n952\tgreyed: \"Departures only\").\n953\t\n954\t**Controls.**\n955\t\n956\t- The stick or d-pad jumps the cursor to the nearest pin in that direction; L1/R1 cycle pins; mouse hover highlights\n957\t  (`r.pick`).\n958\t- ✕ or a click opens the **location card**: name, a small picture, who's there (portraits with mood icons, NPC pairs\n959\t  marked), activities, open or closed. ✕ again travels, with an `iris` transition at the pin.\n960\t- □ opens Friends (affinity overview), △ the Journal (save, stats), Options pauses.\n961\t\n962\t**The header** shows the ClockBadge, the MoneyBadge and the partner card.\n963\t\n964\t**Sky and weather:** a morning pastel sky, a bright afternoon, a night of stars, lit windows and neon; weather\n965\tparticles.\n966\t\n967\t### 4.14 Walkable locations (`32-location.js`)\n968\t\n969\t**One scene, driven by data per location** (§5.4): a TileMap in `threequarter`, the outside color or a backdrop,\n970\tshapes (`map.solid` for collision), NPC spots, interactables, music and ambience, exits.\n971\t\n972\t- **You:** an `E.Body` (r 5) moving at 70 units/s walking and 110 running, with the camera on you\n973\t  (`game.follow(hero, { z: 16 })`, `cam.bounds`). Lights and GPU lighting come on at night.\n974\t- **NPCs present** (from the schedule) sit at spots doing idle activities and turn their heads toward you within 40\n975\t  units.\n976\t- **Talk.** Interact within 22 units opens the talk panel: her portrait, mood, hearts, and a vertical list.\n977\t\n978\t| Choice | Notes |\n979\t| --- | --- |\n980\t| **Chat** | |\n981\t| **Give a Gift** | |\n982\t| **Team Up** | if she isn't your partner; for your partner: \"Our next match?\", which opens the Match Board |\n983\t| **Challenge** | beach only, when she's in a pair |\n984\t| **Bye** | |\n985\t\n986\t- **Interactables:**\n987\t\n988\t| Place | Interactables |\n989\t| --- | --- |\n990\t| Beach | Match Board (challengeable pairs with difficulty stars and records, your partner, Play), changing hut (Wardrobe) |\n991\t| Pool | Pool Hop start deck, changing hut (Wardrobe) |\n992\t| Promenade | the three shop doors |\n993\t| Villa | bed (Rest / Sleep), closet (Wardrobe), desk (Journal), album frame, mailbox (letters) |\n994\t| Casino floor (its own scene, §4.16) | cashier, slot machines, blackjack table, roulette table, prize counter, VIP lounge (events) |\n995\t\n996\t- **Leaving:** walk to the exit, or press `leave` (△ / M / Tab), then confirm \"Leave? This ends the Afternoon.\" Back on\n997\t  the map, it is the next slot.\n998\t\n999\t### 4.15 Pool Hop (`40-poolhop.js`)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf","uuid":"dfb4746f-a868-45af-8279-f282225d7828","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:11:59.695Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/PLAN.md","content":"`M.now()` in seconds: `game.time` locally, or `AIHub.time() / 1000` in a hub session.\n\n**Closed form.** With τ = t − t0, e = exp(−kτ), k ≥ 1e-4:\n\n```\nx = x0 + vx(1−e)/k\ny = y0 + vy(1−e)/k + ay(τ/k − (1−e)/k²) + wobble(τ)            wobble = a·sin(wτ + ph)·min(1, τ/0.3)  (float serves)\nz = z0 + (vz + g/k)(1−e)/k − gτ/k\nvelocity: (vx·e,  vy·e + ay(1−e)/k,  (vz + g/k)e − g/k)\n```\n\n- `ball.at(t)` and `ball.vel(t)` are sampled every step for drawing. There is no integration drift, and every machine\n  agrees, which the online play relies on.\n- **Aiming** (`aim(from, to, T)`): given a flight time T,\n  - vx = (xT − x0)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)), and vy the same way (subtract the wind term when `ay` ≠ 0);\n  - vz = ((zT − z0) + gT/k)·k / (1 − e^(−kT)) − g/k.\n- **Flight times by kind:**\n\n| Kind | T |\n| --- | --- |\n| pass | `T.passT` (1.05 s) |\n| set | `T.setT` (1.1 s); quick set .75 |\n| float serve | `T.serveT` (1.3 s) |\n| jump serve | `T.jumpServeT` (.85 s) |\n| spike | from speed: horizontal distance / (spikeSpeed · cos 15°) |\n| shot | `T.shotT` (.95 s) |\n| free ball | 1.2 s |\n| setter dump | .6 s |\n\n- **Precomputed events.** Each new launch computes these once:\n  - `tNet`, when x crosses NET_X (x is monotonic). At that moment:\n    - **clear** if z − r > NET_H;\n    - **tape** (net cord) if z + r ≥ NET_H − 3. A new launch starts from the crossing point: with probability\n      `T.netCordOver` it keeps going (vx·.35, vz 60 ± 20, from the `match` rng), otherwise it drops back (vx·−.3);\n    - **net** if lower: it bounces back (vx·−.25, vy·.5, vz·.3), and the team still has its touches;\n    - **antenna/outside** if |y − CY| > 64 + r: a fault on the team that hit it.\n  - `tLand`, when z = r. Use bisection on the descending branch to 1e-4 s. The ball is **in** when\n    X0 − r ≤ x ≤ X1 + r and Y0 − r ≤ y ≤ Y1 + r (touching the line is in).\n  - `timeAtHeight(h)` (descending branch) and `posAt(t)`, for contact planning.\n- **The ball itself:** radius r = 3.5; a 10-px sprite (white with blue and yellow panels) whose rotation follows its\n  speed; a ground shadow `r.shadow(x, y, 4 − min(2, z·.03), .4)`. The shadow is essential for reading depth.\n- **Landing:** dust (`particles.dust`), `sfx('sand')`, and a ball-mark decal for 2.5 s. The ball rolls about 6 units\n  for show after the point is decided.\n- Players may chase and play the ball outside the court lines, but never past the net plane.\n\n**Default feel** (all of these are sliders): g 330, k .12, r 3.5. With these numbers:\n\n| Shot | Path | Apex / timing |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| pass | from z 18 to set height 40 | apex ≈ 75 |\n| set | from 40 to the spike contact ≈ 62 | apex ≈ 100 |\n| float serve | from 52 to the floor in 1.3 s | apex ≈ 98; clears the net by ≈ 40 |\n| spike from 20 behind the net, 330 u/s | to 100 beyond the net | lands in ≈ .38 s; clears the tape by ≈ 7 |\n\nA spike hit from far behind the net with a short, sharp target hits the net. Errors come out of the physics.\n\n### 4.5 Rules and referee (`21-rules.js`)\n\n- **Scoring:** rally scoring; one set to `pointsToWin` (vacation 7, final 11, exhibition 7/11/15/21, hub 7); win by 2;\n  hard cap at pointsToWin + 4 (to 7, the first to 11 wins even at 11–10). Exhibition can play best of 3 sets of the\n  same length.\n- **Touches:** at most 3 a side. A block counts as a touch (the beach rule). The same player may not touch twice in a\n  row, except straight after her own block.\n- **Faults** (point to the other team):\n  - the ball lands out after the team's last touch;\n  - a 4th touch;\n  - a double touch;\n  - the ball crosses outside the antennae or under the net;\n  - a **net touch**: an airborne player's hands or body pass NET_X ± 2 while the ball is live within 40 units (rare;\n    mostly from early, fast blocks);\n  - a **serve fault**: into the net, out, or no hit within 1.2 s of the toss.\n- **Serve rotation:** on a side-out the receiving team serves, and its server is the player who did not serve last time\n  for that team. The first serve goes by coin toss: the player's team, unless an event says otherwise.\n- **After a point:** `dead` (1.0 s: the ball settles) → `point` (1.6 s: celebrations) → optional replay → `serveSetup`.\n- **Calls:** big banners with a whistle: \"IN!\", \"OUT!\", \"NET!\", \"4 TOUCHES\", \"DOUBLE TOUCH\", \"ANTENNA\", \"ACE!\", \"KILL!\",\n  \"BLOCK!\", \"NET TOUCH\". Each is text plus an icon, never color alone.\n- **Stats:**\n\n| Scope | Counted |\n| --- | --- |\n| per player | serves, aces, serve faults, digs, perfect passes, sets, kills, attack errors, blocks, points |\n| per match | rallies, longest rally |\n\n### 4.6 Players, actions and the timing judge (`22-players.js`)\n\n**The player entity:** `{ id, side: 0 | 1, slot: 0 | 1, cast, rig, x, y, z, vx, vy, vz, facing, act, input | null, ai,\ncall: 'auto' | 'mine' | 'yours', lockT, stats }`.\n\n**Movement.**\n\n- Speed is `T.runSpeed × (0.86 + 0.03 × SPD)`, default 96, with acceleration 900 u/s². Players face the ball while it\n  is live.\n- They can't cross NET_X (clamp at ±6). They can leave the court, but not the map.\n- **Auto-run** (`T.autoMove`, Settings): while a human's stick is neutral and she is assigned the next contact, she\n  steers toward the contact point at `autoMove ×` her speed.\n\n**Contact planning.** `planContacts(side)` runs whenever a launch heads to a side and after each touch on that side.\nFor each player on that side it computes:\n\n- **kind**, by touch number: 0 = receive/dig, 1 = set, 2 = attack. A ball arriving from the other side is always\n  touch 0.\n- **contact height h:** bump 18; set 40; attack = that player's reach, about `50·size/1.25` plus her jump apex\n  `12 + 1.2·JMP` (≈ 58–66). If the ball is too low to set or attack, fall back to bump height.\n- **t\\*** = `timeAtHeight(h)`. If the ball never comes down to h, use tLand − .05 and the ball's height then: a dig.\n- **P\\*** = `posAt(t*)` on the ground, and her travel time to it.\n\n**Assignment.**\n\n- A human's call wins: Mine gives her the ball and Yours gives it to the partner, provided that player can reach P* by\n  t* + .1 s.\n- Otherwise the faster arrival takes it; on a tie, whoever didn't make the previous touch.\n- The partner **covers** a ball assigned to the human only when the human is more than 40 units from P* at t* − .4 s.\n\n**Timing ring.** A ground ring at P* (decal) shrinks from radius 22 to the reach radius over the last .8 s. It turns\nfrom white to gold inside the PERFECT window, and a \"!\" pip appears over the head .35 s before t*. Settings can turn it\noff, and the final's Golden Glare hides it (§4.8.6).\n\n**The judge.**\n\n- The **first** `play` press in [t* − .6, t* + okWin] counts; other presses do nothing. err = tPress − t*.\n- PERFECT if |err| ≤ `T.perfectWin` (.05 s), GREAT if ≤ `T.greatWin` (.10), OK if ≤ `T.okWin` (.16); otherwise MISS:\n  a whiff animation and a .45 s lock.\n- **Reach check:** horizontal distance from the player to P* ≤ `T.reach` (14 + .4·TEC) keeps the judged quality; up to\n  8 more gives a **stretch** (one quality lower); beyond that, a whiff.\n- **Timing assist** multiplies the windows: Tight × .8, Normal × 1, Generous × 1.6.\n- **Auto-receive** (Settings; forced on for the tutorial's first 2 receives): with no press by t*, a receive (not a set\n  or spike) happens at OK quality.\n- No press means the ball passes her. If it lands, the point is lost, unless the partner covered it (see Assignment\n  above).\n\n**What each quality does:**\n\n| Quality | Accuracy radius around the intended target | Speed |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| PERFECT | 4 | × 1.12 |\n| GREAT | 10 | × 1.0 |\n| OK | 20 | × .85 |\n| stretch | 30 | × .8 |\n\n**Actions:**\n\n| Action | Input | What happens |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Receive / dig** (touch 0) | Play | Bump to the **pass target** (NET_X ∓ 40, the partner's y) in passT; the stick biases the target ±24. Holding **Shot** instead sends a free ball over the net to the deepest open zone. |\n| **Set** (touch 1) | Play | Set to the **attack spot** (NET_X ∓ 22, the hitter's y) in setT. Stick neutral = high set; toward the net = quick set (T .75, lower apex); away = back set. **Shot** = setter dump (a tip to the nearest open short zone, T .6). |\n| **Attack** (touch 2) | Play = spike, Shot = cut/roll shot | She approaches and jumps on her own: the jump starts at t* − jumpTime(JMP) so her hand meets the ball at t*. The press at t* swings. Spike speed is `T.spikeSpeed × (0.85 + .035·POW) × quality`; a shot takes shotT and peaks just over the block. If she wasn't in reach (a bad set), the press makes a high, soft free ball. |\n| **Aim** | Stick at contact, or mouse | Pad and keyboard pick one of 9 zones on the opponents' half: neutral = deep centre, up/down on screen = line or cross-court, toward the net = short angle, away = deep. With the mouse as the last device, the reticle's ground point is the target, clamped 6 inside the lines. Quality then scatters by the radius above, which can push it out. |\n| **Spike assist** | difficulty | If the aimed spike can't clear the net from the contact point, raise the arc just enough: always on Easy; on Normal only when the miss would be under 4 units; never on Hard or Pro, where it goes into the net. |\n| **Serve** | Play (float) or Shot (jump serve) to toss; the same button again at the top of the toss | Before the toss she walks along the baseline with the stick. The hit's timing is judged against the toss apex with the same windows. Aim with the stick or mouse; a target marker shows during the toss. Jump serves are faster and scatter × 1.5. No second press within 1.2 s is a serve fault. AI serves after 1.2–2.5 s; a human gets an automatic float serve after 10 s. |\n| **Block** | Shot, within 20 of the net while the opponents attack | She jumps; her hands reach the top `T.blockRise` (.28 s) after the press and stay up .18 s. When the spike crosses the net plane, it is blocked if abs(y_ball − y_blocker) ≤ 9 + .6·JMP and NET_H ≤ z_ball ≤ handTop(t). Timing error = (tPress + blockRise) − tNet. PERFECT or GREAT is a **stuff** (back down on the attacker's side: v = (−.35vx, .3vy ± 20, −60)). OK is a **soft block**: it pops up on her side as a touch. Cut shots arc over the block unless she has JMP 9 and timed it PERFECT. |\n| **Dive** | Dive | Lunge toward the stick (or toward P* when neutral) at 190 u/s for .22 s, slide .3 s, down .45 s. Reach is +`T.diveReach` (16) during the lunge. A judged Play press during it is a **dig**: accuracy radius × 1.6 and a higher apex. A dive with no ball is just the lunge and recovery. |\n| **Call** | Call | Cycles mine → yours → auto. A speech bubble (\"MINE!\" / \"YOURS!\") appears with a gibberish shout. AI teammates call too (\"MINE!\" when they take a ball). |\n\nEvery action sets the rig state `{ act, phase, u }` for animation (§4.26).\n\n### 4.7 AI (`23-ai.js`)\n\n**Skill.** Each AI player, for each touch, has\n`skill = clamp((base × T.aiSkillMul + difficulty) × (0.8 + 0.05 × stat) × chem, 0, 1)`:\n\n- `base` is the day's value (§5.6);\n- `difficulty` is the setting's offset: Easy −.2, Normal 0, Hard +.12, Pro +.22;\n- `stat` is the stat the touch uses: TEC for passes, digs and sets; POW for attacks and serves; JMP for blocks. SPD\n  scales movement speed instead (§4.6).\n- `chem` is 1 for opponents. For the player's AI partner it is `(1 − T.chemistry/2) + T.chemistry × affinity/100`; the\n  default `T.chemistry` .3 gives .85–1.15.\n\n**Reaction.** She starts toward P* `T.aiReaction × (1.2 − skill)` s after a launch, and moves at speed × `T.aiSpeedMul`.\n\n**Errors per touch.** Roll on the `match` rng:\n\n| Outcome | Probability |\n| --- | --- |\n| PERFECT | .10 + .45·skill |\n| GREAT | .30 |\n| MISS | max(.02, .16·(1 − skill)): a shank in a random direction, or no touch |\n| OK | the rest |\n\n**Formation by phase:**\n\n| Phase | Positions |\n| --- | --- |\n| receiving serve | split the court in y, 40% deep |\n| own attack | the setter under the pass target; the hitter backs off for her approach |\n| defending an attack | if the set is near the net and a skill roll passes, one blocks in line with the attacker; the other defends deep cross-court |\n| free ball | both back |\n\n**Decisions.**\n\n- **Attack target:** of the 9 zones, the one with the largest \"distance to the nearest defender's predicted spot minus\n  her reach\", minus 8·(1 − skill) for zones within 10 of a line.\n- **Shot or spike:** a shot when a blocker is up and in line, plus 20% at random for variety.\n- **Serve:** float 70% and jump 30% (50% jump when POW ≥ 8), aimed at the deep corners or the seam between receivers.\n- **Setter dump:** 8% when the opponents' front court is empty.\n\n**AI with a human teammate.** Beach pattern: whoever passes, attacks. When the human passes, the AI sets back to her;\nwhen the AI passes, the human sets and the AI attacks.\n\n**Spectacle mode** (attract only): perfect skill until the rally reaches a random 3–9 touches, then the attacking side's\nspike goes into the biggest gap, a guaranteed kill.\n\n**Determinism.** Every roll comes from `G.rng('match')`, so the same seed and inputs give the same score (tested).\n\n### 4.8 Match flow and presentation (`24-match.js`)\n\n**4.8.1 Phases.** `intro` → `coin` → `serveSetup` → `toss` → `rally` → `dead` → `point` → [`replay`] → … →\n`matchPoint` sting → `end`.\n\n- `intro`: walk-on, Sonny's PA line, the teams line up at the net; 3 s, skippable.\n- `coin`: who serves; 1 s.\n\n**4.8.2 Cameras.**\n\n- **Broadcast:** `cam.frame([ball, ...players, netTop], { margin: 28, zoom: [.78, 1] })` with `cam.smooth` .22. During\n  `serveSetup` it frames the server and the receivers.\n- **Serve Cam:** follows the ball's x with a lead, fixed at the court's centre y, zoom .9.\n- `view` (V / R3) toggles them; Settings has \"Match camera\". The scene's `camera: { zoom: [.85, 1.25] }` lets the\n  player nudge the zoom.\n\n**4.8.3 HUD** (pixel art, anchored to the screen):\n\n| Where | What |\n| --- | --- |\n| top left | TV score bug: per team two small portraits, names, score, a serve ball icon, set count, and a MATCH POINT tag |\n| top right | ClockBadge (vacation) or the hub clock |\n| bottom left | partner card: portrait, name, hearts = chemistry, mood |\n| bottom centre | context prompts (at most 3, e.g. \"✕ BUMP · ○ DIVE · △ CALL\") |\n| at players | judgement popups (PERFECT! gold, GREAT cyan, OK white, MISS grey) and call bubbles |\n| bottom right | commentary box: `E.Dialog` with `modal: false, auto: 2.2`, Sonny's portrait, his voice |\n\n**4.8.4 Crowd and set dressing.**\n\n- 24 spectators on the far-side bleachers and towels, drawn as small pixel sprites like the sports kit's crowd, plus 4\n  HD rigs at size .9 drawn `every: 2`. They sway, jump and cheer on points (more for the home side) and groan at errors.\n- Sonny reacts at his DJ booth.\n- Pepper sits at the scorer's table beside a flip scoreboard shape whose cards change with the score.\n- Night matches add floodlights (lights) and tiki torches.\n\n**4.8.5 Celebrations.**\n\n| Moment | Animation |\n| --- | --- |\n| point won | the partners high-five (§4.26), plus a fist pump |\n| ace, kill or block | the scorer's signature celebration |\n| point lost | a shrug, an encouraging pat or a facepalm (short) |\n| match won | both cheer, then the MVP's signature move |\n| match lost | kneel and sigh |\n\nAll of these fit inside the `point` phase.\n\n**4.8.6 Specials in the final against Sonny & Pepper (\"The House\").** Each is telegraphed in Pepper's Day 4 letter and\nby the commentary.\n\n- **Golden Glare:** half of Sonny's serves. His sunglasses flash (a .6 s telegraph: glint particle, `sfx('glare')`), and\n  the receiving human's timing ring is hidden for that serve (\"DAZZLED!\"). A receiver wearing **any sunglasses**\n  accessory is immune (\"SHADES ON!\").\n- **House Edge:** once per set Pepper hits a precise line shot. The AI partner covers it only at chemistry Good Friend\n  or better (\"I've got line!\").\n- **Lucky Seven:** the first time The House reaches game point, Sonny's next attack clips the tape and is guaranteed to\n  dribble over.\n\n**4.8.7 Highlight replay.**\n\n- Keep a ring buffer of the last 6 s at 60 Hz: rig states, launches and camera.\n- After an ace, a stuff block, a spike over 400 u/s, or a rally of 8+ touches (at most once every 3 points), replay the\n  last 3 s at .4× from the other camera with a \"REPLAY\" letterbox. Any button skips.\n- Off in hub sessions.\n\n**4.8.8 Results.**\n\n- The winners pose.\n- Three big stat cards: points, kills, longest rally. The MVP (most points) gets a portrait and her signature move.\n- Vacation: prize money counts up, the partner's affinity change animates as hearts, then **Continue**.\n- Beach Match: Rematch / Change setup / Title.\n\n**4.8.9 Sound.**\n\n- The match song `spike` has a named drum layer `rally` that comes in on long rallies (`audio.layer`). At match point\n  the tempo goes up by 6 (`audio.tempo`) with a sting.\n- Ball sounds per kind, the whistle, crowd swells, and Sonny's PA voice.\n\n### 4.9 Beach Match: exhibition and local multiplayer (`52-exhibition.js`)\n\n**The setup screen.** Four columns, one per slot (Left 1, Left 2, Right 1, Right 2). Each shows a fighter on a pedestal\nand who controls it: CPU or P1–P4.\n\n- **Joining:** `game.allowJoin({ max: 4, onJoin })`. Start or ✕ on a free pad, or 2 on the keyboard (the split halves).\n- **Each joined player:** left/right moves her badge between slots; up/down picks the fighter; □ picks the outfit\n  (signature suits, plus suits ever owned in a vacation, or every suit once a vacation is finished); ✕ is ready.\n- **Options row:** points (7/11/15/21), sets (1/3), difficulty, court time (Morning/Sunset/Night), camera.\n- The match starts when every joined player is ready.\n\n**Any mix works:** 1P with a CPU partner vs CPU; 2P co-op vs CPU; 1v1 with CPU partners; 2v2; 3 players (2 vs 1 + CPU).\n\nEach player's prompts use her own device (`p.input.label`, per-player glyph style). Results offer Rematch / Change setup\n/ Title.\n\n### 4.10 Calendar, slots, weather, schedules, moods (`30-vacation.js`)\n\n**Days and slots.** `DAYS = 5` (data). Slots are Morning (06–12), Afternoon (12–18) and Night (18–24). The ClockBadge\nshows \"Day 2 · Afternoon\" with weather.\n\n**What uses up a slot:** finishing a match; finishing Pool Hop; leaving a location you entered (the confirm says\n\"Leaving ends the Morning.\"); leaving the casino at night; Rest in the villa. Talking, gifting, shopping and changing\nclothes inside a location don't.\n\n**At night** only the Villa, the Casino and story events are open. The map shows the rest as closed.\n\n**Day start** (seeded from `world`):\n\n- roll moods, form NPC teams, place NPCs by schedule, pick each shop's 2 daily deals, and add any items whose day has\n  come (§4.12);\n- set the weather from the table: D1 sunny; D2 sunny or cloudy; D3 cloudy morning, rain in the afternoon, clear night;\n  D4 sunny; D5 sunny with a golden afternoon (sunset light);\n- autosave.\n\n**Day end (sleep)** shows a summary card: money earned and spent, matches, affinity changes (arrows by each portrait),\ntomorrow's weather. Then:\n\n- your partner leaves if you lost a match that day and her affinity is below 35;\n- affinity drifts `T.affinityDecay` (2) toward its base value for every NPC you didn't talk to;\n- NPC pairs \"play\" each other off-screen for that day's record: one simulated result per pair from skills on the\n  `world` rng. The Match Board shows records like \"Lola & Tess 3–1\".\n\n**Schedules** (weights in §5.4).\n\n- Each NPC has weights over locations for each slot, changed by weather and mood; the `world` rng picks.\n- NPC team-mates go together, to the place chosen for the first one.\n- Story events override the schedule.\n- Guarantee at least one NPC pair at the Beach in every daytime slot.\n- Your partner isn't scheduled: she \"jogs over\" whenever you open the Match Board.\n\n**Moods.**\n\n| Mood | Icon and word |\n| --- | --- |\n| Happy | ☀ |\n| Normal | ◐ |\n| Gloomy | ☁ |\n\nDaily roll 35/45/20. One step up if the weather is one she likes; one step down if you beat her yesterday or the\nweather is one she dislikes. Mood shifts gift thresholds and invite chances.\n\n### 4.11 Affinity, gifts and team-ups (`30-vacation.js`, `32-location.js`)\n\n**Affinity** is 0–100 between you and each NPC: one symmetric number per pair, shown as 5 hearts in half steps. Start\nvalues come from the table in §5.3.\n\n| Stage | Affinity |\n| --- | --- |\n| Stranger | 0–19 |\n| Acquaintance | 20–39 |\n| Friend | 40–59 |\n| Good Friend | 60–79 |\n| Best Friend | 80–100 |\n\n**Changes.** Positive changes are multiplied by `T.affinityGainMul`.\n\n| Cause | Change |\n| --- | --- |\n| chat, first of the day | +2 |\n| chat, later (once per slot) | +1 |\n| gift loved / liked / neutral | +12 / +6 / +2 |\n| gift disliked | −6 (and the gift comes back to your bag) |\n| your team wins / loses | +6 / −2 (−5 if she is Gloomy) |\n| you beat her team | −3 (+1 for good sports: Tess and Rin) |\n| event choices | ±4 |\n| winning the final, for your partner | +10 |\n\n**Gift acceptance.** score = taste + stage bonus + mood.\n\n- taste: love 3, like 2, neutral 0, dislike −3;\n- stage bonus: Friend 1, Good Friend 1, Best Friend 2;\n- mood: Happy +1, Normal 0, Gloomy −1.\n\nShe accepts if score ≥ `T.giftThreshold` (0). So neutral gifts are accepted unless she is a Gloomy stranger, and\ndislikes are refused unless she is a Happy Best Friend. One gift per NPC per slot.\n\n**Reactions:**\n\n| Reaction | Animation and sound |\n| --- | --- |\n| love | jumps, a burst of hearts, \"I love it!\"-style line, jingle `gift_love` |\n| like | smile and nod |\n| neutral | polite nod |\n| refuse | folded arms and a head shake (`Reject` or `Idle_FoldArms`), jingle `gift_refuse` |\n\n**Known likes.** The first time you see her reaction to an item, record it in `known[npc][item]`. The Villa journal's\nFriends page shows what you've learned as icons.\n\n**Team-up.**\n\n- She accepts if affinity ≥ `T.inviteThreshold` (40), with the threshold −10 if she's Happy and +10 if Gloomy.\n- If she's already on an NPC team she needs 20 more. Her old team-mate then goes solo and is sour with you (−4).\n- You have one partner at a time. Switching asks first (\"Tess will be disappointed…\").\n- Partner chemistry is her affinity, shown as hearts on the match HUD.\n\n**Swimsuit gifts.** A suit you give must match one of her tastes or she refuses it (\"Not really my style\"). An accepted\nsuit becomes her outfit (in matches and around the island), and she keeps it.\n\n### 4.12 Money, shops, wardrobe, inventory (`33-shop.js`)\n\n**Currency:** Sonny Dollars, written S$12,500. You start with S$30,000 (`T.startMoney`).\n\n**Income** (match prizes × `T.prizeMul`):\n\n| Source | Amount |\n| --- | --- |\n| match win | S$ (12,000 + 3,000·day + 1,000·winning margin) |\n| match loss | S$3,000 |\n| tutorial | S$10,000 |\n| semifinal win | S$30,000 |\n| final win | S$100,000 and the \"Fortuna Gold\" suit |\n| Pool Hop | S$ (2,000 + 400·perfects + 150·seconds left) |\n| casino | chips cashed out at S$100 each |\n\n**Shops**, all on the Promenade. Each shows its whole stock from §5.2. Items marked \"Day N+\" arrive on that day and\ncarry a NEW badge for it. Every day each shop also has **2 daily deals at −25%**, picked by the `world` rng. Prices ×\n`T.priceMul`.\n\n| Shop | Keeper | Sells |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Riptide Sports** | Coach Bo | sporty suits, sports accessories, sports gifts |\n| **Coral Couture** | Odette | fashion suits and accessories, fashion gifts |\n| **Sundries & Smiles** | Kai | food, goods and books gifts, the luchador mask |\n\n**The shop screen.**\n\n- Category tabs; a 3×2 card grid; a detail panel.\n- For suits and accessories, a **live rig of your fighter wearing the focused item** turns on a pedestal (right stick,\n  L1/R1 or a mouse drag). □ \"Try on\" switches between the item and your current outfit.\n- ✕ buys. A confirm appears when the price is over 30% of your money.\n- Badges show OWNED and WEARING. Items you can't afford are dimmed with the shortfall shown.\n- The keeper's portrait says a short quip, with voice.\n\n**Wardrobe** (the Villa closet, and the changing hut at the Beach and Pool): the suits and accessories you own; ✕\nequip, □ remove an accessory, the same rotating preview. A second page shows your partner and the suits she has\naccepted.\n\n**Gift Bag:** counts per gift, sorted by category, at most 9 of each. Opened from talk menus, or with □ on the map or in\na location to browse.\n\n### 4.13 Island map (`31-map.js`)\n\n**The map:** an iso view of Isla Fortuna, a TileMap of about 48×36 tiles.\n\n- Sea all round (`outside` set to the sea color, animated water floor at the edges); beaches, grass, palm groves.\n- A dormant volcano: stepped rock walls, 3 levels, with steam wisps.\n- The lagoon pool, the courts, the Promenade, a row of villas, the casino (neon at night), the Dock with Sonny's\n  seaplane, a lighthouse.\n\n**Pins:** Sunset Courts, Lagoon Pool, Fortuna Promenade, Your Villa, Casino Fortuna (night only), and the Dock (shown\ngreyed: \"Departures only\").\n\n**Controls.**\n\n- The stick or d-pad jumps the cursor to the nearest pin in that direction; L1/R1 cycle pins; mouse hover highlights\n  (`r.pick`).\n- ✕ or a click opens the **location card**: name, a small picture, who's there (portraits with mood icons, NPC pairs\n  marked), activities, open or closed. ✕ again travels, with an `iris` transition at the pin.\n- □ opens Friends (affinity overview), △ the Journal (save, stats), Options pauses.\n\n**The header** shows the ClockBadge, the MoneyBadge and the partner card.\n\n**Sky and weather:** a morning pastel sky, a bright afternoon, a night of stars, lit windows and neon; weather\nparticles.\n\n### 4.14 Walkable locations (`32-location.js`)\n\n**One scene, driven by data per location** (§5.4): a TileMap in `threequarter`, the outside color or a backdrop,\nshapes (`map.solid` for collision), NPC spots, interactables, music and ambience, exits.\n\n- **You:** an `E.Body` (r 5) moving at 70 units/s walking and 110 running, with the camera on you\n  (`game.follow(hero, { z: 16 })`, `cam.bounds`). Lights and GPU lighting come on at night.\n- **NPCs present** (from the schedule) sit at spots doing idle activities and turn their heads toward you within 40\n  units.\n- **Talk.** Interact within 22 units opens the talk panel: her portrait, mood, hearts, and a vertical list.\n\n| Choice | Notes |\n| --- | --- |\n| **Chat** | |\n| **Give a Gift** | |\n| **Team Up** | if she isn't your partner; for your partner: \"Our next match?\", which opens the Match Board |\n| **Challenge** | beach only, when she's in a pair |\n| **Bye** | |\n\n- **Interactables:**\n\n| Place | Interactables |\n| --- | --- |\n| Beach | Match Board (challengeable pairs with difficulty stars and records, your partner, Play), changing hut (Wardrobe) |\n| Pool | Pool Hop start deck, changing hut (Wardrobe) |\n| Promenade | the three shop doors |\n| Villa | bed (Rest / Sleep), closet (Wardrobe), desk (Journal), album frame, mailbox (letters) |\n| Casino floor (its own scene, §4.16) | cashier, slot machines, blackjack table, roulette table, prize counter, VIP lounge (events) |\n\n- **Leaving:** walk to the exit, or press `leave` (△ / M / Tab), then confirm \"Leave? This ends the Afternoon.\" Back on\n  the map, it is the next slot.\n\n### 4.15 Pool Hop (`40-poolhop.js`)","numLines":500,"startLine":500,"totalLines":2193}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01X2gR3pXrZibMazX2LAxjCB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghPkYmDXtf5VoUXUjUxL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YNraQd2oEEdYPSeG9BwVBs","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/PLAN.md","offset":1000,"limit":650},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13121,"cache_read_input_tokens":39917,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13121},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf","uuid":"67966226-c5bd-448f-92fd-215d28535f2d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:12:02.400Z","request_id":"req_011CghPkYWabgQpjSYjcqU7Q","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01YNraQd2oEEdYPSeG9BwVBs":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/PLAN.md","offset":1000,"limit":650}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YNraQd2oEEdYPSeG9BwVBs","type":"tool_result","content":"1000\t\n1001\t**Goal:** cross the lagoon on 32 floating pads in `T.poolTime` (40 s). Each pad shows the glyph of one of the four face\n1002\tbuttons for the current device (✕○□△, A B X Y, or J L K I keycaps). Press it as the hopper lands, on the beat.\n1003\t\n1004\t**Rhythm.**\n1005\t\n1006\t- The song `lagoon` runs at `T.poolBpm` (112) with `sync: true`. One hop per beat, judged against the music clock\n1007\t  (`audio.pos`).\n1008\t- PERFECT is within 60 ms and GOOD within 130 ms (× `T.poolWindowMul`).\n1009\t- Too early, too late or the wrong button: she slips, splashes, swims back (1.8 s), and continues from the same pad on\n1010\t  the next bar.\n1011\t- Each run of 8 PERFECT hops in a row adds +1 s.\n1012\t\n1013\t**Twists:**\n1014\t\n1015\t- from pad 12, **wobble pads**: the glyph flips between two buttons and settles one beat before you need it;\n1016\t- from pad 22, **double pads**: two glyphs; press both together.\n1017\t\n1018\t**Score and reward.** Time, perfects and falls give the prize (§4.12). Your best time is saved. Characters at the pool\n1019\tcheer, and a present partner gains +2 affinity when you clear it.\n1020\t\n1021\t**Camera and effects:** the Broadcast angle follows the hopper; pads bob to the beat; splashes; water shimmer.\n1022\t\n1023\tThe attract mode runs Pool Hop with a perfect bot.\n1024\t\n1025\t### 4.16 Casino Fortuna (`41-casino.js`, nights only)\n1026\t\n1027\t**The floor** is a `threequarter` map with neon, chandeliers and lights, and a crowd. Stations:\n1028\t\n1029\t- **Cashier:** chips at S$100 each; buy in steps of 10, 50 or 100; cash out any time. The chip count shows on every\n1030\t  casino screen.\n1031\t- **6 slot machines.**\n1032\t- **Blackjack table**, dealer Pepper.\n1033\t- **Roulette table**, croupier Kai.\n1034\t- **Sonny's VIP lounge**, for story events.\n1035\t\n1036\tOn the first night Sonny hands you 20 free chips and explains the games. A prize counter swaps 300 chips for the\n1037\t\"Jackpot\" suit.\n1038\t\n1039\t**Fortuna Sevens (pachislot).**\n1040\t\n1041\t- 3 reels with 3 visible rows. Bet 1, 2 or 3 chips: 1 = the centre line, 2 = plus the top and bottom lines, 3 = plus\n1042\t  both diagonals.\n1043\t- ✕ / Space spins. Then ✕ ○ □ (J K L) stop reels 1, 2 and 3. A stop \"slips\" 0–4 symbols on the `casino` rng, so\n1044\t  timing matters a little.\n1045\t- Strips of 21 stops per reel. Payouts per line bet:\n1046\t\n1047\t| Line | Pays |\n1048\t| --- | --- |\n1049\t| 7-7-7 | ×100, with a jackpot fanfare and coin shower |\n1050\t| BAR-BAR-BAR | ×30 |\n1051\t| Sonny-Sonny-Sonny | ×20 (Sonny is wild) |\n1052\t| Volleyball ×3 | ×12 |\n1053\t| Palm ×3 | ×8 |\n1054\t| Coconut ×3 | ×5 |\n1055\t| Cherry, by count on the line | 1 ×2, 2 ×5, 3 ×10 |\n1056\t\n1057\t- Tune the strips so the RTP is **92% ± 3** at `T.slotsPayMul` 1 (a simulation test checks it).\n1058\t- Spinning reels show blur rows, then a stop clunk and a line highlight.\n1059\t\n1060\t**Blackjack.**\n1061\t\n1062\t- 6-deck shoe, reshuffled at 75%. The dealer stands on soft 17 (`T.dealerHitsSoft17` toggles it). Blackjack pays 3:2.\n1063\t  Double on any first two cards. Split once; split aces get one card each. No insurance, no surrender.\n1064\t- Bets of 1, 5, 10 or 25 chips (a stepper).\n1065\t- Controls: ✕/H hit, □/S stand, △/D double, R1/P split (only when legal), ○ leave between hands. Every button is also\n1066\t  clickable on screen. The betting phase (left/right sets the bet) and the playing phase each read only their own\n1067\t  actions, so S and D never clash with WASD.\n1068\t- Cards are pixel sprites (rank glyphs and suit sprites ♠ ♥ ♦ ♣ made with `E.sprite`), dealt with tweens and flipped.\n1069\t  Pepper has deadpan lines for a blackjack and a bust.\n1070\t\n1071\t**Roulette.**\n1072\t\n1073\t- A single-zero wheel in real order: 0, 32, 15, 19, 4, 21, 2, 25, 17, 34, 6, 27, 13, 36, 11, 30, 8, 23, 10, 5, 24, 16,\n1074\t  33, 1, 20, 14, 31, 9, 22, 18, 29, 7, 28, 12, 35, 3, 26.\n1075\t- **Betting layout:** a cursor moved with the stick, WASD or the mouse.\n1076\t\n1077\t| Bet | Pays |\n1078\t| --- | --- |\n1079\t| straight number | 35:1 |\n1080\t| red/black, odd/even, 1–18/19–36 | 1:1 |\n1081\t| dozens, columns | 2:1 |\n1082\t\n1083\t- Controls: ✕ place a chip (L1/R1 sizes 1/5/10/25), □ remove, △ spin, ○ leave.\n1084\t- An inset wheel shows the pocket ring turning while the ball spirals in, slows, bounces two pockets and settles. Then\n1085\t  the result is highlighted, payouts made, and a strip shows the last 10 results.\n1086\t- The dev-only toggle `T.rouletteDoubleZero` gives an American wheel.\n1087\t\n1088\tLeaving the casino ends the night and goes to the day-end card.\n1089\t\n1090\t### 4.17 Postcards (photo mode) and album (`42-photo.js`)\n1091\t\n1092\t**Where:** the pause menu's \"Take a Postcard\", or Create / C in walkable locations and on match results. Never in hub\n1093\tsessions or the attract. Gameplay time freezes (`timeScale` 0), while cosmetic motion (water, breathing idles) keeps\n1094\tgoing.\n1095\t\n1096\t**Controls:**\n1097\t\n1098\t| Input | Does |\n1099\t| --- | --- |\n1100\t| left stick / WASD | pan the focus |\n1101\t| right stick / right-drag | orbit at any angle (`game.rotateView`) |\n1102\t| L2/R2 / wheel | zoom .75–2.5 |\n1103\t| ✕ | take the photo |\n1104\t| ○ | exit |\n1105\t| □ | choose the subject: you, or any NPC present |\n1106\t| △ | the panel |\n1107\t| R3 / H | hide the UI |\n1108\t\n1109\tThe △ panel has:\n1110\t\n1111\t- **pose:** Wave, Peace, Hips, Cheer, Stretch, Look Back, Sit, Victory, Salute, Bow;\n1112\t- **expression:** smile, shout, wince, neutral;\n1113\t- **filter:** Clean, Sunny, Sepia, Retro, Night Glow;\n1114\t- **frame:** none, or a postcard border with a \"Greetings from Isla Fortuna\" stamp and the date.\n1115\t\n1116\t**Taking a photo.** The shutter sound and a white flash, then a \"developing\" postcard slides to a corner. It is saved\n1117\tin `state.album` (at most 24; asks before replacing the oldest) as a **spec**, never pixels:\n1118\t`{ loc, day, slot, tod, weather, cam: { x, y, z, yaw, zoom, view }, people: [{ id, suit, acc, pose, expr, x, y, facing\n1119\t}], filter, frame }`.\n1120\t\n1121\t**The album** (Villa, or the menu for the latest save):\n1122\t\n1123\t- A 4×2 grid of live thumbnails: each spec is re-rendered at half size.\n1124\t- Opening one re-renders it full screen, live, so the palms still sway.\n1125\t- □ deletes (with a confirm); △ \"Set as title backdrop\"; R1 exports a PNG download (not in sessions).\n1126\t\n1127\tThe credits slideshow re-renders the album, plus a group photo taken automatically at the party.\n1128\t\n1129\t### 4.18 Story, dialogue, voices, cutscenes (`34-story.js`)\n1130\t\n1131\t- `E.Story` holds `people` for every speaker (portrait = their rig) and the nodes from `05-data-text.js`. Its `on`\n1132\t  events run game actions: `startMatch`, `giveMoney`, `giveItem`, `setPartner`, `openShop`, `photo`, `fade`.\n1133\t  `story.state()` goes in the save.\n1134\t- **The dialog box:** bottom, 2 lines, the name tag in the speaker's color, a portrait with expression\n1135\t  (`portraitOpts`), markup for emphasis (`{c=#ffd36a}…{/c}`, `{wave}`, `{shake}`). The Animalese voice runs from the\n1136\t  per-letter hook (patch 3). Text speed is a setting. Hold ○ or right click to fast-forward; Options on a cutscene asks\n1137\t  \"Skip scene?\".\n1138\t- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens, walk-ons (`game.tween` on bodies), emotes\n1139\t  (`story.emote(target, 'heart' | '!' | '?' | 'note' | 'dots')`), fades. The list is in §5.5.\n1140\t\n1141\t### 4.19 Save and load (`30-vacation.js`)\n1142\t\n1143\t**Slots:** `game.saves` (3 slots plus autosave). The title's Load and the Villa journal's Save open `saves.show('load'\n1144\t| 'save')`. The game autosaves at every slot start; Continue loads `saves.latest()`.\n1145\t\n1146\t- `saves.write = () => ({ data: G.state, place: locationName, level: 'Day ' + day })`;\n1147\t- `read = save => G.loadState(save.data)`, with `version: 1` and a `migrate`.\n1148\t\n1149\t**State shape:**\n1150\t\n1151\t```js\n1152\t{ v: 1, seed, day: 1, slot: 0, weather: ['sunny', …], me: 'rin', money: 30000, chips: 0,\n1153\t  wardrobe: { suits: ['seigaiha'], acc: ['ribbon'] }, wearing: { suit: 'seigaiha', acc: ['ribbon'] },\n1154\t  npcWear: { lola: { suit: 'estrella', acc: ['sweatband'] }, … }, bag: { mango_smoothie: 1 },\n1155\t  affinity: { lola: 20, … }, mood: { lola: 'happy', … }, known: { lola: { hot_sauce: 'love' } },\n1156\t  partner: null, teams: [['lola', 'tess'], ['amara', 'mei']], record: { 'lola+tess': [0, 0] },\n1157\t  flags: {}, story: {}, chatted: {}, gifted: {}, album: [], titlePostcard: null,\n1158\t  stats: { matches: 0, wins: 0, points: 0, kills: 0, aces: 0, blocks: 0, poolBest: null, casinoNet: 0, gifts: 0,\n1159\t           photos: 0, earned: 0, spent: 0 } }\n1160\t```\n1161\t\n1162\t**New Vacation+** (after an ending) keeps the wardrobe, album and lifetime stats. It resets the days and affinity (to\n1163\tbase +10) and starts money at S$30,000 plus 10% of your final money.\n1164\t\n1165\t**Unlocks** for Beach Match (suits ever owned; everything after the first ending) live in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\n1166\t\n1167\t### 4.20 Front end: boot, title, menu, How to Play, About (`50-title.js`)\n1168\t\n1169\t**Boot.** Boot steps build the rigs, maps, music and caches behind the engine's boot screen, with messages: \"Raking the\n1170\tsand\", \"Inflating volleyballs\", \"Chilling the smoothies\", \"Counting Sonny's chips\", \"Polishing the golden sunglasses\".\n1171\t\n1172\t**Title.**\n1173\t\n1174\t- A sunset beach backdrop: sea layers, the sun, distant islands, palms, gentle waves.\n1175\t- The six fighters stand on the sand in their signature suits, each with her own idle: Rin stretching, Lola flexing,\n1176\t  Ingrid fanning herself, Amara dancing, Tess juggling a ball, Mei waving. Now and then Sonny jogs across the background\n1177\t  with a giant trophy.\n1178\t- The logo **AHEAD OR ALIVE**: `E.font.title` scale 4, colors `['#fff7d6', '#ffd36a', '#ff9e5e', '#ff5f7a']`, depth 3,\n1179\t  with a small spinning volleyball beside it. Under it **XTREME BEACH VOLLEYBALL** at scale 2, white with a teal shadow.\n1180\t- A blinking \"PRESS ✕\" in the current device's glyph.\n1181\t- A footer with the version label (`E.versionLabel()`) and \"An original parody-tribute game\".\n1182\t- If a postcard is set as the title backdrop, it renders behind the logo instead.\n1183\t\n1184\t**Main menu.** A big list on the left; a turning fighter preview on the right.\n1185\t\n1186\t- **New Vacation**\n1187\t- **Continue** (if a save exists)\n1188\t- **Load**\n1189\t- **Beach Match**\n1190\t- **Album** (if there are postcards)\n1191\t- **How to Play**\n1192\t- **Settings** (`game.menu('settings')`)\n1193\t- **About & Credits**\n1194\t\n1195\t10 s idle starts the attract mode.\n1196\t\n1197\t**How to Play.** 10 pages, one idea each, with a live mini-scene in the panel and the current device's glyphs:\n1198\t\n1199\t1. Moving and the ring\n1200\t2. The touch chain: bump, set, spike\n1201\t3. Aiming and shots\n1202\t4. Serving\n1203\t5. Blocking and diving\n1204\t6. Calls and chemistry\n1205\t7. The vacation: slots, map, money\n1206\t8. Friends and gifts\n1207\t9. Casino and Pool Hop\n1208\t10. Postcards\n1209\t\n1210\t**About & Credits.** Pages turned with L1/R1, left/right or the on-screen arrows; the stick scrolls; large text, one\n1211\tfield per line. Contents in §10:\n1212\t\n1213\t1. Credits\n1214\t2. Source Information\n1215\t3. Testing Feedback\n1216\t4. Engine Feedback\n1217\t5. Prompt Feedback\n1218\t\n1219\t### 4.21 Attract mode (`51-attract.js`)\n1220\t\n1221\t**Trigger.** 10.0 s without input on `title` or `menu`. Input means any key, a pad button, a stick past its dead zone,\n1222\tthe mouse moving more than 4 px, a click, the wheel, or a touch; each resets the timer.\n1223\t\n1224\t**Playlist.** A director kept alive across scenes (`game.script(…, { keep: true })` plus the overlay watcher) plays it,\n1225\tre-seeded each cycle for variety. Demo scenes run on a throwaway demo state, never the player's save.\n1226\t\n1227\t1. **Match, about 50 s.** AI vs AI on Sunset Courts with random fighters, outfits and time of day: `spectacle` AI, the\n1228\t   camera cutting between Broadcast and Serve Cam every 2 points, commentary and highlight replays on.\n1229\t2. **Vacation montage, about 50 s.** 7 beats of 6–8 s, each with a big caption banner:\n1230\t\n1231\t| Caption | Shows |\n1232\t| --- | --- |\n1233\t| FIVE DAYS IN PARADISE | the island map flying from morning to night |\n1234\t| MAKE FRIENDS · GIVE GIFTS | a gift scene with hearts |\n1235\t| COLLECT 21 SWIMSUITS | the shop preview cycling suits |\n1236\t| POOL HOP | a perfect-bot run |\n1237\t| CASINO NIGHTS | slots hitting 7-7-7, then a blackjack |\n1238\t| SNAP POSTCARDS | a photo-mode orbit |\n1239\t| BEAT THE HOUSE | a slice of the final against Sonny & Pepper, with the Golden Glare |\n1240\t\n1241\t3. **Title card, 5 s**, with \"PRESS ✕\". Then repeat.\n1242\t\n1243\t**Rules.**\n1244\t\n1245\t- The AI may cheat freely: perfect timing, scripted outcomes, instant travel.\n1246\t- **Any input** returns to `title` with the input consumed, so it doesn't also press a menu item, and the title music\n1247\t  resumes.\n1248\t- A \"DEMO\" tag shows top left. On touch-only devices the bottom banner reads \"Controller or keyboard required\".\n1249\t- Sound starts only after the browser's first gesture (engine rule), so before that the attract runs silent.\n1250\t\n1251\t### 4.22 Dev mode (`53-dev.js`)\n1252\t\n1253\t**Reach.** The pause menu's **Dev Mode**, in every pausable scene. Once opened, F1 (or L3+R3 on a pad) reopens it for\n1254\tthe rest of the session. Never in hub sessions.\n1255\t\n1256\t**While it is open:**\n1257\t\n1258\t- gameplay time is frozen (`game.timeScale = 0`; the overlay updates on real time);\n1259\t- the panel is a 10-foot canvas overlay built with the UI kit;\n1260\t- tabs (L1/R1, Q/E or a click): **Tools · Match · Vacation · Minigames · Presentation · Tuning**;\n1261\t- **Back to game** restores `timeScale`.\n1262\t\n1263\t**4.22.1 Tools** (every button calls `game.debug.tools.*`).\n1264\t\n1265\t| Tab | Tools |\n1266\t| --- | --- |\n1267\t| Tools | jump to any scene, location or minigame; set the day (1–5) and slot; jump to the Semifinal, the Final, the party or ending, the credits; restart the scene; reset the save (with a confirm) |\n1268\t| Match | start a match against any pair; force a point left or right; set the score; end the match (win/lose); CPU controls your player (watch); Perfect Player (all your presses PERFECT); the debug overlay (trajectory line, landing point, every player's P* ring, AI assignment and state labels, a judge-window bar); slow motion ×.25 / ×.5 / ×1; frame step (one step per press while frozen); switch camera |\n1269\t| Vacation | money +10k / +100k / set to 0; chips +100; unlock all items; fill the gift bag ×3; set affinity per fighter (a slider 0–100); set mood; make or clear partner; reveal all likes |\n1270\t| Minigames | Pool Hop autopilot; slots: force 7-7-7 next; blackjack: deal a blackjack; roulette: force a number |\n1271\t| Presentation | time-of-day override (0–24 h); weather (sunny/cloudy/rain); show FPS (engine setting); **Voice Lab** (pick a speaker and a preset phrase, play it); music jukebox; SFX board; rig sheet viewer (fighter × suit × pose × view) |\n1272\t\n1273\t**4.22.2 Live sliders** (the Tuning tab).\n1274\t\n1275\t- Changes apply at once: every system reads `G.T` every step.\n1276\t- Each slider shows its default as a tick. △ or R on a slider resets it.\n1277\t- **Reset all to defaults** asks to confirm.\n1278\t- Values persist in `E.store('aoa-dev-tuning')`, and **Copy JSON** copies them to the clipboard.\n1279\t\n1280\t| Group | Key | Default | Range | Step |\n1281\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1282\t| Ball | `ballGravity` | 330 | 180–500 | 5 |\n1283\t| Ball | `ballDrag` | .12 | 0–.6 | .01 |\n1284\t| Ball | `passT` | 1.05 | .7–1.6 | .05 |\n1285\t| Ball | `setT` | 1.1 | .7–1.6 | .05 |\n1286\t| Ball | `serveT` | 1.3 | .9–1.8 | .05 |\n1287\t| Ball | `jumpServeT` | .85 | .6–1.3 | .05 |\n1288\t| Ball | `spikeSpeed` | 330 | 220–480 | 5 |\n1289\t| Ball | `shotT` | .95 | .6–1.4 | .05 |\n1290\t| Ball | `netCordOver` | .45 | 0–1 | .05 |\n1291\t| Timing | `perfectWin` (s) | .05 | .02–.12 | .005 |\n1292\t| Timing | `greatWin` (s) | .10 | .05–.2 | .005 |\n1293\t| Timing | `okWin` (s) | .16 | .08–.3 | .01 |\n1294\t| Timing | `reach` | 14 | 8–24 | 1 |\n1295\t| Timing | `diveReach` | 16 | 6–30 | 1 |\n1296\t| Timing | `blockRise` (s) | .28 | .15–.45 | .01 |\n1297\t| Players | `runSpeed` | 96 | 60–140 | 2 |\n1298\t| Players | `autoMove` | .85 | 0–1 | .05 |\n1299\t| AI | `aiSkillMul` (× the day's base) | 1 | .3–1.6 | .02 |\n1300\t| AI | `aiReaction` (s) | .25 | 0–.6 | .01 |\n1301\t| AI | `aiSpeedMul` | 1 | .6–1.4 | .02 |\n1302\t| AI | `chemistry` | .3 | 0–.6 | .02 |\n1303\t| Match | `pointsToWin` (vacation) | 7 | 3–21 | 1 |\n1304\t| Economy | `prizeMul` | 1 | 0–3 | .05 |\n1305\t| Economy | `priceMul` | 1 | .25–3 | .05 |\n1306\t| Economy | `startMoney` | 30000 | 0–200000 | 5000 |\n1307\t| Social | `affinityGainMul` | 1 | 0–3 | .05 |\n1308\t| Social | `affinityDecay` | 2 | 0–10 | 1 |\n1309\t| Social | `inviteThreshold` | 40 | 0–100 | 1 |\n1310\t| Social | `giftThreshold` | 0 | −3–3 | 1 |\n1311\t| Pool Hop | `poolBpm` | 112 | 80–150 | 2 |\n1312\t| Pool Hop | `poolWindowMul` | 1 | .5–2 | .05 |\n1313\t| Pool Hop | `poolTime` (s) | 40 | 20–80 | 1 |\n1314\t| Casino | `slotsPayMul` | 1 | .5–1.5 | .01 |\n1315\t| Casino | `dealerHitsSoft17` | off | toggle | — |\n1316\t| Casino | `rouletteDoubleZero` | off | toggle | — |\n1317\t| Presentation | `textSpeed` (letters/s) | 45 | 10–200 | 5 |\n1318\t| Presentation | `cameraZoomMul` | 1 | .7–1.3 | .02 |\n1319\t\n1320\t### 4.23 AI Hub sessions (`25-netplay.js`)\n1321\t\n1322\t**Head tags** in the deliverable. Keep the goal ≤ 60 characters and the howto ≤ 80.\n1323\t\n1324\t```html\n1325\t<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n1326\t<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1327\t<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n1328\t<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n1329\t<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Win the beach volleyball match: first to 7, by 2\">\n1330\t<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · Cross/Space hit on time · Circle/Shift dive · Square/E shot\">\n1331\t<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n1332\t<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n1333\t```\n1334\t\n1335\t**Flow when `AIHub.active` is true.**\n1336\t\n1337\t1. **Build the game for a session:** `menu: false` (no pause), `autoPause: false`, `corner: false`,\n1338\t   `fullscreen: false`, no saves, touch `'never'`, no title and no attract.\n1339\t2. **Connect.** Boot straight into the `hub` scene, which calls\n1340\t   `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, go to\n1341\t   `title` and run normally.\n1342\t3. **Teams.** Left = seat indexes 0 and 2; Right = 1 and 3. Empty slots are CPUs (Normal).\n1343\t   - Fighters: shuffle the six with `AIHub.rng('cast')`; everyone wears signature suits.\n1344\t   - Court time: `AIHub.rng('court')`.\n1345\t   - Each human's fighter gets a ground ring and a name tag in her seat color (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`,\n1346\t     `#f5b700`). Names are drawn with `E.font` on the canvas, never inserted as HTML.\n1347\t4. **Our own card**, until `start`:\n1348\t   - Shows: the court at sunset with the four fighters lined up (CPUs tagged), the logo, the goal line, this player's\n1349\t     controls in her device's glyphs, every player's name in her color with a READY tick (from `card.ready`), and the\n1350\t     countdown from `card.left` (\"Paused: more time\" while `paused`).\n1351\t   - Two buttons: **READY** (✕ / Enter / click) → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; **MORE TIME** (△ / T / click) →\n1352\t     `AIHub.answer('more')`, which toggles.\n1353\t   - Nothing else to choose. Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the card is built, with no key press.\n1354\t   - The server copy (`AIHub.server`) builds the world, calls `ready()`, and draws a minimal \"Hosting\" screen.\n1355\t5. **Start.** On `start`, the intro walk-on plays. Play begins when `AIHub.time() >= 0`, with a 3-2-1 countdown from the\n1356\t   negative clock.\n1357\t6. **Messages.** All are small JSON with short keys.\n1358\t\n1359\t| Msg | Direction | Rate | Reliable | Content |\n1360\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1361\t| `m` | client → host | 12/s while playing (also as a heartbeat) | no | `{ t: 'm', at, x, y, f, a }`: own fighter's position, facing, action |\n1362\t| `c` | client → host | per judged press | yes | `{ t: 'c', at, k, q, aim: [x, y], sh }`: a touch claim; `at` = hub ms of contact, `k` kind, `q` quality, `sh` shot or play |\n1363\t| `v` | client → host | when serving | yes | `{ t: 'v', at, q, aim, jump }`: a serve claim |\n1364\t| `s` | host → all | 12/s | no | `{ t: 's', at, p: [[id, x, y, f, a, u], …], sc: [l, r], ph, sv, tc }` |\n1365\t| `b` | host → all | each launch | yes | `{ t: 'b', t0, p, v, k, g, ay, wob, by, kind }` |\n1366\t| `e` | host → all | per point, fault or phase | yes | `{ t: 'e', ev, side, why, sc, next }` |\n1367\t| final `s` | host → all | once | yes | the last snapshot with `over: 1` |\n1368\t\n1369\t   The budget: the host sends ≤ 16 messages/s and each client ≤ 14, under the hub's 20/s. Unreliable messages stay\n1370\t   under 1,200 bytes.\n1371\t7. **Authority.**\n1372\t   - The host runs the rules and the AI, and accepts claims.\n1373\t   - Each client moves its own fighter at once and sends it at 12 Hz. The host clamps reports to max speed and the court.\n1374\t   - Each client judges its own touches against the shared ball. Every copy computes the same trajectory from `b` on the\n1375\t     shared clock, so the timing is fair whatever the latency.\n1376\t   - The host validates a claim: contact time within the planned window ±.12 s; the claimant within reach + 12 of the\n1377\t     ball at that time; the touch still open; the first valid claim wins. It then broadcasts the new launch with\n1378\t     `t0 = claim.at`, so every copy continues from the same instant; clients ease the visual jump over .12 s.\n1379\t   - Before awarding a point, the host waits for remote claims until `tLand + .25 s`.\n1380\t8. **Others' fighters.** Clients interpolate other fighters from snapshots with a 100 ms buffer. A client's own fighter\n1381\t   is never overwritten.\n1382\t9. **Reporting** (only the host calls `finish()`):\n1383\t   - Match over: `AIHub.finish({ standings: [[winner ids…], [loser ids…]], scores: { id: teamScore }, stats: { id: {\n1384\t     Points, Kills } }, awards: [{ id, title: 'MVP', detail }] })`.\n1385\t   - With one human against CPUs: `standings: [[me]]` and `won: true | false`.\n1386\t   - On `time-up`: finish at once with the current score, the team ahead first. If tied, everyone goes in one array.\n1387\t10. **Leaving.** On `leave`, that seat becomes a CPU and its fighter plays on. If the host leaves, `end` arrives with\n1388\t    `host-left`: show \"Round cancelled\" and stop.\n1389\t11. **End.** On `end`: stop input and sound (music off, mute the buses), freeze the simulation, and draw the final\n1390\t    standings with names. Send nothing more.\n1391\t12. **Session rules.** No pause, quit or title; no dialogs, alerts or new windows; nothing relies on storage; no network\n1392\t    but `AIHub.send`. Options is ignored while Create is held (patch 6).\n1393\t13. **Outside a session** nothing changes: the client is inert when `!AIHub.active`.\n1394\t\n1395\t### 4.24 Audio (`12-audio.js`, `06-data-music.js`)\n1396\t\n1397\t**4.24.1 Music.** The engine's step sequencer plus the instrument patch (patch 4).\n1398\t\n1399\t**Instruments:**\n1400\t\n1401\t| Instrument | Built from |\n1402\t| --- | --- |\n1403\t| `steel` | partials 1, 2, 3, 4.2 at amps 1, .5, .35, .2; decay .5 s |\n1404\t| `marimba` | partials 1, 4, 9.9 at amps 1, .3, .05; decay .35 s |\n1405\t| `pluck` | saw through lowpass 1800; decay .25 s (ukulele and guitar) |\n1406\t| `bell` | partials 1, 2.76, 5.4, 8.9; decay 1.2 s |\n1407\t| `organ` | partials 1, 2, 3, 4; held |\n1408\t| `pad` | saw + detune 8 cents, lowpass 1200; held |\n1409\t\n1410\tPlus the engine's square, pulse, triangle, saw and sine waves, and drums.\n1411\t\n1412\t**Tracks.** Original compositions. Each loops cleanly over 16–32 bars, with named layers so drums can drop in and out.\n1413\t\n1414\t| id | Where | Tempo, key | Feel and instruments | Chords |\n1415\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1416\t| `sunrise` | title, menu | 116, C | bright tropical pop: steel lead, marimba arpeggios, pluck chords, bass, light drums | C G Am F; bridge Dm G |\n1417\t| `island` | map, Promenade | 100, F | breezy: ukulele pluck, marimba melody, shaker hats | F Bb C F; Dm Gm C |\n1418\t| `spike` | matches | 138, Am | driving synth-pop: square lead, saw bass; drum layer `rally` comes in on long rallies; +6 bpm at match point | Am F C G |\n1419\t| `house` | the final | 150, Dm | campy-dramatic: organ stabs, brassy pulse lead, tom rolls, a cheesy key change up a step in the last 8 bars | Dm Bb C A |\n1420\t| `lagoon` | pool, Pool Hop | 112, G | bossa-nova: pluck comping, soft steel lead, rim clicks on the quarter notes (the hop beat) | G Em Am D |\n1421\t| `boutique` | shops, wardrobe | 108, Bb | cute shopping funk: bell arpeggios, popping bass | Bb Gm Eb F |\n1422\t| `neon` | casino | 96, Em | lounge funk: organ, muted bass, swung hats, bell sparkles on wins | Em A vamp; C B7 turnaround |\n1423\t| `siesta` | villa, night map | 80, D | gentle pad and marimba lullaby, with a cricket ambience | D Bm G A |\n1424\t| `farewell` | party, endings, credits | 124, C → D | anthemic: steel and square in harmony, full drums, firework hits | C G Am F, then the key change to D |\n1425\t\n1426\t**Jingles** (`audio.sting`): `win` (3 s), `lose`, `ace`, `matchpoint`, `gift_love`, `gift_refuse`, `jackpot`,\n1427\t`daystart` (a bright chime), `levelup` (an affinity stage up), `photo`.\n1428\t\n1429\t**Ambience loops** (noise on the sfx bus): waves (lowpass swells on a 6 s period), wind, crowd murmur, lapping pool\n1430\twater, casino murmur with distant slot jingles, night crickets (pulse chirps). Rain is the engine weather's sound.\n1431\t\n1432\t**4.24.2 Sound effects** (`audio.define`). Leave about 6 dB of headroom and balance them by ear.\n1433\t\n1434\t| Group | Effects |\n1435\t| --- | --- |\n1436\t| Ball | `bump` (soft sine thump 160→90 Hz plus noise), `set` (short tap, 400 Hz), `spike` (noise crack plus sine 120→40, louder with speed), `block` (two-hand slap), `serveToss` (whoosh), `serveHit`, `sand` (lowpass noise 600→150), `net` (rattle: 3 noise ticks), `tape` (tick and wobble), `whistle` (square 2200 Hz with vibrato) |\n1437\t| Crowd and court | `crowdCheer` (1.4 s noise swell), `crowdGroan` (noise down-sweep), `ooh`, `step_sand`, `dive` (slide noise), `high_five` (clap), `glare` (shimmer bell), `seagull` (sine squeak glides) |\n1438\t| Pool | `splash`, `hopLand` (plop) |\n1439\t| UI | `ui_tick`, `ui_select`, `ui_back`, `ui_error`, `ui_tab` |\n1440\t| Casino | `cash` (coin arpeggio), `chip` (click), `card_deal`, `card_flip`, `reel_spin` (a looped tick), `reel_stop` (clunk), `wheel_spin`, `ball_rattle` |\n1441\t| Story and misc | `gift_unwrap` (paper noise plus chime), `heart_up` and `heart_down` (arpeggios), `shutter`, `flash`, `firework` (boom and crackle), `door` |\n1442\t\n1443\t**4.24.3 Animalese voices** (`G.voice`). Synthesized letter by letter on the voice bus.\n1444\t\n1445\t- **Speaker profile:** `{ base: Hz, range: semitones, rate: letters/s, formant: × shift, wave: 'saw' | 'pulse' |\n1446\t  'triangle', breath: 0..1, vib: Hz }`. The values are in §5.1.\n1447\t- **Letters to sounds:**\n1448\t\n1449\t| Letter class | Sound |\n1450\t| --- | --- |\n1451\t| vowels a e i o u y | a 70 ms voiced tone at pitch p through two bandpass \"formants\" × the formant shift (Q 6): a 800/1200, e 450/1900, i 300/2300, o 500/900, u 350/750 |\n1452\t| plosives b d g k p t | a 12 ms noise burst, then a 40 ms schwa (500/1500) |\n1453\t| fricatives f h s z c x | 45 ms of high-passed noise |\n1454\t| nasals and liquids l m n r w j v | 50 ms of triangle at p, lowpass 900 |\n1455\t| pauses | comma 120 ms, period 220 ms; digits and other marks silent |\n1456\t\n1457\t- **Pitch:** each letter is `base × 2^(range·n/12)`, where n follows a gentle random walk on the `cosmetic` rng seeded\n1458\t  by the line's hash, so a line always sounds the same.\n1459\t- **Contours:** questions rise over the last 4 letters; exclamations go up 3 semitones and × 1.15 rate; ellipses slow\n1460\t  to × .7.\n1461\t- **Emotion** from the line's `mood`: happy +2 semitones and bouncier; angry −1, × 1.2 rate, pulse wave; sad −2,\n1462\t  × .8 rate, falling.\n1463\t- **Two ways in:** the dialog's per-letter hook (patch 3), at typing speed, keeps speech and text together.\n1464\t  `voice.say(text, who, mood)` plays barks without a box: calls (\"MINE!\"), cheers, laughs (\"hahaha\" as three rising\n1465\t  /a/ blips), gasps.\n1466\t- The Voices slider sets the volume; mute is respected; headless it does nothing.\n1467\t\n1468\t### 4.25 Art direction and assets\n1469\t\n1470\t**4.25.1 Look.** The engine's native PS1-era pixel art, following every step of API.md's Look target: `ps1` with\n1471\texpand, HD Humanoids at size 1.15–1.4, dressed characters in real palettes, backdrops, textured floors, 3–8 props a\n1472\tscreen, effects on every hit, `E.tones` shading, title fonts, lights and portraits.\n1473\t\n1474\t**Palette:**\n1475\t\n1476\t| Group | Colors |\n1477\t| --- | --- |\n1478\t| sea | `#0b5a7a` → `#2ec4c9` → `#9ff3e8` |\n1479\t| sand | `#f3d9a4`, `#e2c088`; wet `#c9a06a` |\n1480\t| foliage | `#2f8f4e`, `#5fc35a` |\n1481\t| sunset | `#ff9e5e`, `#ff5f7a`, `#6a3fa0` |\n1482\t| night | `#14163a`; neon `#ff5fa2`, `#5ff0ff` |\n1483\t| gold accents | `#ffd36a` |\n1484\t\n1485\t**Light by time of day:**\n1486\t\n1487\t| Time | Light |\n1488\t| --- | --- |\n1489\t| morning | ambient .9, slightly cool |\n1490\t| afternoon | ambient 1.0, warm |\n1491\t| Day 5 afternoon | sunset tint |\n1492\t| night | ambient .38; torches, lamps, neon and floodlights as `game.lights` |\n1493\t\n1494\tLocations at night also try `game.enableGPU({ map })` (it falls back to canvas lighting by itself).\n1495\t\n1496\t**4.25.2 Characters.**\n1497\t\n1498\t**The `athletic` build:** `{ legUpper: 7.1, legLower: 7.2, hipZ: 13.9, torso: 8.9, shoulderHalf: 2.95, headR: 3.0,\n1499\tneck: 1.4, armUpper: 5.1, armLower: 4.9, hipHalf: 2.05, limbW: 1.75, torsoW: 2.7, stride: 7.4, speedRef: 80 }`.\n1500\t\n1501\t- Faces use `face: { eyes: 'big', bangs: .5 }`.\n1502\t- Arms are bare (`sleeves: 'none'`) unless the suit has sleeves. Legs are skin color. Feet are bare or in sandals.\n1503\t\n1504\t**Swimsuits** (`outfit: 'swim'`):\n1505\t\n1506\t| cut | torso | hips and thighs | arms |\n1507\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1508\t| `onepiece` | main color over the whole torso plate, a scoop neckline (a skin wedge at the front top), straps | a brief band (top 15% of the thigh) | bare |\n1509\t| `racer` | onepiece plus accent side panels and racer-back straps | brief | bare |\n1510\t| `halter` | onepiece with a halter strap to the neck (trim) | brief | bare |\n1511\t| `sport2` | a crop top from the shoulders to 55% of the torso; skin midriff from 55% to 88%; the bottom band from 88% | shorts to 35% of the thigh, or a brief with `brief: true` | bare |\n1512\t| `tankini` | a top to 80% of the torso | shorts to 30% of the thigh | bare |\n1513\t| `rash` | a rash guard: whole torso plus sleeves (short or long) in main, with a zip line (trim) | board shorts to 45% of the thigh, in accent | sleeves |\n1514\t| `sarong` | onepiece | a wrap skirt (the engine's tunic slab) in accent, knotted at the hip | bare |\n1515\t\n1516\t**Patterns.** Drawn per pixel inside the filled torso and shorts polygons, with 1-px features so they read on a 50-px\n1517\tcharacter.\n1518\t\n1519\t| Pattern | Look |\n1520\t| --- | --- |\n1521\t| `solid` | plain |\n1522\t| `stripes` | horizontal accent rows every 2 px |\n1523\t| `pin` | thin vertical lines |\n1524\t| `dots` | a 2-px offset grid |\n1525\t| `waves` | scallops |\n1526\t| `stars` | 3-px stars |\n1527\t| `floral` | 3-px flowers in accent and trim |\n1528\t| `palms` | leaf strokes |\n1529\t| `check` | 2-px gingham with a blended cross |\n1530\t| `gradient` | 3 bands from main to accent |\n1531\t| `geo` | zigzag |\n1532\t| `scales` | small arcs |\n1533\t| `sevens` | tiny 7s |\n1534\t| `lame` | gold sparkle dither with an animated glint |\n1535\t\n1536\t**Hair and hats:**\n1537\t\n1538\t| Style | Shape |\n1539\t| --- | --- |\n1540\t| `twinbuns` | two balls (.55 headR) on the top sides, plus short tails |\n1541\t| `bun` | one ball at the back top |\n1542\t| `braid` | a simulated chain like `long`, with alternating segment widths and a tie |\n1543\t| `bob` | a cap down to the jaw, with side bangs |\n1544\t| `puff` | a big ball (1.1 headR) at the back top, with a hairband in trim |\n1545\t| `curly` | a bob with a bumpy dithered outline |\n1546\t| `sunhat` (hat) | a wide brim ellipse with a band |\n1547\t| `visor` (hat) | a cap with no crown |\n1548\t\n1549\t**Accessories** draw through `extras` (§5.2.2 lists them).\n1550\t\n1551\t**Rig sheet.** `tools/rigsheet.mjs` renders every fighter in every suit, at 4 facings, in the court, servecam,\n1552\tthreequarter and iso views, at 2×, into `test-output/rigsheet/`. Screenshots are the check for art.\n1553\t\n1554\t**4.25.3 Environment assets.** `E.SHAPES` written per `docs/ASSETS.md` and checked with `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs`:\n1555\t\n1556\t| Group | Shapes |\n1557\t| --- | --- |\n1558\t| Beach | `umbrella` (params color, stripes: pole and an 8-segment canopy), `lounger`, `beachtowel`, `cooler`, `sandcastle`, `surfboard` (params color), `surfrack`, `lifeguard` (tower), `bleacher` (3 tiers), `scoreboard` (flip cards; params left, right), `djbooth` (speakers and a gold disc), `netpost` (with antenna), `tikibar` (thatch hut, counter, stools), `changinghut` |\n1559\t| Pool | `cabana`, `poolfloat` (round pad; params color), `flamingo` (inflatable), `pooledge` (tiled coping), `deckchair` |\n1560\t| Casino | `slotmachine` (params color), `bjtable` (half-moon felt), `roulettetable` (with the wheel bowl), `cashier` (a cage), `neonsign` (glow material), `velvetrope` |\n1561\t| Promenade | `shopfront` (facade with an awning; params color and sign), `icecreamcart`, `bench`, `planter` |\n1562\t| Villa | `bed`, `wardrobe`, `desk`, `mailbox`, `rug` |\n1563\t| Island | `seaplane`, `dockplanks`, `lighthouse` |\n1564\t\n1565\t- **Engine props:** `torch` (tiki torches, `light: true`), `lamp`, `palm`, `flowers`, `rock`, `chandelier`, `sign`.\n1566\t- **Store:** cut `kenney-pirate:palm-detailed-straight`, `kenney-pirate:boat-row-large` and `kenney-holiday:present-a-cube`\n1567\t  with `tools/asset-set.mjs`, then load them with `E.addAssets`.\n1568\t- Shop windows show posed rigs, not mannequin shapes.\n1569\t\n1570\t**Materials:** `sand` (tuned), `wetsand`, `pooltile` (tiles, aqua), sea and pool `water` with a shimmer floor tag,\n1571\t`boardwalk` (bleached planks), `felt` (green), `carpet` (casino diamonds), `gold`.\n1572\t\n1573\t**Backdrops** (`E.Backdrop`, custom per time of day): a sky gradient, the sun or moon, clouds, distant teal islands\n1574\t(`mountains` layer), the volcano's silhouette, and a `sea` layer with glints. At night: stars, the moon, and a lit\n1575\tyacht.\n1576\t\n1577\t**Effects:** sand puffs, splashes (blue bits and a ring), sparkles on PERFECT, hearts (gifts and affinity), confetti\n1578\t(wins), fireworks (the party), a coin shower (jackpot), sweat drops (Ingrid's running joke), the glare star (Sonny).\n1579\t\n1580\t**4.25.4 UI art.**\n1581\t\n1582\t- The logo.\n1583\t- Icons made with `E.sprite`: heart (full, half, empty), coin, chip, gift box, hanger (suits), sunglasses, star, mood\n1584\t  icons, weather icons, lock, NEW badge, camera.\n1585\t- Glyph icons (§4.1.2); gradient panels with borders; portraits from the rigs.\n1586\t\n1587\t### 4.26 Animation (`15-anim.js`)\n1588\t\n1589\t**Technique, in layers:**\n1590\t\n1591\t1. The rig's own procedural walk, run, idle and jump.\n1592\t2. The **arm-IK overlay:** after `rig.update`, override the hand targets with `E.ik3` for timed moves, blended by a\n1593\t   weight curve (wind 0→1, hold, release 1→0). Wrap `rig.solvePose` as AI_GUIDE's \"New animation on the rigs\" shows.\n1594\t3. Body offsets through rig state: `crouch`, `lean`, `air`, `land`, `flip`, `down`.\n1595\t4. Mocap clips through `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)`, faded with `rig.mocapW`, or upper body only with\n1596\t   `rig.mocapMask = 'upper'`.\n1597\t5. Faces through `expr`.\n1598\t\n1599\tAnimation is driven from the simulation's plan, not the other way round. A spike's jump starts at t* minus its rise time,\n1600\tand the hand's IK target is the ball's position at t*.\n1601\t\n1602\t**Moves:**\n1603\t\n1604\t| Move | Timing (s) | How |\n1605\t| --- | --- | --- |\n1606\t| ready stance | loop | crouch .35, hands low in front (IK), weight shifts, eyes on the ball |\n1607\t| bump | .12 wind, .08 hit, .3 recover | crouch .55 then extend; hands joined at hip height in front (IK); arms swing up 20° through contact |\n1608\t| dig (low) | as bump | crouch .8, `land: .4` |\n1609\t| set | .1, .06, .25 | hands above the forehead (IK, wrists back), knees push; a small hop for quick sets |\n1610\t| approach and spike | .38 rise, .06 hit, .3 land | 2-step approach toward the net; `air`; the right arm cocks back (IK) then whips over (the engine's `overhead` arc with `hop`); the left arm points at the ball; land squash (`rig.land(.6)`) |\n1611\t| shot (cut / roll) | as spike, slower arm | open-hand poke (IK) |\n1612\t| block | .28 rise, .18 hold, .3 fall | both arms straight up over the net (IK), hands angled forward; land |\n1613\t| float serve | .5 toss, .1 hit | the left hand tosses (IK), then the right arm hits overhead, with a step |\n1614\t| jump serve | .6 toss, .4 approach, .1 hit | high toss, 2 steps, a jump, a spike-like swing |\n1615\t| dive | .22 lunge, .3 slide, .45 down | the mocap `Dive_Roll` (CMU), or `flip` with a forward lunge; arms out; a sand trail |\n1616\t| call | .5 | free arm up, `expr: 'shout'` |\n1617\t| high five | .5 | partners turn to face each other; the near hands meet at shoulder height + 4 (IK to the midpoint); clap sound and a sparkle |\n1618\t| celebrations | 1.2 | Rin `Bow`; Lola `Victory Fist Pump`; Ingrid `Head Nod` with a small fist; Amara `Dance Charleston` or `Cartwheel`; Tess `Wave_Hello` (a shaka); Mei `Backflip`; Sonny `Cheering_Two_Hands`; Pepper `Salute` (deadpan) |\n1619\t| disappointment | 1 | `Idle_No_Loop`, `Shrug`, the facepalm pose |\n1620\t| give / receive a gift | 1 | give: both hands forward holding a gift-box sprite. Receive: love = a hop, `Cheer_One_arm` and hearts; like = `Yes` or `Head Nod`; refuse = `Reject` or `Idle_FoldArms_Loop` |\n1621\t| idles | loop | `Idle_Talking_Loop`; `Sitting_Idle_Loop` (bar stools, loungers); `Sitting_Talking_Loop`; sunbathing (`down: 1` plus the `sunbathe` pose); `Swim_Idle_Loop` and `Swim_Fwd_Loop` (pool); `Stretch_Yawn`; `Jumping_Jacks_Loop` (warm-ups); `Meditate` (Rin); `Idle_TalkingPhone_Loop` (Sonny) |\n1622\t| party | loop | `Dance_Loop`, `Dance Body Roll`, `Dance Reach Hip`, `Dance Charleston` |\n1623\t| Pool Hop | .45 a hop | crouch, an `air` arc between pads, a land squash. A slip blends `hurt` and `down` with a splash, then `Swim_Fwd_Loop` back and `ClimbUp_1m_RM` onto the pad |\n1624\t| casino | loop | sitting at slots, leaning on the table, cheering on wins |\n1625\t| photo poses | hold | Wave, Peace (IK hand by the face with a two-finger sprite), Hips, Cheer, Stretch, Look Back (torso twist and head turn), Sit, Victory, Salute, Bow |\n1626\t| Sonny gags | 1–2 | `Fall_On_Face` (tripping into the pool), `Confused`, `Angry` |\n1627\t\n1628\t**The clip set to cut.** Make it with `tools/anim-set.mjs` into `vendor/mocap/aoa-clips.js` (name `AOA`) and keep it\n1629\tunder about 250 KB. Quote the `--clips` argument, since some names have spaces.\n1630\t\n1631\t| Source set | Clips |\n1632\t| --- | --- |\n1633\t| quaternius | `Idle_Talking_Loop`, `Sitting_Enter`, `Sitting_Idle_Loop`, `Sitting_Talking_Loop`, `Sitting_Exit`, `Swim_Idle_Loop`, `Swim_Fwd_Loop`, `Dance_Loop`, `Idle_FoldArms_Loop`, `Idle_No_Loop`, `Yes`, `Idle_TalkingPhone_Loop`, `LayToIdle`, `ClimbUp_1m_RM`, `Jump_Start`, `Jump_Loop`, `Jump_Land` |\n1634\t| mesh2motion | `Bow`, `Victory`, `Victory Fist Pump`, `Cheer_One_arm`, `Cheering_Two_Hands`, `Dance Charleston`, `Dance Body Roll`, `Dance Reach Hip`, `Reject`, `Head Nod`, `Greeting`, `Salute`, `Backflip`, `Meditate`, `Confused`, `Angry` |\n1635\t| cmu | `Dive_Roll`, `Wave_Hello`, `Shrug`, `Stretch_Yawn`, `Cartwheel`, `Jumping_Jacks_Loop`, `Fall_On_Face` |\n1636\t\n1637\t**Checks.**\n1638\t\n1639\t- Check every clip on the athletic build in the rig sheet. Use `mocapMask: 'upper'` where the legs look wrong, and fall\n1640\t  back to a procedural pose for any clip that still fails.\n1641\t- Record every move with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` and look for a wind-up, a strike and a clean settle, with no jerks or\n1642\t  backward sweeps. Keep the strips in `test-output/filmstrips/`.\n1643\t\n1644\t---\n1645\t\n1646\t## 5. Content\n1647\t\n1648\t### 5.1 Cast\n1649\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf","uuid":"7f359b92-71a7-4c74-b2a8-0643e3db951c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:12:02.535Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**Goal:** cross the lagoon on 32 floating pads in `T.poolTime` (40 s). Each pad shows the glyph of one of the four face\nbuttons for the current device (✕○□△, A B X Y, or J L K I keycaps). Press it as the hopper lands, on the beat.\n\n**Rhythm.**\n\n- The song `lagoon` runs at `T.poolBpm` (112) with `sync: true`. One hop per beat, judged against the music clock\n  (`audio.pos`).\n- PERFECT is within 60 ms and GOOD within 130 ms (× `T.poolWindowMul`).\n- Too early, too late or the wrong button: she slips, splashes, swims back (1.8 s), and continues from the same pad on\n  the next bar.\n- Each run of 8 PERFECT hops in a row adds +1 s.\n\n**Twists:**\n\n- from pad 12, **wobble pads**: the glyph flips between two buttons and settles one beat before you need it;\n- from pad 22, **double pads**: two glyphs; press both together.\n\n**Score and reward.** Time, perfects and falls give the prize (§4.12). Your best time is saved. Characters at the pool\ncheer, and a present partner gains +2 affinity when you clear it.\n\n**Camera and effects:** the Broadcast angle follows the hopper; pads bob to the beat; splashes; water shimmer.\n\nThe attract mode runs Pool Hop with a perfect bot.\n\n### 4.16 Casino Fortuna (`41-casino.js`, nights only)\n\n**The floor** is a `threequarter` map with neon, chandeliers and lights, and a crowd. Stations:\n\n- **Cashier:** chips at S$100 each; buy in steps of 10, 50 or 100; cash out any time. The chip count shows on every\n  casino screen.\n- **6 slot machines.**\n- **Blackjack table**, dealer Pepper.\n- **Roulette table**, croupier Kai.\n- **Sonny's VIP lounge**, for story events.\n\nOn the first night Sonny hands you 20 free chips and explains the games. A prize counter swaps 300 chips for the\n\"Jackpot\" suit.\n\n**Fortuna Sevens (pachislot).**\n\n- 3 reels with 3 visible rows. Bet 1, 2 or 3 chips: 1 = the centre line, 2 = plus the top and bottom lines, 3 = plus\n  both diagonals.\n- ✕ / Space spins. Then ✕ ○ □ (J K L) stop reels 1, 2 and 3. A stop \"slips\" 0–4 symbols on the `casino` rng, so\n  timing matters a little.\n- Strips of 21 stops per reel. Payouts per line bet:\n\n| Line | Pays |\n| --- | --- |\n| 7-7-7 | ×100, with a jackpot fanfare and coin shower |\n| BAR-BAR-BAR | ×30 |\n| Sonny-Sonny-Sonny | ×20 (Sonny is wild) |\n| Volleyball ×3 | ×12 |\n| Palm ×3 | ×8 |\n| Coconut ×3 | ×5 |\n| Cherry, by count on the line | 1 ×2, 2 ×5, 3 ×10 |\n\n- Tune the strips so the RTP is **92% ± 3** at `T.slotsPayMul` 1 (a simulation test checks it).\n- Spinning reels show blur rows, then a stop clunk and a line highlight.\n\n**Blackjack.**\n\n- 6-deck shoe, reshuffled at 75%. The dealer stands on soft 17 (`T.dealerHitsSoft17` toggles it). Blackjack pays 3:2.\n  Double on any first two cards. Split once; split aces get one card each. No insurance, no surrender.\n- Bets of 1, 5, 10 or 25 chips (a stepper).\n- Controls: ✕/H hit, □/S stand, △/D double, R1/P split (only when legal), ○ leave between hands. Every button is also\n  clickable on screen. The betting phase (left/right sets the bet) and the playing phase each read only their own\n  actions, so S and D never clash with WASD.\n- Cards are pixel sprites (rank glyphs and suit sprites ♠ ♥ ♦ ♣ made with `E.sprite`), dealt with tweens and flipped.\n  Pepper has deadpan lines for a blackjack and a bust.\n\n**Roulette.**\n\n- A single-zero wheel in real order: 0, 32, 15, 19, 4, 21, 2, 25, 17, 34, 6, 27, 13, 36, 11, 30, 8, 23, 10, 5, 24, 16,\n  33, 1, 20, 14, 31, 9, 22, 18, 29, 7, 28, 12, 35, 3, 26.\n- **Betting layout:** a cursor moved with the stick, WASD or the mouse.\n\n| Bet | Pays |\n| --- | --- |\n| straight number | 35:1 |\n| red/black, odd/even, 1–18/19–36 | 1:1 |\n| dozens, columns | 2:1 |\n\n- Controls: ✕ place a chip (L1/R1 sizes 1/5/10/25), □ remove, △ spin, ○ leave.\n- An inset wheel shows the pocket ring turning while the ball spirals in, slows, bounces two pockets and settles. Then\n  the result is highlighted, payouts made, and a strip shows the last 10 results.\n- The dev-only toggle `T.rouletteDoubleZero` gives an American wheel.\n\nLeaving the casino ends the night and goes to the day-end card.\n\n### 4.17 Postcards (photo mode) and album (`42-photo.js`)\n\n**Where:** the pause menu's \"Take a Postcard\", or Create / C in walkable locations and on match results. Never in hub\nsessions or the attract. Gameplay time freezes (`timeScale` 0), while cosmetic motion (water, breathing idles) keeps\ngoing.\n\n**Controls:**\n\n| Input | Does |\n| --- | --- |\n| left stick / WASD | pan the focus |\n| right stick / right-drag | orbit at any angle (`game.rotateView`) |\n| L2/R2 / wheel | zoom .75–2.5 |\n| ✕ | take the photo |\n| ○ | exit |\n| □ | choose the subject: you, or any NPC present |\n| △ | the panel |\n| R3 / H | hide the UI |\n\nThe △ panel has:\n\n- **pose:** Wave, Peace, Hips, Cheer, Stretch, Look Back, Sit, Victory, Salute, Bow;\n- **expression:** smile, shout, wince, neutral;\n- **filter:** Clean, Sunny, Sepia, Retro, Night Glow;\n- **frame:** none, or a postcard border with a \"Greetings from Isla Fortuna\" stamp and the date.\n\n**Taking a photo.** The shutter sound and a white flash, then a \"developing\" postcard slides to a corner. It is saved\nin `state.album` (at most 24; asks before replacing the oldest) as a **spec**, never pixels:\n`{ loc, day, slot, tod, weather, cam: { x, y, z, yaw, zoom, view }, people: [{ id, suit, acc, pose, expr, x, y, facing\n}], filter, frame }`.\n\n**The album** (Villa, or the menu for the latest save):\n\n- A 4×2 grid of live thumbnails: each spec is re-rendered at half size.\n- Opening one re-renders it full screen, live, so the palms still sway.\n- □ deletes (with a confirm); △ \"Set as title backdrop\"; R1 exports a PNG download (not in sessions).\n\nThe credits slideshow re-renders the album, plus a group photo taken automatically at the party.\n\n### 4.18 Story, dialogue, voices, cutscenes (`34-story.js`)\n\n- `E.Story` holds `people` for every speaker (portrait = their rig) and the nodes from `05-data-text.js`. Its `on`\n  events run game actions: `startMatch`, `giveMoney`, `giveItem`, `setPartner`, `openShop`, `photo`, `fade`.\n  `story.state()` goes in the save.\n- **The dialog box:** bottom, 2 lines, the name tag in the speaker's color, a portrait with expression\n  (`portraitOpts`), markup for emphasis (`{c=#ffd36a}…{/c}`, `{wave}`, `{shake}`). The Animalese voice runs from the\n  per-letter hook (patch 3). Text speed is a setting. Hold ○ or right click to fast-forward; Options on a cutscene asks\n  \"Skip scene?\".\n- **Cutscenes** are `game.script` generators: camera tweens, walk-ons (`game.tween` on bodies), emotes\n  (`story.emote(target, 'heart' | '!' | '?' | 'note' | 'dots')`), fades. The list is in §5.5.\n\n### 4.19 Save and load (`30-vacation.js`)\n\n**Slots:** `game.saves` (3 slots plus autosave). The title's Load and the Villa journal's Save open `saves.show('load'\n| 'save')`. The game autosaves at every slot start; Continue loads `saves.latest()`.\n\n- `saves.write = () => ({ data: G.state, place: locationName, level: 'Day ' + day })`;\n- `read = save => G.loadState(save.data)`, with `version: 1` and a `migrate`.\n\n**State shape:**\n\n```js\n{ v: 1, seed, day: 1, slot: 0, weather: ['sunny', …], me: 'rin', money: 30000, chips: 0,\n  wardrobe: { suits: ['seigaiha'], acc: ['ribbon'] }, wearing: { suit: 'seigaiha', acc: ['ribbon'] },\n  npcWear: { lola: { suit: 'estrella', acc: ['sweatband'] }, … }, bag: { mango_smoothie: 1 },\n  affinity: { lola: 20, … }, mood: { lola: 'happy', … }, known: { lola: { hot_sauce: 'love' } },\n  partner: null, teams: [['lola', 'tess'], ['amara', 'mei']], record: { 'lola+tess': [0, 0] },\n  flags: {}, story: {}, chatted: {}, gifted: {}, album: [], titlePostcard: null,\n  stats: { matches: 0, wins: 0, points: 0, kills: 0, aces: 0, blocks: 0, poolBest: null, casinoNet: 0, gifts: 0,\n           photos: 0, earned: 0, spent: 0 } }\n```\n\n**New Vacation+** (after an ending) keeps the wardrobe, album and lifetime stats. It resets the days and affinity (to\nbase +10) and starts money at S$30,000 plus 10% of your final money.\n\n**Unlocks** for Beach Match (suits ever owned; everything after the first ending) live in `E.store('aoa-unlocks')`.\n\n### 4.20 Front end: boot, title, menu, How to Play, About (`50-title.js`)\n\n**Boot.** Boot steps build the rigs, maps, music and caches behind the engine's boot screen, with messages: \"Raking the\nsand\", \"Inflating volleyballs\", \"Chilling the smoothies\", \"Counting Sonny's chips\", \"Polishing the golden sunglasses\".\n\n**Title.**\n\n- A sunset beach backdrop: sea layers, the sun, distant islands, palms, gentle waves.\n- The six fighters stand on the sand in their signature suits, each with her own idle: Rin stretching, Lola flexing,\n  Ingrid fanning herself, Amara dancing, Tess juggling a ball, Mei waving. Now and then Sonny jogs across the background\n  with a giant trophy.\n- The logo **AHEAD OR ALIVE**: `E.font.title` scale 4, colors `['#fff7d6', '#ffd36a', '#ff9e5e', '#ff5f7a']`, depth 3,\n  with a small spinning volleyball beside it. Under it **XTREME BEACH VOLLEYBALL** at scale 2, white with a teal shadow.\n- A blinking \"PRESS ✕\" in the current device's glyph.\n- A footer with the version label (`E.versionLabel()`) and \"An original parody-tribute game\".\n- If a postcard is set as the title backdrop, it renders behind the logo instead.\n\n**Main menu.** A big list on the left; a turning fighter preview on the right.\n\n- **New Vacation**\n- **Continue** (if a save exists)\n- **Load**\n- **Beach Match**\n- **Album** (if there are postcards)\n- **How to Play**\n- **Settings** (`game.menu('settings')`)\n- **About & Credits**\n\n10 s idle starts the attract mode.\n\n**How to Play.** 10 pages, one idea each, with a live mini-scene in the panel and the current device's glyphs:\n\n1. Moving and the ring\n2. The touch chain: bump, set, spike\n3. Aiming and shots\n4. Serving\n5. Blocking and diving\n6. Calls and chemistry\n7. The vacation: slots, map, money\n8. Friends and gifts\n9. Casino and Pool Hop\n10. Postcards\n\n**About & Credits.** Pages turned with L1/R1, left/right or the on-screen arrows; the stick scrolls; large text, one\nfield per line. Contents in §10:\n\n1. Credits\n2. Source Information\n3. Testing Feedback\n4. Engine Feedback\n5. Prompt Feedback\n\n### 4.21 Attract mode (`51-attract.js`)\n\n**Trigger.** 10.0 s without input on `title` or `menu`. Input means any key, a pad button, a stick past its dead zone,\nthe mouse moving more than 4 px, a click, the wheel, or a touch; each resets the timer.\n\n**Playlist.** A director kept alive across scenes (`game.script(…, { keep: true })` plus the overlay watcher) plays it,\nre-seeded each cycle for variety. Demo scenes run on a throwaway demo state, never the player's save.\n\n1. **Match, about 50 s.** AI vs AI on Sunset Courts with random fighters, outfits and time of day: `spectacle` AI, the\n   camera cutting between Broadcast and Serve Cam every 2 points, commentary and highlight replays on.\n2. **Vacation montage, about 50 s.** 7 beats of 6–8 s, each with a big caption banner:\n\n| Caption | Shows |\n| --- | --- |\n| FIVE DAYS IN PARADISE | the island map flying from morning to night |\n| MAKE FRIENDS · GIVE GIFTS | a gift scene with hearts |\n| COLLECT 21 SWIMSUITS | the shop preview cycling suits |\n| POOL HOP | a perfect-bot run |\n| CASINO NIGHTS | slots hitting 7-7-7, then a blackjack |\n| SNAP POSTCARDS | a photo-mode orbit |\n| BEAT THE HOUSE | a slice of the final against Sonny & Pepper, with the Golden Glare |\n\n3. **Title card, 5 s**, with \"PRESS ✕\". Then repeat.\n\n**Rules.**\n\n- The AI may cheat freely: perfect timing, scripted outcomes, instant travel.\n- **Any input** returns to `title` with the input consumed, so it doesn't also press a menu item, and the title music\n  resumes.\n- A \"DEMO\" tag shows top left. On touch-only devices the bottom banner reads \"Controller or keyboard required\".\n- Sound starts only after the browser's first gesture (engine rule), so before that the attract runs silent.\n\n### 4.22 Dev mode (`53-dev.js`)\n\n**Reach.** The pause menu's **Dev Mode**, in every pausable scene. Once opened, F1 (or L3+R3 on a pad) reopens it for\nthe rest of the session. Never in hub sessions.\n\n**While it is open:**\n\n- gameplay time is frozen (`game.timeScale = 0`; the overlay updates on real time);\n- the panel is a 10-foot canvas overlay built with the UI kit;\n- tabs (L1/R1, Q/E or a click): **Tools · Match · Vacation · Minigames · Presentation · Tuning**;\n- **Back to game** restores `timeScale`.\n\n**4.22.1 Tools** (every button calls `game.debug.tools.*`).\n\n| Tab | Tools |\n| --- | --- |\n| Tools | jump to any scene, location or minigame; set the day (1–5) and slot; jump to the Semifinal, the Final, the party or ending, the credits; restart the scene; reset the save (with a confirm) |\n| Match | start a match against any pair; force a point left or right; set the score; end the match (win/lose); CPU controls your player (watch); Perfect Player (all your presses PERFECT); the debug overlay (trajectory line, landing point, every player's P* ring, AI assignment and state labels, a judge-window bar); slow motion ×.25 / ×.5 / ×1; frame step (one step per press while frozen); switch camera |\n| Vacation | money +10k / +100k / set to 0; chips +100; unlock all items; fill the gift bag ×3; set affinity per fighter (a slider 0–100); set mood; make or clear partner; reveal all likes |\n| Minigames | Pool Hop autopilot; slots: force 7-7-7 next; blackjack: deal a blackjack; roulette: force a number |\n| Presentation | time-of-day override (0–24 h); weather (sunny/cloudy/rain); show FPS (engine setting); **Voice Lab** (pick a speaker and a preset phrase, play it); music jukebox; SFX board; rig sheet viewer (fighter × suit × pose × view) |\n\n**4.22.2 Live sliders** (the Tuning tab).\n\n- Changes apply at once: every system reads `G.T` every step.\n- Each slider shows its default as a tick. △ or R on a slider resets it.\n- **Reset all to defaults** asks to confirm.\n- Values persist in `E.store('aoa-dev-tuning')`, and **Copy JSON** copies them to the clipboard.\n\n| Group | Key | Default | Range | Step |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Ball | `ballGravity` | 330 | 180–500 | 5 |\n| Ball | `ballDrag` | .12 | 0–.6 | .01 |\n| Ball | `passT` | 1.05 | .7–1.6 | .05 |\n| Ball | `setT` | 1.1 | .7–1.6 | .05 |\n| Ball | `serveT` | 1.3 | .9–1.8 | .05 |\n| Ball | `jumpServeT` | .85 | .6–1.3 | .05 |\n| Ball | `spikeSpeed` | 330 | 220–480 | 5 |\n| Ball | `shotT` | .95 | .6–1.4 | .05 |\n| Ball | `netCordOver` | .45 | 0–1 | .05 |\n| Timing | `perfectWin` (s) | .05 | .02–.12 | .005 |\n| Timing | `greatWin` (s) | .10 | .05–.2 | .005 |\n| Timing | `okWin` (s) | .16 | .08–.3 | .01 |\n| Timing | `reach` | 14 | 8–24 | 1 |\n| Timing | `diveReach` | 16 | 6–30 | 1 |\n| Timing | `blockRise` (s) | .28 | .15–.45 | .01 |\n| Players | `runSpeed` | 96 | 60–140 | 2 |\n| Players | `autoMove` | .85 | 0–1 | .05 |\n| AI | `aiSkillMul` (× the day's base) | 1 | .3–1.6 | .02 |\n| AI | `aiReaction` (s) | .25 | 0–.6 | .01 |\n| AI | `aiSpeedMul` | 1 | .6–1.4 | .02 |\n| AI | `chemistry` | .3 | 0–.6 | .02 |\n| Match | `pointsToWin` (vacation) | 7 | 3–21 | 1 |\n| Economy | `prizeMul` | 1 | 0–3 | .05 |\n| Economy | `priceMul` | 1 | .25–3 | .05 |\n| Economy | `startMoney` | 30000 | 0–200000 | 5000 |\n| Social | `affinityGainMul` | 1 | 0–3 | .05 |\n| Social | `affinityDecay` | 2 | 0–10 | 1 |\n| Social | `inviteThreshold` | 40 | 0–100 | 1 |\n| Social | `giftThreshold` | 0 | −3–3 | 1 |\n| Pool Hop | `poolBpm` | 112 | 80–150 | 2 |\n| Pool Hop | `poolWindowMul` | 1 | .5–2 | .05 |\n| Pool Hop | `poolTime` (s) | 40 | 20–80 | 1 |\n| Casino | `slotsPayMul` | 1 | .5–1.5 | .01 |\n| Casino | `dealerHitsSoft17` | off | toggle | — |\n| Casino | `rouletteDoubleZero` | off | toggle | — |\n| Presentation | `textSpeed` (letters/s) | 45 | 10–200 | 5 |\n| Presentation | `cameraZoomMul` | 1 | .7–1.3 | .02 |\n\n### 4.23 AI Hub sessions (`25-netplay.js`)\n\n**Head tags** in the deliverable. Keep the goal ≤ 60 characters and the howto ≤ 80.\n\n```html\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"1-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"5\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"Win the beach volleyball match: first to 7, by 2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Stick/WASD move · Cross/Space hit on time · Circle/Shift dive · Square/E shot\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Game\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1-4\">\n```\n\n**Flow when `AIHub.active` is true.**\n\n1. **Build the game for a session:** `menu: false` (no pause), `autoPause: false`, `corner: false`,\n   `fullscreen: false`, no saves, touch `'never'`, no title and no attract.\n2. **Connect.** Boot straight into the `hub` scene, which calls\n   `const info = await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'shared-world', seats: [1, 4], card: true })`. If it returns `null`, go to\n   `title` and run normally.\n3. **Teams.** Left = seat indexes 0 and 2; Right = 1 and 3. Empty slots are CPUs (Normal).\n   - Fighters: shuffle the six with `AIHub.rng('cast')`; everyone wears signature suits.\n   - Court time: `AIHub.rng('court')`.\n   - Each human's fighter gets a ground ring and a name tag in her seat color (`#e8443a`, `#3b82f6`, `#22c55e`,\n     `#f5b700`). Names are drawn with `E.font` on the canvas, never inserted as HTML.\n4. **Our own card**, until `start`:\n   - Shows: the court at sunset with the four fighters lined up (CPUs tagged), the logo, the goal line, this player's\n     controls in her device's glyphs, every player's name in her color with a READY tick (from `card.ready`), and the\n     countdown from `card.left` (\"Paused: more time\" while `paused`).\n   - Two buttons: **READY** (✕ / Enter / click) → `AIHub.answer('ready')`; **MORE TIME** (△ / T / click) →\n     `AIHub.answer('more')`, which toggles.\n   - Nothing else to choose. Call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as the card is built, with no key press.\n   - The server copy (`AIHub.server`) builds the world, calls `ready()`, and draws a minimal \"Hosting\" screen.\n5. **Start.** On `start`, the intro walk-on plays. Play begins when `AIHub.time() >= 0`, with a 3-2-1 countdown from the\n   negative clock.\n6. **Messages.** All are small JSON with short keys.\n\n| Msg | Direction | Rate | Reliable | Content |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `m` | client → host | 12/s while playing (also as a heartbeat) | no | `{ t: 'm', at, x, y, f, a }`: own fighter's position, facing, action |\n| `c` | client → host | per judged press | yes | `{ t: 'c', at, k, q, aim: [x, y], sh }`: a touch claim; `at` = hub ms of contact, `k` kind, `q` quality, `sh` shot or play |\n| `v` | client → host | when serving | yes | `{ t: 'v', at, q, aim, jump }`: a serve claim |\n| `s` | host → all | 12/s | no | `{ t: 's', at, p: [[id, x, y, f, a, u], …], sc: [l, r], ph, sv, tc }` |\n| `b` | host → all | each launch | yes | `{ t: 'b', t0, p, v, k, g, ay, wob, by, kind }` |\n| `e` | host → all | per point, fault or phase | yes | `{ t: 'e', ev, side, why, sc, next }` |\n| final `s` | host → all | once | yes | the last snapshot with `over: 1` |\n\n   The budget: the host sends ≤ 16 messages/s and each client ≤ 14, under the hub's 20/s. Unreliable messages stay\n   under 1,200 bytes.\n7. **Authority.**\n   - The host runs the rules and the AI, and accepts claims.\n   - Each client moves its own fighter at once and sends it at 12 Hz. The host clamps reports to max speed and the court.\n   - Each client judges its own touches against the shared ball. Every copy computes the same trajectory from `b` on the\n     shared clock, so the timing is fair whatever the latency.\n   - The host validates a claim: contact time within the planned window ±.12 s; the claimant within reach + 12 of the\n     ball at that time; the touch still open; the first valid claim wins. It then broadcasts the new launch with\n     `t0 = claim.at`, so every copy continues from the same instant; clients ease the visual jump over .12 s.\n   - Before awarding a point, the host waits for remote claims until `tLand + .25 s`.\n8. **Others' fighters.** Clients interpolate other fighters from snapshots with a 100 ms buffer. A client's own fighter\n   is never overwritten.\n9. **Reporting** (only the host calls `finish()`):\n   - Match over: `AIHub.finish({ standings: [[winner ids…], [loser ids…]], scores: { id: teamScore }, stats: { id: {\n     Points, Kills } }, awards: [{ id, title: 'MVP', detail }] })`.\n   - With one human against CPUs: `standings: [[me]]` and `won: true | false`.\n   - On `time-up`: finish at once with the current score, the team ahead first. If tied, everyone goes in one array.\n10. **Leaving.** On `leave`, that seat becomes a CPU and its fighter plays on. If the host leaves, `end` arrives with\n    `host-left`: show \"Round cancelled\" and stop.\n11. **End.** On `end`: stop input and sound (music off, mute the buses), freeze the simulation, and draw the final\n    standings with names. Send nothing more.\n12. **Session rules.** No pause, quit or title; no dialogs, alerts or new windows; nothing relies on storage; no network\n    but `AIHub.send`. Options is ignored while Create is held (patch 6).\n13. **Outside a session** nothing changes: the client is inert when `!AIHub.active`.\n\n### 4.24 Audio (`12-audio.js`, `06-data-music.js`)\n\n**4.24.1 Music.** The engine's step sequencer plus the instrument patch (patch 4).\n\n**Instruments:**\n\n| Instrument | Built from |\n| --- | --- |\n| `steel` | partials 1, 2, 3, 4.2 at amps 1, .5, .35, .2; decay .5 s |\n| `marimba` | partials 1, 4, 9.9 at amps 1, .3, .05; decay .35 s |\n| `pluck` | saw through lowpass 1800; decay .25 s (ukulele and guitar) |\n| `bell` | partials 1, 2.76, 5.4, 8.9; decay 1.2 s |\n| `organ` | partials 1, 2, 3, 4; held |\n| `pad` | saw + detune 8 cents, lowpass 1200; held |\n\nPlus the engine's square, pulse, triangle, saw and sine waves, and drums.\n\n**Tracks.** Original compositions. Each loops cleanly over 16–32 bars, with named layers so drums can drop in and out.\n\n| id | Where | Tempo, key | Feel and instruments | Chords |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `sunrise` | title, menu | 116, C | bright tropical pop: steel lead, marimba arpeggios, pluck chords, bass, light drums | C G Am F; bridge Dm G |\n| `island` | map, Promenade | 100, F | breezy: ukulele pluck, marimba melody, shaker hats | F Bb C F; Dm Gm C |\n| `spike` | matches | 138, Am | driving synth-pop: square lead, saw bass; drum layer `rally` comes in on long rallies; +6 bpm at match point | Am F C G |\n| `house` | the final | 150, Dm | campy-dramatic: organ stabs, brassy pulse lead, tom rolls, a cheesy key change up a step in the last 8 bars | Dm Bb C A |\n| `lagoon` | pool, Pool Hop | 112, G | bossa-nova: pluck comping, soft steel lead, rim clicks on the quarter notes (the hop beat) | G Em Am D |\n| `boutique` | shops, wardrobe | 108, Bb | cute shopping funk: bell arpeggios, popping bass | Bb Gm Eb F |\n| `neon` | casino | 96, Em | lounge funk: organ, muted bass, swung hats, bell sparkles on wins | Em A vamp; C B7 turnaround |\n| `siesta` | villa, night map | 80, D | gentle pad and marimba lullaby, with a cricket ambience | D Bm G A |\n| `farewell` | party, endings, credits | 124, C → D | anthemic: steel and square in harmony, full drums, firework hits | C G Am F, then the key change to D |\n\n**Jingles** (`audio.sting`): `win` (3 s), `lose`, `ace`, `matchpoint`, `gift_love`, `gift_refuse`, `jackpot`,\n`daystart` (a bright chime), `levelup` (an affinity stage up), `photo`.\n\n**Ambience loops** (noise on the sfx bus): waves (lowpass swells on a 6 s period), wind, crowd murmur, lapping pool\nwater, casino murmur with distant slot jingles, night crickets (pulse chirps). Rain is the engine weather's sound.\n\n**4.24.2 Sound effects** (`audio.define`). Leave about 6 dB of headroom and balance them by ear.\n\n| Group | Effects |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ball | `bump` (soft sine thump 160→90 Hz plus noise), `set` (short tap, 400 Hz), `spike` (noise crack plus sine 120→40, louder with speed), `block` (two-hand slap), `serveToss` (whoosh), `serveHit`, `sand` (lowpass noise 600→150), `net` (rattle: 3 noise ticks), `tape` (tick and wobble), `whistle` (square 2200 Hz with vibrato) |\n| Crowd and court | `crowdCheer` (1.4 s noise swell), `crowdGroan` (noise down-sweep), `ooh`, `step_sand`, `dive` (slide noise), `high_five` (clap), `glare` (shimmer bell), `seagull` (sine squeak glides) |\n| Pool | `splash`, `hopLand` (plop) |\n| UI | `ui_tick`, `ui_select`, `ui_back`, `ui_error`, `ui_tab` |\n| Casino | `cash` (coin arpeggio), `chip` (click), `card_deal`, `card_flip`, `reel_spin` (a looped tick), `reel_stop` (clunk), `wheel_spin`, `ball_rattle` |\n| Story and misc | `gift_unwrap` (paper noise plus chime), `heart_up` and `heart_down` (arpeggios), `shutter`, `flash`, `firework` (boom and crackle), `door` |\n\n**4.24.3 Animalese voices** (`G.voice`). Synthesized letter by letter on the voice bus.\n\n- **Speaker profile:** `{ base: Hz, range: semitones, rate: letters/s, formant: × shift, wave: 'saw' | 'pulse' |\n  'triangle', breath: 0..1, vib: Hz }`. The values are in §5.1.\n- **Letters to sounds:**\n\n| Letter class | Sound |\n| --- | --- |\n| vowels a e i o u y | a 70 ms voiced tone at pitch p through two bandpass \"formants\" × the formant shift (Q 6): a 800/1200, e 450/1900, i 300/2300, o 500/900, u 350/750 |\n| plosives b d g k p t | a 12 ms noise burst, then a 40 ms schwa (500/1500) |\n| fricatives f h s z c x | 45 ms of high-passed noise |\n| nasals and liquids l m n r w j v | 50 ms of triangle at p, lowpass 900 |\n| pauses | comma 120 ms, period 220 ms; digits and other marks silent |\n\n- **Pitch:** each letter is `base × 2^(range·n/12)`, where n follows a gentle random walk on the `cosmetic` rng seeded\n  by the line's hash, so a line always sounds the same.\n- **Contours:** questions rise over the last 4 letters; exclamations go up 3 semitones and × 1.15 rate; ellipses slow\n  to × .7.\n- **Emotion** from the line's `mood`: happy +2 semitones and bouncier; angry −1, × 1.2 rate, pulse wave; sad −2,\n  × .8 rate, falling.\n- **Two ways in:** the dialog's per-letter hook (patch 3), at typing speed, keeps speech and text together.\n  `voice.say(text, who, mood)` plays barks without a box: calls (\"MINE!\"), cheers, laughs (\"hahaha\" as three rising\n  /a/ blips), gasps.\n- The Voices slider sets the volume; mute is respected; headless it does nothing.\n\n### 4.25 Art direction and assets\n\n**4.25.1 Look.** The engine's native PS1-era pixel art, following every step of API.md's Look target: `ps1` with\nexpand, HD Humanoids at size 1.15–1.4, dressed characters in real palettes, backdrops, textured floors, 3–8 props a\nscreen, effects on every hit, `E.tones` shading, title fonts, lights and portraits.\n\n**Palette:**\n\n| Group | Colors |\n| --- | --- |\n| sea | `#0b5a7a` → `#2ec4c9` → `#9ff3e8` |\n| sand | `#f3d9a4`, `#e2c088`; wet `#c9a06a` |\n| foliage | `#2f8f4e`, `#5fc35a` |\n| sunset | `#ff9e5e`, `#ff5f7a`, `#6a3fa0` |\n| night | `#14163a`; neon `#ff5fa2`, `#5ff0ff` |\n| gold accents | `#ffd36a` |\n\n**Light by time of day:**\n\n| Time | Light |\n| --- | --- |\n| morning | ambient .9, slightly cool |\n| afternoon | ambient 1.0, warm |\n| Day 5 afternoon | sunset tint |\n| night | ambient .38; torches, lamps, neon and floodlights as `game.lights` |\n\nLocations at night also try `game.enableGPU({ map })` (it falls back to canvas lighting by itself).\n\n**4.25.2 Characters.**\n\n**The `athletic` build:** `{ legUpper: 7.1, legLower: 7.2, hipZ: 13.9, torso: 8.9, shoulderHalf: 2.95, headR: 3.0,\nneck: 1.4, armUpper: 5.1, armLower: 4.9, hipHalf: 2.05, limbW: 1.75, torsoW: 2.7, stride: 7.4, speedRef: 80 }`.\n\n- Faces use `face: { eyes: 'big', bangs: .5 }`.\n- Arms are bare (`sleeves: 'none'`) unless the suit has sleeves. Legs are skin color. Feet are bare or in sandals.\n\n**Swimsuits** (`outfit: 'swim'`):\n\n| cut | torso | hips and thighs | arms |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `onepiece` | main color over the whole torso plate, a scoop neckline (a skin wedge at the front top), straps | a brief band (top 15% of the thigh) | bare |\n| `racer` | onepiece plus accent side panels and racer-back straps | brief | bare |\n| `halter` | onepiece with a halter strap to the neck (trim) | brief | bare |\n| `sport2` | a crop top from the shoulders to 55% of the torso; skin midriff from 55% to 88%; the bottom band from 88% | shorts to 35% of the thigh, or a brief with `brief: true` | bare |\n| `tankini` | a top to 80% of the torso | shorts to 30% of the thigh | bare |\n| `rash` | a rash guard: whole torso plus sleeves (short or long) in main, with a zip line (trim) | board shorts to 45% of the thigh, in accent | sleeves |\n| `sarong` | onepiece | a wrap skirt (the engine's tunic slab) in accent, knotted at the hip | bare |\n\n**Patterns.** Drawn per pixel inside the filled torso and shorts polygons, with 1-px features so they read on a 50-px\ncharacter.\n\n| Pattern | Look |\n| --- | --- |\n| `solid` | plain |\n| `stripes` | horizontal accent rows every 2 px |\n| `pin` | thin vertical lines |\n| `dots` | a 2-px offset grid |\n| `waves` | scallops |\n| `stars` | 3-px stars |\n| `floral` | 3-px flowers in accent and trim |\n| `palms` | leaf strokes |\n| `check` | 2-px gingham with a blended cross |\n| `gradient` | 3 bands from main to accent |\n| `geo` | zigzag |\n| `scales` | small arcs |\n| `sevens` | tiny 7s |\n| `lame` | gold sparkle dither with an animated glint |\n\n**Hair and hats:**\n\n| Style | Shape |\n| --- | --- |\n| `twinbuns` | two balls (.55 headR) on the top sides, plus short tails |\n| `bun` | one ball at the back top |\n| `braid` | a simulated chain like `long`, with alternating segment widths and a tie |\n| `bob` | a cap down to the jaw, with side bangs |\n| `puff` | a big ball (1.1 headR) at the back top, with a hairband in trim |\n| `curly` | a bob with a bumpy dithered outline |\n| `sunhat` (hat) | a wide brim ellipse with a band |\n| `visor` (hat) | a cap with no crown |\n\n**Accessories** draw through `extras` (§5.2.2 lists them).\n\n**Rig sheet.** `tools/rigsheet.mjs` renders every fighter in every suit, at 4 facings, in the court, servecam,\nthreequarter and iso views, at 2×, into `test-output/rigsheet/`. Screenshots are the check for art.\n\n**4.25.3 Environment assets.** `E.SHAPES` written per `docs/ASSETS.md` and checked with `node tools/asset-sheet.mjs`:\n\n| Group | Shapes |\n| --- | --- |\n| Beach | `umbrella` (params color, stripes: pole and an 8-segment canopy), `lounger`, `beachtowel`, `cooler`, `sandcastle`, `surfboard` (params color), `surfrack`, `lifeguard` (tower), `bleacher` (3 tiers), `scoreboard` (flip cards; params left, right), `djbooth` (speakers and a gold disc), `netpost` (with antenna), `tikibar` (thatch hut, counter, stools), `changinghut` |\n| Pool | `cabana`, `poolfloat` (round pad; params color), `flamingo` (inflatable), `pooledge` (tiled coping), `deckchair` |\n| Casino | `slotmachine` (params color), `bjtable` (half-moon felt), `roulettetable` (with the wheel bowl), `cashier` (a cage), `neonsign` (glow material), `velvetrope` |\n| Promenade | `shopfront` (facade with an awning; params color and sign), `icecreamcart`, `bench`, `planter` |\n| Villa | `bed`, `wardrobe`, `desk`, `mailbox`, `rug` |\n| Island | `seaplane`, `dockplanks`, `lighthouse` |\n\n- **Engine props:** `torch` (tiki torches, `light: true`), `lamp`, `palm`, `flowers`, `rock`, `chandelier`, `sign`.\n- **Store:** cut `kenney-pirate:palm-detailed-straight`, `kenney-pirate:boat-row-large` and `kenney-holiday:present-a-cube`\n  with `tools/asset-set.mjs`, then load them with `E.addAssets`.\n- Shop windows show posed rigs, not mannequin shapes.\n\n**Materials:** `sand` (tuned), `wetsand`, `pooltile` (tiles, aqua), sea and pool `water` with a shimmer floor tag,\n`boardwalk` (bleached planks), `felt` (green), `carpet` (casino diamonds), `gold`.\n\n**Backdrops** (`E.Backdrop`, custom per time of day): a sky gradient, the sun or moon, clouds, distant teal islands\n(`mountains` layer), the volcano's silhouette, and a `sea` layer with glints. At night: stars, the moon, and a lit\nyacht.\n\n**Effects:** sand puffs, splashes (blue bits and a ring), sparkles on PERFECT, hearts (gifts and affinity), confetti\n(wins), fireworks (the party), a coin shower (jackpot), sweat drops (Ingrid's running joke), the glare star (Sonny).\n\n**4.25.4 UI art.**\n\n- The logo.\n- Icons made with `E.sprite`: heart (full, half, empty), coin, chip, gift box, hanger (suits), sunglasses, star, mood\n  icons, weather icons, lock, NEW badge, camera.\n- Glyph icons (§4.1.2); gradient panels with borders; portraits from the rigs.\n\n### 4.26 Animation (`15-anim.js`)\n\n**Technique, in layers:**\n\n1. The rig's own procedural walk, run, idle and jump.\n2. The **arm-IK overlay:** after `rig.update`, override the hand targets with `E.ik3` for timed moves, blended by a\n   weight curve (wind 0→1, hold, release 1→0). Wrap `rig.solvePose` as AI_GUIDE's \"New animation on the rigs\" shows.\n3. Body offsets through rig state: `crouch`, `lean`, `air`, `land`, `flip`, `down`.\n4. Mocap clips through `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)`, faded with `rig.mocapW`, or upper body only with\n   `rig.mocapMask = 'upper'`.\n5. Faces through `expr`.\n\nAnimation is driven from the simulation's plan, not the other way round. A spike's jump starts at t* minus its rise time,\nand the hand's IK target is the ball's position at t*.\n\n**Moves:**\n\n| Move | Timing (s) | How |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ready stance | loop | crouch .35, hands low in front (IK), weight shifts, eyes on the ball |\n| bump | .12 wind, .08 hit, .3 recover | crouch .55 then extend; hands joined at hip height in front (IK); arms swing up 20° through contact |\n| dig (low) | as bump | crouch .8, `land: .4` |\n| set | .1, .06, .25 | hands above the forehead (IK, wrists back), knees push; a small hop for quick sets |\n| approach and spike | .38 rise, .06 hit, .3 land | 2-step approach toward the net; `air`; the right arm cocks back (IK) then whips over (the engine's `overhead` arc with `hop`); the left arm points at the ball; land squash (`rig.land(.6)`) |\n| shot (cut / roll) | as spike, slower arm | open-hand poke (IK) |\n| block | .28 rise, .18 hold, .3 fall | both arms straight up over the net (IK), hands angled forward; land |\n| float serve | .5 toss, .1 hit | the left hand tosses (IK), then the right arm hits overhead, with a step |\n| jump serve | .6 toss, .4 approach, .1 hit | high toss, 2 steps, a jump, a spike-like swing |\n| dive | .22 lunge, .3 slide, .45 down | the mocap `Dive_Roll` (CMU), or `flip` with a forward lunge; arms out; a sand trail |\n| call | .5 | free arm up, `expr: 'shout'` |\n| high five | .5 | partners turn to face each other; the near hands meet at shoulder height + 4 (IK to the midpoint); clap sound and a sparkle |\n| celebrations | 1.2 | Rin `Bow`; Lola `Victory Fist Pump`; Ingrid `Head Nod` with a small fist; Amara `Dance Charleston` or `Cartwheel`; Tess `Wave_Hello` (a shaka); Mei `Backflip`; Sonny `Cheering_Two_Hands`; Pepper `Salute` (deadpan) |\n| disappointment | 1 | `Idle_No_Loop`, `Shrug`, the facepalm pose |\n| give / receive a gift | 1 | give: both hands forward holding a gift-box sprite. Receive: love = a hop, `Cheer_One_arm` and hearts; like = `Yes` or `Head Nod`; refuse = `Reject` or `Idle_FoldArms_Loop` |\n| idles | loop | `Idle_Talking_Loop`; `Sitting_Idle_Loop` (bar stools, loungers); `Sitting_Talking_Loop`; sunbathing (`down: 1` plus the `sunbathe` pose); `Swim_Idle_Loop` and `Swim_Fwd_Loop` (pool); `Stretch_Yawn`; `Jumping_Jacks_Loop` (warm-ups); `Meditate` (Rin); `Idle_TalkingPhone_Loop` (Sonny) |\n| party | loop | `Dance_Loop`, `Dance Body Roll`, `Dance Reach Hip`, `Dance Charleston` |\n| Pool Hop | .45 a hop | crouch, an `air` arc between pads, a land squash. A slip blends `hurt` and `down` with a splash, then `Swim_Fwd_Loop` back and `ClimbUp_1m_RM` onto the pad |\n| casino | loop | sitting at slots, leaning on the table, cheering on wins |\n| photo poses | hold | Wave, Peace (IK hand by the face with a two-finger sprite), Hips, Cheer, Stretch, Look Back (torso twist and head turn), Sit, Victory, Salute, Bow |\n| Sonny gags | 1–2 | `Fall_On_Face` (tripping into the pool), `Confused`, `Angry` |\n\n**The clip set to cut.** Make it with `tools/anim-set.mjs` into `vendor/mocap/aoa-clips.js` (name `AOA`) and keep it\nunder about 250 KB. Quote the `--clips` argument, since some names have spaces.\n\n| Source set | Clips |\n| --- | --- |\n| quaternius | `Idle_Talking_Loop`, `Sitting_Enter`, `Sitting_Idle_Loop`, `Sitting_Talking_Loop`, `Sitting_Exit`, `Swim_Idle_Loop`, `Swim_Fwd_Loop`, `Dance_Loop`, `Idle_FoldArms_Loop`, `Idle_No_Loop`, `Yes`, `Idle_TalkingPhone_Loop`, `LayToIdle`, `ClimbUp_1m_RM`, `Jump_Start`, `Jump_Loop`, `Jump_Land` |\n| mesh2motion | `Bow`, `Victory`, `Victory Fist Pump`, `Cheer_One_arm`, `Cheering_Two_Hands`, `Dance Charleston`, `Dance Body Roll`, `Dance Reach Hip`, `Reject`, `Head Nod`, `Greeting`, `Salute`, `Backflip`, `Meditate`, `Confused`, `Angry` |\n| cmu | `Dive_Roll`, `Wave_Hello`, `Shrug`, `Stretch_Yawn`, `Cartwheel`, `Jumping_Jacks_Loop`, `Fall_On_Face` |\n\n**Checks.**\n\n- Check every clip on the athletic build in the rig sheet. Use `mocapMask: 'upper'` where the legs look wrong, and fall\n  back to a procedural pose for any clip that still fails.\n- Record every move with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` and look for a wind-up, a strike and a clean settle, with no jerks or\n  backward sweeps. Keep the strips in `test-output/filmstrips/`.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Content\n\n### 5.1 Cast\n","numLines":650,"startLine":1000,"totalLines":2193}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01YNraQd2oEEdYPSeG9BwVBs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
