{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LgsyxLxPkEQHViZkffDavt","type":"tool_result","content":"1649\t\n1650\t**The six fighters: look and personality.** All use the `athletic` build. Sizes are rig `size`.\n1651\t\n1652\t| id | Name, epithet | From · style · age | Look | Personality |\n1653\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1654\t| `rin` | Rin Takamine, \"The Quiet Blade\" | Japan · kendo and iaido champion · 24 | 1.22; long blue-black high ponytail `#1d1a24`, bangs .6; skin `#f1cfb2`; eyes `#4a2c22` | composed perfectionist, dry one-liners; secretly adores cute things |\n1655\t| `lola` | Dolores \"Lola\" Vega, \"La Tormenta\" | Mexico · luchadora (pro wrestler) · 27 | 1.30, shoulderHalf +.25; curly dark brown `#3a2218` with a red bandana (`band` `#d8302a`); skin `#b9825a`; eyes `#3a2416` | loud, warm, theatrical; trash-talks with a grin; lives for a crowd |\n1656\t| `ingrid` | Ingrid Halvorsen, \"The Glacier\" | Norway · glíma wrestling and kickboxing, ex-biathlete · 26 | 1.38, the tallest; platinum braid `#f2ead2`; skin `#f7dccb`; eyes `#5aa0d8` | stoic and deadpan; hates the heat and misses snow; secretly a karaoke fiend |\n1657\t| `amara` | Amara Okafor, \"Rhythm Queen\" | UK/Nigeria · capoeira and dance fighting · 22 | 1.26; high puff `#2a1810` with gold cuffs; skin `#7a4a2e`; eyes `#2a1810` | cheerful social butterfly who loves music and fashion; dramatic |\n1658\t| `tess` | Tess Callahan, \"Riptide\" | Australia · surfer and MMA brawler · 25 | 1.28; sun-bleached messy bob `#f0d890`; skin `#e2ad84`; eyes `#3c7a5a` | laid-back but fiercely competitive; cheeky and outdoorsy |\n1659\t| `mei` | Mei-Lin Zhou, \"Little Phoenix\" | Hong Kong · wushu acrobat and xiangqi prodigy · 21 | 1.16, the smallest; black twin buns `#1a1418` with pink ribbons; skin `#f3d2b8`; eyes `#3a2420` | mischievous prankster with a sweet tooth; hates losing at anything |\n1660\t\n1661\t**The six fighters: play and voice.** Stats are 1–10. Voice values are base Hz, range in semitones, rate in letters/s,\n1662\tformant shift and wave (§4.24.3).\n1663\t\n1664\t| id | Tastes | POW / TEC / SPD / JMP | Voice | Signature suit | Starts with | Celebration |\n1665\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1666\t| `rin` | classic, elegant | 5 / 9 / 7 / 6 | 330, 3, 13, 1.05, triangle | Seigaiha | Ribbon (red) | `Bow` |\n1667\t| `lola` | bold, sporty | 9 / 5 / 5 / 8 | 260, 6, 16, .95, saw | Estrella | Sweatband | `Victory Fist Pump` |\n1668\t| `ingrid` | sporty, classic | 7 / 6 / 4 / 9 | 210, 2, 10, .9, triangle | Fjord | Sport Shades | `Head Nod` and a small fist |\n1669\t| `amara` | bold, cute | 5 / 6 / 9 / 8 | 340, 7, 15, 1.1, pulse; sing-song contour | Kente Pop | Hibiscus | `Dance Charleston` or `Cartwheel` |\n1670\t| `tess` | sporty, bold | 7 / 7 / 7 / 6 | 290, 5, 14, 1.0, saw; statements end rising | Reef Break | Wristbands | `Wave_Hello` (a shaka) |\n1671\t| `mei` | cute, elegant | 4 / 8 / 8 / 6 | 400, 6, 18, 1.18, pulse | Peony | Ribbon (pink) | `Backflip` |\n1672\t\n1673\t**Hosts and staff:**\n1674\t\n1675\t| id | Who | Look | Voice | Role |\n1676\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1677\t| `sonny` | Sonny Fortuna, \"The Man with the Golden Tan\": jackpot billionaire, DJ and would-be champion; a harmless buffoon | `bulky` 1.32; slick black hair (`spiky` `#121014`); gold aviators; a loud palm-print shirt (`shirt`, pattern `palms`, `#2fb5a0` / `#ffd36a`); white shorts; gold chain; skin `#d9a27a`. Final kit: black-and-gold tank and board shorts | 120, 7, 13, .8, saw, vibrato 6 Hz | host, PA commentator, casino boss, final opponent (POW 8 / TEC 5 / SPD 5 / JMP 5) |\n1678\t| `pepper` | Pepper Quill: concierge, scorekeeper and dealer; deadpan, ultra-competent, quietly holds Sonny's debts | `athletic` 1.24; auburn `bun` `#5a2a1e`; thin glasses; navy vest `#1d2433` with gold trim, slacks. Final kit: the Pinstripe racer | 230, 1, 17, 1.0, triangle | concierge, tutorial coach, blackjack dealer, final opponent (POW 6 / TEC 10 / SPD 7 / JMP 6) |\n1679\t| `kai` | Kai Makoa, an islander: bartender and croupier | `heroic` 1.25; short black hair; skin `#a8714a`; floral shirt (`#2fb5a0`), khaki shorts | 170, 4, 12, .85, triangle | Tiki Tok Bar, Sundries & Smiles, roulette |\n1680\t| `odette` | Odette Belrose, couturier | `athletic` 1.2; long silver-lilac hair `#c8b8e8`; pink sundress (`robe`, `#ff8aa8`); sun hat | 300, 5, 12, 1.1, pulse | Coral Couture |\n1681\t| `bo` | Coach Bo Brannigan, a retired beach pro | `bulky` 1.28; bald; visor; whistle; yellow tank `#ffd04a`, blue shorts | 150, 3, 14, .85, square | Riptide Sports |\n1682\t| crowd | staff and guests | small pixel sprites, plus a few HD rigs at .9 | — | spectators, casino crowd |\n1683\t\n1684\t### 5.2 Items\n1685\t\n1686\t**5.2.1 Swimsuits (21).** Colors are main · accent · trim. \"Day N+\" items reach the shop on that day.\n1687\t\n1688\t| id | Name | Cut | Pattern | Colors | Tastes | Where | S$ |\n1689\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1690\t| `seigaiha` | Seigaiha | onepiece | waves | `#23306b` `#e8eef8` `#c8303a` | classic, elegant | Rin's signature | — |\n1691\t| `estrella` | Estrella | sport2, shorts | stars | `#c8202c` `#ffd04a` `#1a1a1a` | bold, sporty | Lola's signature | — |\n1692\t| `fjord` | Fjord | rash, short sleeves | solid | `#9fd8f0` `#1d3560` `#ffffff` | sporty, classic | Ingrid's signature | — |\n1693\t| `kentepop` | Kente Pop | tankini | geo | `#ff8a1e` `#2f9e4a` `#ffd36a` | bold, cute | Amara's signature | — |\n1694\t| `reefbreak` | Reef Break | racer | gradient | `#1fb7b0` `#ff7a5e` `#ffffff` | sporty, bold | Tess's signature | — |\n1695\t| `peony` | Peony | halter | floral | `#ffb2a0` `#e85a8a` `#ffffff` | cute, elegant | Mei's signature | — |\n1696\t| `protour` | Pro Tour | racer | pin | `#f4f6fa` `#d8283a` `#1a2a5a` | sporty | Riptide | 12,000 |\n1697\t| `sandstorm` | Sandstorm | sport2, shorts | solid | `#e8c06a` `#1a1a1a` `#ffffff` | sporty, bold | Riptide | 9,000 |\n1698\t| `lifeguard` | Lifeguard | onepiece | solid | `#e0302a` `#ffd04a` `#ffffff` | sporty, classic | Riptide | 8,000 |\n1699\t| `coralrash` | Coral Rash | rash, long sleeves | stripes | `#ff7a5e` `#ffffff` `#2a3a5a` | sporty | Riptide | 14,000 |\n1700\t| `neonrush` | Neon Rush | tankini | gradient | `#7cff5a` `#ff4fb8` `#1a1a1a` | bold, sporty | Riptide, Day 2+ | 16,000 |\n1701\t| `monaco` | Monaco | halter | stripes | `#1d2f6a` `#ffffff` `#d8283a` | classic, elegant | Coral Couture | 22,000 |\n1702\t| `polkapop` | Polka Pop | sport2, brief | dots | `#e8283a` `#ffffff` `#ffd04a` | cute | Coral Couture | 18,000 |\n1703\t| `tropicana` | Tropicana | sarong | palms | `#2f8f4e` `#ffe0a0` `#ff8a1e` | elegant | Coral Couture | 26,000 |\n1704\t| `mermaid` | Mermaid | onepiece | scales | `#1fb7b0` `#7a5fd8` `#e8f8ff` | cute, elegant | Coral Couture, Day 3+ | 30,000 |\n1705\t| `sunsetblvd` | Sunset Boulevard | tankini | gradient | `#ff9e5e` `#7a3fa0` `#ffd36a` | bold, elegant | Coral Couture | 28,000 |\n1706\t| `midnight` | Midnight | onepiece | solid | `#16141c` `#ffd36a` `#ffd36a` | elegant, bold | Coral Couture, Day 4+ | 35,000 |\n1707\t| `gingham` | Gingham Picnic | tankini | check | `#6aa8e8` `#ffffff` `#e8283a` | cute, classic | Coral Couture | 15,000 |\n1708\t| `fortunagold` | Fortuna Gold | racer | lame | `#ffd36a` `#fff3c0` `#1a1a1a` | bold | win the Final | — |\n1709\t| `jackpot` | Jackpot | sport2, shorts | sevens | `#1a1a2a` `#ffd36a` `#e8283a` | bold, cute | casino prize counter | 300 chips |\n1710\t| `pinstripe` | Pepper's Pinstripe | racer | pin | `#121216` `#f4f4f4` `#ffd36a` | classic, elegant | Pepper's gift on Day 4 (see §5.5) | — |\n1711\t\n1712\t**5.2.2 Accessories (10).** One per anchor: head, face, hair, neck, wrists.\n1713\t\n1714\t| id | Name | Anchor | Look | Tastes | Where | S$ |\n1715\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1716\t| `ribbon` | Ribbon | hair | a bow in the wearer's accent color | classic, cute | Rin and Mei start with it; Coral Couture | 2,000 |\n1717\t| `sweatband` | Sweatband | head (`band`) | terry band | sporty | Riptide; Lola starts with it | 3,000 |\n1718\t| `sportshades` | Sport Shades | face | wraparound lenses `#20262e`, frame `#e8eef2`; **sunglasses** | sporty | Riptide; Ingrid starts with them | 6,000 |\n1719\t| `heartshades` | Heart Shades | face | two pink hearts; **sunglasses** | cute, bold | Coral Couture | 7,500 |\n1720\t| `aviators` | Gold Aviators | face | like Sonny's; **sunglasses** | bold | Coral Couture, Day 3+ | 15,000 |\n1721\t| `visor` | Sun Visor | head (`visor`) | white with a colored brim | sporty | Riptide | 4,000 |\n1722\t| `sunhat` | Straw Sun Hat | head (`sunhat`) | wide straw brim, ribbon band | elegant, classic | Coral Couture | 9,000 |\n1723\t| `hibiscus` | Hibiscus | hair | a red flower behind the ear | cute, elegant | Sundries; Amara starts with it | 2,500 |\n1724\t| `shellnecklace` | Shell Necklace | neck | white shell dots | cute, classic | Sundries | 4,500 |\n1725\t| `wristbands` | Wristbands | wrists | 2-px bands | sporty | Riptide; Tess starts with them | 3,500 |\n1726\t\n1727\t**5.2.3 Gifts (25).** Stock and daily deals work as for every shop item (§4.12). Icons are `E.shapeSprite` of a store\n1728\tshape where one exists (`kenney-food:coconut`, `kenney-food:ice-cream`, `kenney-holiday:present-a-cube` for the\n1729\twrapping), otherwise a 12×12 `E.sprite`.\n1730\t\n1731\t| Category | Items (S$) | Shop |\n1732\t| --- | --- | --- |\n1733\t| food and drink | `mango_smoothie` Mango Smoothie 800 · `bubble_tea` Bubble Tea 900 · `matcha_icecream` Matcha Ice Cream 700 · `mochi_box` Mochi Box 1,500 · `bbq_skewers` BBQ Skewers 1,200 · `hot_sauce` Hot Sauce Sampler 2,000 · `iced_coffee` Iced Coffee 600 · `coconut` Fresh Coconut 400 | Sundries & Smiles |\n1734\t| goods | `plush_seal` Plush Seal 3,000 · `snow_globe` Snow Globe 2,500 · `puzzle_cube` Puzzle Cube 2,200 · `portable_speaker` Portable Speaker 9,000 · `matcha_kit` Matcha Kit 4,500 · `calligraphy_set` Calligraphy Set 6,000 · `knitting_kit` Knitting Kit 2,800 · `maracas` Maracas 1,400 · `luchador_mask` Luchador Mask 5,000 (Day 2+) | Sundries & Smiles |\n1735\t| books | `beach_paperback` Beach Paperback 1,200 · `fashion_mag` Fashion Magazine 800 | Sundries & Smiles |\n1736\t| sports | `energy_drink` Energy Drink 500 · `surf_wax` Surf Wax Deluxe 1,600 · `sunscreen` Sunscreen SPF 100 1,000 · `foam_finger` Foam Finger 900 | Riptide Sports |\n1737\t| fashion | `glitter_sandals` Glitter Sandals 5,500 · `gold_hoops` Gold Hoop Earrings 12,000 | Coral Couture |\n1738\t\n1739\t### 5.3 Tastes and starting affinity\n1740\t\n1741\t**Gift tastes.** L = love (+3), + = like (+2), · = neutral, − = dislike (−3). Each fighter has 2 loves, at least 3 likes\n1742\tand at least 3 dislikes; the data test checks it.\n1743\t\n1744\t| Gift | Rin | Lola | Ingrid | Amara | Tess | Mei |\n1745\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1746\t| mango_smoothie | · | + | · | + | + | · |\n1747\t| bubble_tea | · | · | · | · | · | + |\n1748\t| matcha_icecream | + | · | + | · | · | + |\n1749\t| mochi_box | + | · | · | · | · | L |\n1750\t| bbq_skewers | · | + | · | · | L | − |\n1751\t| hot_sauce | − | L | − | · | + | − |\n1752\t| iced_coffee | · | · | + | · | · | · |\n1753\t| coconut | · | · | · | · | + | · |\n1754\t| plush_seal | L | · | + | · | · | + |\n1755\t| snow_globe | · | · | L | − | · | · |\n1756\t| puzzle_cube | + | − | · | · | · | L |\n1757\t| portable_speaker | − | + | · | L | + | · |\n1758\t| matcha_kit | L | − | · | · | · | + |\n1759\t| calligraphy_set | + | · | · | · | − | · |\n1760\t| knitting_kit | · | · | L | − | · | − |\n1761\t| maracas | · | + | · | + | · | · |\n1762\t| luchador_mask | · | L | · | · | + | · |\n1763\t| beach_paperback | + | − | + | · | · | · |\n1764\t| fashion_mag | · | · | − | + | − | + |\n1765\t| energy_drink | − | · | · | − | + | − |\n1766\t| surf_wax | · | · | · | · | L | · |\n1767\t| sunscreen | · | · | + | · | + | · |\n1768\t| foam_finger | − | + | · | · | + | · |\n1769\t| glitter_sandals | · | · | − | + | − | + |\n1770\t| gold_hoops | · | + | · | L | · | · |\n1771\t\n1772\t**Weather tastes** (for mood):\n1773\t\n1774\t| Fighter | Likes | Dislikes |\n1775\t| --- | --- | --- |\n1776\t| Ingrid | cloudy, rain | — |\n1777\t| Amara | sunny | rain |\n1778\t| Tess | sunny | — |\n1779\t| others | neutral | neutral |\n1780\t\n1781\t**Starting affinity.** One symmetric value per pair. It is also used to pair NPCs into teams.\n1782\t\n1783\t| | Rin | Lola | Ingrid | Amara | Tess | Mei |\n1784\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1785\t| **Rin** | — | 20 | 35 | 25 | 30 | 40 |\n1786\t| **Lola** | 20 | — | 25 | 40 | 45 | 20 |\n1787\t| **Ingrid** | 35 | 25 | — | 20 | 35 | 25 |\n1788\t| **Amara** | 25 | 40 | 20 | — | 30 | 40 |\n1789\t| **Tess** | 30 | 45 | 35 | 30 | — | 25 |\n1790\t| **Mei** | 40 | 20 | 25 | 40 | 25 | — |\n1791\t\n1792\tEvery fighter except Ingrid starts with someone at 40 or more, who is willing to team up at once. Ingrid (\"The\n1793\tGlacier\") has to earn a partner; Pepper's tutorial gives everyone a starter partner anyway: the highest-affinity NPC.\n1794\t\n1795\t### 5.4 Locations and schedules\n1796\t\n1797\t**Locations.**\n1798\t\n1799\t| Location | Open | Map (tiles) | Features | NPC spots |\n1800\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1801\t| **Sunset Courts** | Morning, Afternoon (final and party override) | the 44×28 court map (§4.3) | Court A, bleachers, Tiki Tok Bar (Kai), umbrellas and loungers, lifeguard tower, DJ booth (Sonny in the mornings), surf rack, sandcastle, changing hut, Match Board | 3 bar stools, 3 loungers, 2 on the shoreline, 1 practice pair bumping a ball |\n1802\t| **Lagoon Pool** | Morning, Afternoon | 30×22 | a free-form pool, the Pool Hop deck and 32 pads, cabana bar, loungers, flamingo float, palms, tiki torches, changing hut | 2 swimming, 3 loungers, 2 sitting on the pool edge, 2 cabana stools |\n1803\t| **Fortuna Promenade** | Morning, Afternoon | 36×16 boardwalk | 3 shopfronts with doors, ice-cream cart, benches, lamps, planters, the railing over the sea | 2 benches, 3 window-shopping, 1 at the ice-cream cart |\n1804\t| **Your Villa** | always | 14×10 interior plus a balcony | bed (Rest / Sleep), closet (Wardrobe), desk (Journal: Save, Friends, Stats), album frame, mailbox (letters), a balcony view by time of day | 1 visitor spot (night events) |\n1805\t| **Casino Fortuna** | Night | 30×20 | cashier, 6 slots, blackjack (Pepper), roulette (Kai), VIP lounge (Sonny), prize counter, chandeliers, neon | 3 at slots, 2 at the roulette rail, 2 at the bar |\n1806\t| **Dock** | story only | 24×14 | seaplane, planks, crates, flags | the arrival lineup |\n1807\t\n1808\t**Schedule weights.** Daytime columns are Beach / Pool / Promenade / away; night is Casino / away.\n1809\t\n1810\t| NPC | Morning | Afternoon | Night |\n1811\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1812\t| Rin | 4 / 2 / 3 / 1 | 4 / 3 / 2 / 1 | 3 / 7 |\n1813\t| Lola | 5 / 2 / 2 / 1 | 5 / 2 / 2 / 1 | 6 / 4 |\n1814\t| Ingrid | 3 / 4 / 2 / 1 | 2 / 5 / 2 / 1 | 2 / 8 |\n1815\t| Amara | 3 / 2 / 4 / 1 | 3 / 3 / 3 / 1 | 7 / 3 |\n1816\t| Tess | 6 / 2 / 1 / 1 | 5 / 3 / 1 / 1 | 4 / 6 |\n1817\t| Mei | 2 / 3 / 4 / 1 | 3 / 2 / 4 / 1 | 8 / 2 |\n1818\t\n1819\t- **Rain** multiplies Beach × .2, Pool × .5, Promenade × 1.5 (it's covered) and away × 1.5.\n1820\t- **NPC teams** are formed at day start. Of the NPCs who aren't your partner, choose the pairing with the largest sum of\n1821\t  pair affinities plus ±10 noise from the `world` rng, preferring not to repeat yesterday's pairs. With 5 free NPCs, one\n1822\t  stays solo and can be invited.\n1823\t\n1824\t**Mailbox letters** (a simple letter screen with a portrait):\n1825\t\n1826\t| When | Letter |\n1827\t| --- | --- |\n1828\t| D1 night | Pepper's welcome (the rules again) |\n1829\t| D2 morning | Sonny's flyer: \"Free chips for champions!\" |\n1830\t| D3 morning | a note from your highest-affinity friend |\n1831\t| D4 morning | Pepper's warning |\n1832\t| D5 morning | Sonny's \"FINAL HYPE\" poster |\n1833\t\n1834\t### 5.5 Story beats and events\n1835\t\n1836\tData lives in `05-data-text.js`; triggers live in `30-vacation.js`.\n1837\t\n1838\t| When | Event | What happens | Effects |\n1839\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1840\t| New Vacation | **The Invitation** | The letter on parchment with Sonny's gold seal; \"Who opened it?\" leads to character select (6 cards with portraits, epithets, style, stats as bars, tastes) | — |\n1841\t| D1 Morning | **Arrival** (Dock) | The seaplane lands and your fighter steps off; the other five are already there, each with one line. Sonny's grand welcome reveals the \"tournament\" is volleyball and a vacation. Pepper hands out keys and explains the slots, Sonny Dollars and the Cup in five days. | flags |\n1842\t| D1 Morning | **Welcome Match** (the tutorial) | \"Allow me to demonstrate!\" You and your starter partner (Pepper assigns the highest-affinity NPC) play Sonny & Pepper (\"five percent effort\"), first to 5, with Pepper's coaching (§5.5.1). Sonny loses comically and falls on his face. | partner set; S$10,000 |\n1843\t| D1 Night | Casino opening | If you go: Sonny gives 20 free chips and explains the games | chips |\n1844\t| D2 Night | Villa visit | If you rest in the villa and someone has affinity ≥ 50, she knocks with a snack: a 3-line chat with one choice (±4) | affinity |\n1845\t| D3 Afternoon | Rain shower | Sonny on the PA: \"LIQUID SUNSHINE, PEOPLE!\"; a rain match (wet ball: pass scatter × 1.2) | — |\n1846\t| D3 Night | **The Overheard Call** | At the casino: Sonny on the phone in the VIP lounge, \"…Yeah, I put the island on the Cup. What could go wrong?\" Pepper sees you hear it. Choice: \"Your secret's safe\" (kind) or \"Everyone's going to hear about this\" (cheeky). If you're not at the casino, you get a rumor letter instead. | flag `kind` |\n1847\t| D4 Morning | **Pepper's Letter** | \"The Final is tomorrow. Mr. Fortuna's serve is… dazzling. Eyewear is advised. — P.\" If you were kind on Day 3 and visited the casino at least once, it comes with the Pinstripe suit. | hint, suit |\n1848\t| D4 Afternoon | **Semifinal** | The NPC pair with the best record challenges you; it's marked SEMIFINAL on the Match Board. Win: seeded (you serve first in the Final), S$30,000. Lose: unseeded. | flags |\n1849\t| D5 Afternoon | **THE FORTUNA CUP FINAL** | The beach in banners, a bigger crowd; Sonny & Pepper in match gear as \"THE HOUSE\"; first to 11; the specials of §4.8.6 | win: S$100,000, Fortuna Gold |\n1850\t| D5 Night | **Farewell Party** | The beach at night: torches, fireworks, everyone dancing. Each fighter says goodbye with a line for her affinity stage. A group postcard is taken automatically. | album |\n1851\t| Ending A (Final won) | **The House Folds** | Sonny must hand over the island, but Pepper produces his IOUs: she owns it now. Sonny paddles off on the flamingo float: \"I'LL BE BACK… NEXT SUMMER!\" Pepper: \"Breakfast is at eight. The island is under new management.\" | — |\n1852\t| Ending B (Final lost) | **The House Always Wins** | Sonny gloats, then bets the island on one spin of a giant roulette wheel at the party \"to make it interesting\". Pepper calls red. It lands red. Same flamingo exit. Pepper: \"The house always wins. I am the house.\" | — |\n1853\t| After either | Credits | The postcard slideshow plus the party photo, with credits | — |\n1854\t| Then | **Vacation Results** | A report card: money earned, W–L, best friend (portrait), suits collected x/21, gifts given, best Pool Hop, casino net, postcards. A title: \"Island Icon\" (won the final and 3 Best Friends), \"Fortuna Champion\" (won the final), \"Social Butterfly\" (3+ Good Friends), otherwise \"Beach Bum\". Unlocks New Vacation+ and every suit for Beach Match. | unlocks |\n1855\t\n1856\t**5.5.1 The tutorial script** (Welcome Match, first to 5). Pepper's tips are non-modal callouts (Shell tutorial cards or a\n1857\tUI-kit panel) shown at the right moment, with the current device's glyphs:\n1858\t\n1859\t1. **Receive:** \"The ring shows where the ball comes down. Stand in it. Press ✕ as the ball reaches you.\"\n1860\t   (Auto-receive covers the first 2 receives if you miss.)\n1861\t2. **Set:** \"Your partner passed it to you. ✕ again as it drops, to set her up.\"\n1862\t3. **Spike:** \"She set you. You'll jump on your own. ✕ at the top. Push the stick, or point the mouse, to aim.\"\n1863\t4. **Serve:** \"✕ to toss, ✕ again at the top of the toss. □ tosses for a jump serve.\"\n1864\t5. **Block:** \"When they spike near the net, □ to block.\"\n1865\t6. **Dive:** \"Out of reach? ○ dives.\"\n1866\t7. **Call:** \"△ calls 'Mine!' or 'Yours!'. Your partner listens.\"\n1867\t8. **Chemistry:** \"The better you two get along, the better she plays. Chat. Bring gifts. Win.\"\n1868\t\n1869\tNew Vacation+ offers \"Skip the Welcome Match\".\n1870\t\n1871\t### 5.6 Opponents and difficulty\n1872\t\n1873\t**Day skill base** (before stats, difficulty and `T.aiSkillMul`):\n1874\t\n1875\t| Match | Base |\n1876\t| --- | --- |\n1877\t| tutorial | Sonny .20, Pepper .35 (Pepper never hits hard) |\n1878\t| Day 1 | .40 |\n1879\t| Day 2 | .50 |\n1880\t| Day 3 | .58 |\n1881\t| Day 4 | .66 |\n1882\t| Day 4 semifinal | .74 |\n1883\t| Final | Sonny .70, Pepper .85, plus the specials |\n1884\t\n1885\t- The Match Board lists the pairs present, each with stars (skill) and its record.\n1886\t- Off-screen NPC results (§4.10) decide which pair has the best record, and so who plays the semifinal.\n1887\t\n1888\t### 5.7 Writing\n1889\t\n1890\t**Style.**\n1891\t\n1892\t- Short: at most 2 lines of about 36 characters per page.\n1893\t- Upbeat and a little cheesy; each fighter's voice stays consistent.\n1894\t- **Sonny** speaks in ALL-CAPS bursts, with nicknames (\"CHAMP\", \"SUNSHINE\") and casino metaphors.\n1895\t- **Pepper** is dry, exact and faintly sarcastic, and never uses an exclamation mark.\n1896\t- Jokes come from fighting backgrounds and vacation mishaps. **No innuendo.**\n1897\t\n1898\t**How many lines** (the data test checks the counts):\n1899\t\n1900\t| Speaker | Lines needed |\n1901\t| --- | --- |\n1902\t| each fighter | greet ×3 (by stage); chat ×6 (2 each for affinity 0–39, 40–79, 80+); gift love ×2, like ×2, neutral ×1, refuse ×2; suit accepted ×1, suit refused ×1; invite accept ×2, decline ×2; leaving her old team ×1; pre-match taunt ×2; match win ×2, loss ×2; partner barks ×2; villa visit ×1 (with a choice); party farewell ×2 (low, high); ending ×1 |\n1903\t| Sonny | about 40 PA and commentary lines, plus story |\n1904\t| Pepper | about 25 (tutorial tips, quips, letters) |\n1905\t| Kai, Odette, Bo | about 8 each (shop quips) |\n1906\t\n1907\t**Sample lines.** They set the tone; reuse them.\n1908\t\n1909\t| Speaker | Line |\n1910\t| --- | --- |\n1911\t| Sonny, arrival | \"WELCOME, FIGHTERS, TO ISLA FORTUNA! The tournament of the century is… drumroll… BEACH VOLLEYBALL!\" / \"And a VACATION! You're welcome!\" |\n1912\t| Pepper, arrival | \"Villa keys. Sunscreen is in the minibar. The Cup is in five days. Mr. Fortuna is not taking questions.\" / \"Please don't feed him.\" |\n1913\t| Rin | greet: \"Good morning. The sand is… adequate.\" · chat: \"I practice my swing at dawn. The sea doesn't judge.\" · love (plush seal): \"…It's so round. I will name him Admiral.\" · refuse (energy drink): \"My heart rate is fine as it is. Thank you.\" |\n1914\t| Lola | greet: \"¡Hola, compañera! Ready to bring the THUNDER?\" · love (hot sauce): \"THIS! This is the fuel of champions!\" · refuse (paperback): \"A book? On vacation? Ay, you're funny.\" |\n1915\t| Ingrid | greet: \"It is thirty-one degrees. I am melting. Hello.\" · love (snow globe): \"Snow. Tiny, perfect snow. I may cry.\" · refuse (sandals): \"Glitter gets everywhere. Everywhere.\" |\n1916\t| Amara | greet: \"Hey hey! You hear that? The ocean's got rhythm!\" · love (speaker): \"Okay. The party starts NOW.\" · refuse (snow globe): \"Snow? Babe, we're in paradise.\" |\n1917\t| Tess | greet: \"G'day! Waves are pumping, sun's out. Life's good, yeah?\" · love (surf wax): \"Ohhh, the good stuff! My board says thanks.\" · refuse (calligraphy): \"Mate, I can barely write my own name.\" |\n1918\t| Mei | greet: \"Hehe. Bet you can't beat me at anything today.\" · love (puzzle cube): \"Solved it. Twice. Got another?\" · refuse (skewers): \"I don't eat things on sticks that used to have faces.\" |\n1919\t| Invites | Tess, accepting: \"Partners? Too right!\" · Ingrid, declining: \"I prefer to know someone before I trust them with my spikes.\" |\n1920\t| Results | Lola wins: \"¡VICTORIA! Somebody ring the bell!\" · Rin loses: \"I will reflect on this. Deeply.\" |\n1921\t| Sonny, commentary | \"WHAT A SPIKE! Somebody call a lifeguard!\" · \"ACE! That serve had TAXES on it!\" · \"BLOCKED! The wall is CLOSED for business!\" · \"Long rally, folks. I'm getting a tan just WATCHING.\" · \"MATCH POINT! I can't look! …I'm looking.\" |\n1922\t| Pepper, in the final | \"Statistically, that was unwise.\" · \"The house has noticed.\" |\n1923\t\n1924\t---\n1925\t\n1926\t## 6. UI/UX and controls\n1927\t\n1928\t### 6.1 Screen flow\n1929\t\n1930\t```\n1931\tboot → title ──(10 s idle)──► attract ──(any input)──► title\n1932\ttitle → menu ─ New Vacation → invitation → character select → arrival → Welcome Match → map\n1933\t             ─ Continue / Load → map (at the saved slot)\n1934\t             ─ Beach Match → setup and join (1–4) → match → results → setup / title\n1935\t             ─ Album · How to Play · Settings (engine) · About & Credits\n1936\tmap ⇄ location (Beach / Pool / Promenade / Villa)\n1937\t      inside: talk · gift · team up · challenge → match; shops · wardrobe · journal · album · letters · Pool Hop\n1938\tmap (night) → casino (cashier / slots / blackjack / roulette) or villa → day end → map (next day)\n1939\tDay 5: Final → party → ending A or B → credits → vacation results → title\n1940\tAI Hub session: boot → hub card → match → end overlay (no title, no menus)\n1941\tPause (gameplay scenes): Resume · How to Play · Take a Postcard · Dev Mode · Settings · Controls · Full screen · Quit to title\n1942\t```\n1943\t\n1944\t### 6.2 Controls\n1945\t\n1946\t**Matches:**\n1947\t\n1948\t| Action | DualSense | Xbox | Keyboard | Mouse |\n1949\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1950\t| Move | L stick, d-pad | L stick, d-pad | WASD, arrows | — |\n1951\t| Bump · set · spike · serve (timed) | ✕ | A | Space, J | Left |\n1952\t| Shot / tip · block · jump serve · free ball | □ | X | E, K | Right |\n1953\t| Dive | ○ | B | Shift, L | — |\n1954\t| Call Mine / Yours / Auto | △ | Y | Q, I | Middle |\n1955\t| Aim | L stick at contact | L stick | WASD at contact | the cursor on their court |\n1956\t| Camera | R3 | RS click | V | — |\n1957\t| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc, P | — |\n1958\t\n1959\t**Everywhere else:**\n1960\t\n1961\t| Context | Controls |\n1962\t| --- | --- |\n1963\t| Exploration | Move: stick / WASD · Run: hold ○ or R2 / Shift · Interact: ✕ / E, Space, Enter / click a person or thing · Gift bag: □ / G · Island map: △ / M, Tab · Postcard: Create / C · Pause: Options / Esc |\n1964\t| Menus | Navigate: d-pad, stick / arrows, WASD / hover · Select: ✕ / Enter, Space / click · Back: ○ / Backspace / right click · Tabs: L1, R1 / Q, E / wheel · Option: □ / F · Special: △ / R |\n1965\t| Pool Hop | the four face buttons ✕ ○ □ △ (A B X Y; J, L, K, I or Space, Shift, E, Q); two at once on double pads |\n1966\t| Casino | the on-screen prompts (§4.16), plus blackjack H, S, D, P and slot stops J, K, L |\n1967\t| Beach Match, split keyboard | P1: WASD with F hit, G dive, H shot, R call · P2: arrows with `.` hit, `/` dive, `,` shot, L call |\n1968\t\n1969\t### 6.3 Prompt rules\n1970\t\n1971\t- Every screen has the bottom prompt bar. During a rally, at most 3 context prompts.\n1972\t- Glyphs follow the last device at once, per player.\n1973\t- PlayStation symbols are the default for any controller; Settings → Button symbols switches to Xbox (A B X Y).\n1974\t- Keyboard prompts show keycaps and mouse prompts show the mouse icon. Never show controller glyphs to a keyboard\n1975\t  player, or keys to a pad player.\n1976\t\n1977\t---\n1978\t\n1979\t## 7. Build order and milestones\n1980\t\n1981\t**Every milestone ends with:**\n1982\t\n1983\t- `npm test` green;\n1984\t- a fresh build of `GAME.html` that runs from `file://` with no console errors;\n1985\t- its screenshots reviewed.\n1986\t\n1987\tGrey-box art may appear inside a milestone only if that same milestone replaces it. Nothing shipped carries placeholder\n1988\tart, text or TODOs.\n1989\t\n1990\t| # | Milestone | Build | Tests and acceptance |\n1991\t| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n1992\t| **M0** | Foundation | Fetch the sources (§3.1), copy the engine and tools, `npm install`, `npx playwright install chromium`. `tools/build.mjs`; the `test/run.mjs` skeleton and vm loader (§9.1). `00-core`, `01-tuning`, `10-input` (action maps, glyph icons, prompt bar, touch-only gate), `11-ui` (Panel, Button, List, PromptBar, Slider), `99-main`, and real boot, title and menu scenes. Engine patches 1, 2, 6, 7. | rng reproducibility; glyph per device (PS ✕ / Xbox A / keycap); UI focus by taps and by `input.feed('move')` hover; title → menu. **Accept:** GAME.html shows the title with ✕ on a pad and keycaps on a keyboard; Settings shows Button symbols. |\n1993\t| **M1** | Volleyball core (the most important) | `20-ball`, `21-rules`, `22-players`, `23-ai`, `24-match` (phases, Broadcast camera, basic HUD); the court map with sand, lines and net; human controls with the judge and ring; AI vs AI; 1P with an AI partner vs AI. **Dev panel v1** with the Ball, Timing, Players and AI sliders and Reset, because tuning needs it now. | ball, rules, judge, ai and match suites (§9.3). **Accept:** a full 1P match to 7 is fun with the default numbers; filmstrips of the ring and of a rally look right. |\n1994\t| **M2** | Characters and court art | Engine patch 5 (athletic build, swim cuts and patterns, hair, hats, extras, poses, bare feet); `13-rigs`; `15-anim` (every volleyball move, IK overlay, high-fives, celebrations); cut the mocap set and wire it; `14-world-art` (court surroundings, backdrops for day, sunset and night, bleachers and crowd, net art, DJ booth, scoreboard); the Serve Cam view; `tools/rigsheet.mjs`. | every suit, hair and accessory builds a rig and draws without errors (browser suite); rig sheet and filmstrips reviewed. **Accept:** match screenshots meet the Look target in both cameras; no character in default colors. |\n1995\t| **M3** | Presentation, audio, exhibition, local multiplayer | `12-audio` (patches 3 and 4, SFX, voices, the `spike` and `sunrise` songs, jingles); commentary; judgement popups; celebrations; replay; results; `52-exhibition` with 1–4 joins and per-player prompts; final title and menu art and music. | 4 local players (`addPlayer` pads plus the keyboard halves) each control one fighter; songs parse with no unknown tokens; voices are no-ops headless and play in the browser. **Accept:** a Beach Match end to end with 2 keyboard halves and 2 pads. |\n1996\t| **M4** | Vacation core | `30-vacation` (state, calendar, weather, schedules, moods, affinity, partners, money, saves); `31-map`; `32-location` (Beach, Pool, Promenade, Villa with real maps, props and NPC spots); talk menu, gifts, team-up, Match Board challenges, day end; `34-story` wiring with the invitation, character select, arrival, Welcome Match and its coaching. | vacation suite; New Vacation → tutorial → map; save and load in the middle of a day. **Accept:** Days 1–2 fully playable. |\n1997\t| **M5** | Shops, wardrobe, journal, postcards | `33-shop` (3 shops, deals, try-on), wardrobe and partner page, suit gifts to NPCs, the Journal (Friends with known likes, Stats, Save), letters, `42-photo` (photo mode, album, title backdrop, PNG export). | shop suite; photo specs saved, restored and re-rendered (browser); album replace and delete. |\n1998\t| **M6** | Minigames | `40-poolhop` (song `lagoon`, judging on the music clock, wobble and double pads); `41-casino` (floor, cashier, prize counter, slots, blackjack, roulette; song `neon`). | poolhop and casino suites (RTP, rules, payouts). |\n1999\t| **M7** | Story to the end | Every event of §5.5 (D1 casino opening, D2 villa visit, D3 rain and the overheard call, D4 letter and semifinal, D5 final with its specials, party, endings A and B, credits slideshow, results, New Vacation+); every dialogue line in §5.7's counts; How to Play pages; About & Credits pages (filled at M10); the remaining songs `house`, `island`, `lagoon`, `boutique`, `neon`, `siesta`, `farewell`. | story suite; data counts; the full playthrough (§9.3) to both endings. |\n2000\t| **M8** | AI Hub online | `25-netplay`; session game options; the card; host and client sync; server mode; time-up, leave and end; `test/lib/fakehub.mjs`. | netcode suite (Node, with latency, jitter and loss); hub suite (the harness's four scenarios). |\n2001\t| **M9** | Attract, dev mode, touch-only, polish | `51-attract` with the full playlist; every dev tool and slider; the touch-only gate; every game setting; a juice pass (particles, shake and flash under the comfort settings); lighting per time of day; an art pass on every screen; a mix pass on all sound. | attract, dev and touch tests; the full playthrough again. **Accept:** the screenshot review list (§9.5) passes at 1280×720 and 1920×1080. |\n2002\t| **M10** | Ship | Final build. `npm test` all green, including browser and hub. `tools/check.mjs GAME.html`: act on every look note. Fill in About & Credits (§10). Write and validate `exit-interview.json`. Make sure nothing dev-only is bundled; report the final size. | everything in §11 is true. |\n2003\t\n2004\t---\n2005\t\n2006\t## 8. Risks and how to de-risk them\n2007\t\n2008\t| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risking |\n2009\t| --- | --- | --- |\n2010\t| **Volleyball feel**: floaty, unfair, endless or one-touch rallies | timing, physics and AI all interact | Closed-form ball: exact and testable. Every feel number is a TUNING slider from M1. An AI-vs-AI statistics test: rallies average 3–8 touches, serve faults < 12%, 1.5–4 points a minute. Filmstrips and real play each milestone. Difficulty presets. |\n2011\t| **Swimsuit and athletic rigs** look wrong in some views or facings | the Humanoid draw method is big; characters are about 50 px tall | Spike it in M2's first hours with one cut and one pattern. The rig sheet covers every view and facing. Patterns use 1-px features. Fallback if editing `draw` stalls: overdraw the suit inside the `r.actor` callback from projected joints (`rig.worldOffset(J.x)`), with no engine edit. |\n2012\t| **Animation doesn't meet the ball** at contact | sim and animation could drift apart | Drive animation from the plan: the jump starts at t* − rise and the IK targets the ball's position at t*. A filmstrip check per move. |\n2013\t| **Netcode** under latency, jitter and loss | a timing game, online | Deterministic launches on the shared hub clock; client-judged touches the host validates; snapshots only for positions. Node fake-hub tests with 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss run before the real harness. |\n2014\t| **Hub rule violations**: pause, quit, storage, dialogs, Create+Options | engine defaults | Session-specific game options (no menu, corner or autoPause), patch 6, and the harness's automatic checks inside the one test command. |\n2015\t| **Scope**: many systems | the breadth of the plan | The match comes first and every milestone ships something playable. Content is data. Reuse: one location scene, one Match class for every mode, one UI kit. |\n2016\t| **UI density on a TV** | inventories and stats invite tables | The rules in §4.2 are review items; at most 8 focusables; screenshot reviews at 1920×1080 and 1280×720. |\n2017\t| **Voices** harsh or out of sync | home-made synthesis | The per-letter hook; the dev Voice Lab; soft envelopes and a lowpass; Voices at .8 by default. |\n2018\t| **Music** quality | hand-written step notation | The instrument patch; the chord plans in §4.24.1; layered tracks; a listening pass; loops of at least 16 bars. |\n2019\t| **Mocap on the athletic build** | the clips were measured on other proportions | Check every clip in the rig sheet; `mocapMask: 'upper'`; a procedural fallback for any clip that fails. |\n2020\t| **Determinism** breaking tests or the netcode | a stray `Math.random` | rng streams only. Tests seed `Math.random`, and a test greps `src/` for `Math.random(` and fails. |\n2021\t| **Touch-only misdetected** on hybrid devices | touchscreen laptops | Require coarse-only pointers and no key or pad input yet; the notice goes on the first key or pad press. |\n2022\t| **No Chromium, or a full /tmp** | the machine is shared | `TMPDIR=DEV/.tmp`; `CHROMIUM_PATH` for `check.mjs`; ask the user before skipping a browser check, and never report one as passed if it was skipped. |\n2023\t\n2024\t---\n2025\t\n2026\t## 9. Testing\n2027\t\n2028\t### 9.1 One command\n2029\t\n2030\t`npm test`, which runs `node test/run.mjs`:\n2031\t\n2032\t- It runs every suite and prints **only failures** (`FAIL suite › case: detail`), then **one line**:\n2033\t  `N passed, M failed (core, data, ball, rules, judge, ai, match, vacation, shop, story, poolhop, casino, ui, attract,\n2034\t  dev, netcode, playthrough, browser, hub) in 42 s`. A failure exits with code 1.\n2035\t- Flags: `--only=ball,rules`, `--skip-browser`, `--skip-hub`, `--seed=n`.\n2036\t- As TASK.md says, rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (`--only`). Run everything before a milestone\n2037\t  ends.\n2038\t- **The headless loader** (`test/lib/load.mjs`) builds `build/game.js` first if any src file is newer. It makes a fresh\n2039\t  `vm` context with stand-ins: `window`, `addEventListener`, `location`, `matchMedia: () => ({ matches: false })`,\n2040\t  `navigator: { maxTouchPoints: 0 }`, and `AIHub` either absent or the fake. It loads the engine, the mocap scripts and\n2041\t  `build/game.js`, seeds `Math.random` with `E.rng(seed)`, and returns `{ E, game, G }`. It drives play with\n2042\t  `game.advance(seconds)`, `input.tap` and `input.hold`, and reads `game.debug.snapshot()`. Copy the pattern from the\n2043\t  handoff's `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`.\n2044\t\n2045\t### 9.2 The debug handle (`game.debug`)\n2046\t\n2047\t- **`snapshot()`** returns: `{ scene, day, slot, money, chips, partner, affinity, mood, flags, match: { phase, score,\n2048\t  serving, touches, ball, players: [{ id, x, y, z, act }] }, ui: { screen, focus }, attract, dev }`.\n2049\t- **`tools`**: `goto(scene, data)`, `newVacation(char, seed)`, `setDay(d, slot)`, `give(id, n)`, `money(n)`,\n2050\t  `affinity(id, v)`, `partner(id)`, `match(opts)`, `forcePoint(side)`, `perfectPlayer(on)`, `cpuControl(on)`,\n2051\t  `predict()` (each player's next t*, P* and kind), `step(n)`, `poolBot(on)`, `slotsForce(symbols)`, `deal(cards)`,\n2052\t  `rouletteForce(n)`.\n2053\t- The dev panel calls the same tools.\n2054\t\n2055\t### 9.3 Suites: what each proves\n2056\t\n2057\t| Suite | Cases |\n2058\t| --- | --- |\n2059\t| core | rng streams independent and reproducible; event bus; scene wrapper and overlays; TUNING reset; save migration |\n2060\t| data | unique ids; a taste for every gift and fighter; ≥ 2 loves, ≥ 3 likes and ≥ 3 dislikes each; every shop item exists with a price; every cut and pattern is known; every NPC spot is on walkable floor; schedule weights are valid; every story speaker exists and has a voice and portrait; line counts per §5.7; every line fits 2 lines of the box (`E.font.width`); no \"TODO\", \"TBD\", \"lorem\" or \"placeholder\" anywhere in `src/`; no `Math.random(` in `src/` |\n2061\t| ball | closed form vs stepped 1/120 s integration within .01 units over 3 s; `aim()` lands within .5 units; `timeAtHeight`; net clear / tape / net / antenna for constructed launches; in and out exactly at the line (r tolerance) |\n2062\t| rules | rally scoring, win by 2, the cap; 4 touches; double touch; a block counts as a touch; serve rotation alternates within a team; every fault scores for the right side; the match-point flag |\n2063\t| judge | boundaries at ±perfect, great and ok (inclusive); assist multipliers; first press only; reach, stretch and whiff; auto-receive |\n2064\t| ai | calls respected in assignment; formation by phase; attack zones avoid defenders (statistically); spectacle mode ends rallies within 3–9 touches |\n2065\t| match | AI vs AI over 20 seeds: it finishes; no phase stuck over 15 s; the ball never NaN or off the map; rally stats in range. A perfect bot beats Easy; an idle human loses 0–7. Golden Glare hides the ring, but not for a sunglasses wearer; Lucky Seven fires once; an ace triggers a replay; result stats add up to the score; same seed, same score |\n2066\t| vacation | slots used correctly; night places; weather table; schedules (same seed, same places; pairs together; a pair at the beach every daytime slot); moods; affinity math; gifts (the accept/refuse table, one per slot, a refused gift returns); invite thresholds; partner break-up; prize money; day-end drift; autosave and load mid-slot |\n2067\t| shop | buy, insufficient funds, caps; deals deterministic; equip and unequip; NPC suit acceptance by taste |\n2068\t| story | every event fires at its slot under its conditions; endings A and B; New Vacation+ carries the right things over |\n2069\t| poolhop | a perfect bot clears under time with all PERFECT; a wrong-button bot falls and recovers; double pads need both buttons; payout formula |\n2070\t| casino | slots: payout per line, and RTP 89–95% over 200k seeded spins; blackjack: S17 and H17, 3:2 blackjack, double, split aces, reshuffle; roulette: payouts for every bet type, wheel order, results uniform over 37k spins (loose chi-square); cashier rounding |\n2071\t| ui | focus moves spatially; hover via `input.feed('move', x, y)` focuses; click activates; right click goes back; prompts change with `lastDevice` and the glyph setting (✕, then A, then keycaps) |\n2072\t| attract | 9.9 s idle stays on the title, 10.0 s starts the attract; a key, pad, mouse or touch returns to the title with the input consumed; it plays a match, then the montage beats in order |\n2073\t| dev | the pause menu lists Dev Mode; opening it freezes time; moving a slider changes `G.T` and the behavior (gravity changes flight time); Reset all restores the defaults; jump tools land in the right scenes |\n2074\t| netcode | Node fake hub at 150 ± 50 ms latency and 5% loss, 1 to 4 players: host and clients agree on every launch and score; claims inside the window are accepted and outside it rejected; the host waits for late claims; a leaver becomes a CPU; time-up gives the right standings; a server host with no player runs and finishes; messages per second within limits; unreliable messages under 1,200 bytes |\n2075\t| playthrough | New Vacation as each fighter (6 fast runs): Day 1 tutorial won by a bot; D1 afternoon beach match; D1 night casino slots, blackjack and roulette; D2 morning buy a suit and give a gift; D2 afternoon Pool Hop; D2 night villa rest with a visit; D3 morning Promenade gifts; D3 afternoon rain match; D3 night the overheard call; D4 morning the letter and a postcard; D4 afternoon semifinal; D4 night rest; D5 morning shopping; D5 afternoon the final (won in 3 runs, lost in 3); D5 night party; ending; credits; results; title. Assert state at each step and no errors |\n2076\t| browser | Playwright on `file://GAME.html` at 1280×720. A 30 s tour (title → menu → Beach Match quick start → a few points → pause → Dev Mode open and close → quit) with no console errors; the title has pixels; the attract starts after 10 s idle; an emulated touch-only device (`hasTouch`, `isMobile`; if Chromium still reports a fine pointer, stub `matchMedia` in `page.addInitScript`) shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" and no touch buttons; `tools/check.mjs GAME.html` passes; screenshots saved |\n2077\t| hub | see below |\n2078\t\n2079\t**The hub suite** (Playwright with a local server):\n2080\t\n2081\t- Copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` with `GAME.html` into `DEV/test-output/hub-serve/`.\n2082\t- Start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there and read the port it prints. Confirm the served page's title\n2083\t  is ours before trusting a result.\n2084\t- Run four URLs: `harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with\n2085\t  `&scenario=host-leave`, `&players=2&scenario=server`, and `&players=1&auto=1`.\n2086\t- Each passes when `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. On failure print\n2087\t  the failing checks.\n2088\t- Stop the server **by its own PID** at the end.\n2089\t\n2090\t### 9.4 Art and animation checks\n2091\t\n2092\tThese are screenshots and filmstrips, outside the pass/fail count:\n2093\t\n2094\t- the rig sheet;\n2095\t- filmstrips (`tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1`) of the bump, set, spike, block, float and jump serves, dive, high-five,\n2096\t  every celebration, and a Pool Hop hop and slip;\n2097\t- every screen at 1280×720, at 1920×1080, and in a 4:3 window.\n2098\t\n2099\t### 9.5 Screenshot review list\n2100\t\n2101\t- **Front end:** title; menu; attract (the match and each montage beat); character select; invitation; arrival; tutorial\n2102\t  callouts.\n2103\t- **Travel and places:** island map (morning, night, rain); each location by day and by night; talk menu; a gift\n2104\t  reaction; shop with try-on; wardrobe; the Journal's Friends page.\n2105\t- **Minigames:** Pool Hop; casino floor; a slots jackpot; blackjack; roulette.\n2106\t- **Photos:** photo mode; album.\n2107\t- **Matches:** Broadcast and Serve Cam at day, sunset, night and in rain; the final with banners.\n2108\t- **Story ends:** party; both endings; credits; results.\n2109\t- **Multiplayer:** the Beach Match join screen with 4 players; the hub card.\n2110\t- **System:** every dev panel tab; the pause menu; Settings with Button symbols; the touch-only title.\n2111\t\n2112\t---\n2113\t\n2114\t## 10. Packaging, About screen and exit interview\n2115\t\n2116\t**Build `GAME.html`:** one file that works offline from `file://`. Check that:\n2117\t\n2118\t- it opens with no console errors;\n2119\t- the AI Hub client is the first script after `<meta charset>`, and the hub meta tags are present;\n2120\t- there are no external requests (`check.mjs` lists any);\n2121\t- `DEV/.src`, `DEV/hub` and the tests are not in it.\n2122\t\n2123\t**About & Credits** (the pages of §4.20). Fill them at M10, truthfully; write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n2124\t\n2125\t1. **Credits.**\n2126\t   - *Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball* is an original parody-tribute inspired by *Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach\n2127\t     Volleyball* (Team Ninja / Tecmo, Xbox, 2003). No assets from it are used.\n2128\t   - Design, code, art, music and writing: the builder (name the model).\n2129\t   - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT, github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge), modified (see Engine Feedback).\n2130\t   - Motion clips via the engine's mocap sets: Quaternius Universal Animation Library (CC0), Mesh2Motion (CC0), the CMU\n2131\t     Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses).\n2132\t   - Store shapes, if used: Kenney (CC0).\n2133\t   - The AI Hub session client and its version.\n2134\t2. **Source Information:** TASK.md's 14 fields in its order: Date (2026-11-03 17:47:49), Source, Plan (`PLAN.md`), Genre\n2135\t   and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage.\n2136\t   For Research, add your own to what this plan did: it read the engine handoff (API card, guide, index, asset card,\n2137\t   the sports kit, the Humanoid, Dialog and audio source), the AI Hub protocol, client example and harness checks, and\n2138\t   the engine repository's motion-capture catalogs. The source game was described from general knowledge, with no web\n2139\t   research.\n2140\t3. **Testing Feedback:** the four answers.\n2141\t4. **Engine Feedback:** the six answers, including the list of engine patches.\n2142\t5. **Prompt Feedback:** the four answers.\n2143\t\n2144\tPut the same text in the final chat reply.\n2145\t\n2146\t**`exit-interview.json`:** exactly TASK.md's shape, every value filled in, plain text. Suggested `aiHub` values:\n2147\t\n2148\t```json\n2149\t{\n2150\t  \"name\": \"Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball\",\n2151\t  \"tagline\": \"Stay ahead. Stay alive. Stay tanned.\",\n2152\t  \"description\": \"A five-day island vacation of 2-on-2 beach volleyball, friendships, swimsuit shopping, pool hopping and casino nights, ending with a match for the island against its owner.\",\n2153\t  \"type\": \"Game\",\n2154\t  \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n2155\t  \"source\": \"Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball\",\n2156\t  \"series\": \"Dead or Alive\",\n2157\t  \"players\": \"1–4\",\n2158\t  \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD move · Cross/Space/click hit on time · Square/E shot and block · Circle/Shift dive · Triangle/Q call\",\n2159\t  \"tags\": [\"sports\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"arcade\"]\n2160\t}\n2161\t```\n2162\t\n2163\tCheck that it parses: `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json', 'utf8'))\"`.\n2164\t\n2165\t**Working rules** (from TASK.md):\n2166\t\n2167\t- Keep every dev file in `DEV/`, and don't read other agents' folders.\n2168\t- Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools.\n2169\t- Start a server only for the hub harness, bound to 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks, and confirm the page is ours.\n2170\t- Stop only processes you started, by PID (never pkill, killall, or fuser -k).\n2171\t- Use no subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit.\n2172\t\n2173\t---\n2174\t\n2175\t## 11. Definition of done\n2176\t\n2177\t- [ ] Every item of §0's feature checklist works in `GAME.html`. No TODO, placeholder or stub text or art anywhere; the\n2178\t      data suite's grep passes.\n2179\t- [ ] A vacation plays from the invitation to the results through both endings, with save, load and Continue.\n2180\t- [ ] Beach Match works with 1–4 local players (pads and a split keyboard).\n2181\t- [ ] The AI Hub harness passes all four scenarios, and the game is unaffected outside a session.\n2182\t- [ ] The attract mode starts after 10 s idle on the title or menu, shows matches and every montage beat, and any input\n2183\t      exits it.\n2184\t- [ ] Dev Mode opens from the pause menu, with its tools and live sliders, and Reset to defaults works.\n2185\t- [ ] PlayStation glyphs by default and Xbox (A B X Y) in Settings; native keyboard and mouse with hover focus on every\n2186\t      screen; prompts follow the last device.\n2187\t- [ ] Touch-only devices show \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button and no touch controls, while the\n2188\t      attract runs.\n2189\t- [ ] Every sound is synthesized in code: music, effects, and gibberish voices for every speaker.\n2190\t- [ ] `npm test` prints only failures and one count line, and the final run is green.\n2191\t- [ ] About & Credits holds the Source Information and the Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback; `exit-interview.json`\n2192\t      parses.\n2193\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf","uuid":"d41f4c74-6f13-4018-b6f3-bc1290748b99","timestamp":"2026-11-04T06:12:05.784Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/PLAN.md","content":"\n**The six fighters: look and personality.** All use the `athletic` build. Sizes are rig `size`.\n\n| id | Name, epithet | From · style · age | Look | Personality |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `rin` | Rin Takamine, \"The Quiet Blade\" | Japan · kendo and iaido champion · 24 | 1.22; long blue-black high ponytail `#1d1a24`, bangs .6; skin `#f1cfb2`; eyes `#4a2c22` | composed perfectionist, dry one-liners; secretly adores cute things |\n| `lola` | Dolores \"Lola\" Vega, \"La Tormenta\" | Mexico · luchadora (pro wrestler) · 27 | 1.30, shoulderHalf +.25; curly dark brown `#3a2218` with a red bandana (`band` `#d8302a`); skin `#b9825a`; eyes `#3a2416` | loud, warm, theatrical; trash-talks with a grin; lives for a crowd |\n| `ingrid` | Ingrid Halvorsen, \"The Glacier\" | Norway · glíma wrestling and kickboxing, ex-biathlete · 26 | 1.38, the tallest; platinum braid `#f2ead2`; skin `#f7dccb`; eyes `#5aa0d8` | stoic and deadpan; hates the heat and misses snow; secretly a karaoke fiend |\n| `amara` | Amara Okafor, \"Rhythm Queen\" | UK/Nigeria · capoeira and dance fighting · 22 | 1.26; high puff `#2a1810` with gold cuffs; skin `#7a4a2e`; eyes `#2a1810` | cheerful social butterfly who loves music and fashion; dramatic |\n| `tess` | Tess Callahan, \"Riptide\" | Australia · surfer and MMA brawler · 25 | 1.28; sun-bleached messy bob `#f0d890`; skin `#e2ad84`; eyes `#3c7a5a` | laid-back but fiercely competitive; cheeky and outdoorsy |\n| `mei` | Mei-Lin Zhou, \"Little Phoenix\" | Hong Kong · wushu acrobat and xiangqi prodigy · 21 | 1.16, the smallest; black twin buns `#1a1418` with pink ribbons; skin `#f3d2b8`; eyes `#3a2420` | mischievous prankster with a sweet tooth; hates losing at anything |\n\n**The six fighters: play and voice.** Stats are 1–10. Voice values are base Hz, range in semitones, rate in letters/s,\nformant shift and wave (§4.24.3).\n\n| id | Tastes | POW / TEC / SPD / JMP | Voice | Signature suit | Starts with | Celebration |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `rin` | classic, elegant | 5 / 9 / 7 / 6 | 330, 3, 13, 1.05, triangle | Seigaiha | Ribbon (red) | `Bow` |\n| `lola` | bold, sporty | 9 / 5 / 5 / 8 | 260, 6, 16, .95, saw | Estrella | Sweatband | `Victory Fist Pump` |\n| `ingrid` | sporty, classic | 7 / 6 / 4 / 9 | 210, 2, 10, .9, triangle | Fjord | Sport Shades | `Head Nod` and a small fist |\n| `amara` | bold, cute | 5 / 6 / 9 / 8 | 340, 7, 15, 1.1, pulse; sing-song contour | Kente Pop | Hibiscus | `Dance Charleston` or `Cartwheel` |\n| `tess` | sporty, bold | 7 / 7 / 7 / 6 | 290, 5, 14, 1.0, saw; statements end rising | Reef Break | Wristbands | `Wave_Hello` (a shaka) |\n| `mei` | cute, elegant | 4 / 8 / 8 / 6 | 400, 6, 18, 1.18, pulse | Peony | Ribbon (pink) | `Backflip` |\n\n**Hosts and staff:**\n\n| id | Who | Look | Voice | Role |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `sonny` | Sonny Fortuna, \"The Man with the Golden Tan\": jackpot billionaire, DJ and would-be champion; a harmless buffoon | `bulky` 1.32; slick black hair (`spiky` `#121014`); gold aviators; a loud palm-print shirt (`shirt`, pattern `palms`, `#2fb5a0` / `#ffd36a`); white shorts; gold chain; skin `#d9a27a`. Final kit: black-and-gold tank and board shorts | 120, 7, 13, .8, saw, vibrato 6 Hz | host, PA commentator, casino boss, final opponent (POW 8 / TEC 5 / SPD 5 / JMP 5) |\n| `pepper` | Pepper Quill: concierge, scorekeeper and dealer; deadpan, ultra-competent, quietly holds Sonny's debts | `athletic` 1.24; auburn `bun` `#5a2a1e`; thin glasses; navy vest `#1d2433` with gold trim, slacks. Final kit: the Pinstripe racer | 230, 1, 17, 1.0, triangle | concierge, tutorial coach, blackjack dealer, final opponent (POW 6 / TEC 10 / SPD 7 / JMP 6) |\n| `kai` | Kai Makoa, an islander: bartender and croupier | `heroic` 1.25; short black hair; skin `#a8714a`; floral shirt (`#2fb5a0`), khaki shorts | 170, 4, 12, .85, triangle | Tiki Tok Bar, Sundries & Smiles, roulette |\n| `odette` | Odette Belrose, couturier | `athletic` 1.2; long silver-lilac hair `#c8b8e8`; pink sundress (`robe`, `#ff8aa8`); sun hat | 300, 5, 12, 1.1, pulse | Coral Couture |\n| `bo` | Coach Bo Brannigan, a retired beach pro | `bulky` 1.28; bald; visor; whistle; yellow tank `#ffd04a`, blue shorts | 150, 3, 14, .85, square | Riptide Sports |\n| crowd | staff and guests | small pixel sprites, plus a few HD rigs at .9 | — | spectators, casino crowd |\n\n### 5.2 Items\n\n**5.2.1 Swimsuits (21).** Colors are main · accent · trim. \"Day N+\" items reach the shop on that day.\n\n| id | Name | Cut | Pattern | Colors | Tastes | Where | S$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `seigaiha` | Seigaiha | onepiece | waves | `#23306b` `#e8eef8` `#c8303a` | classic, elegant | Rin's signature | — |\n| `estrella` | Estrella | sport2, shorts | stars | `#c8202c` `#ffd04a` `#1a1a1a` | bold, sporty | Lola's signature | — |\n| `fjord` | Fjord | rash, short sleeves | solid | `#9fd8f0` `#1d3560` `#ffffff` | sporty, classic | Ingrid's signature | — |\n| `kentepop` | Kente Pop | tankini | geo | `#ff8a1e` `#2f9e4a` `#ffd36a` | bold, cute | Amara's signature | — |\n| `reefbreak` | Reef Break | racer | gradient | `#1fb7b0` `#ff7a5e` `#ffffff` | sporty, bold | Tess's signature | — |\n| `peony` | Peony | halter | floral | `#ffb2a0` `#e85a8a` `#ffffff` | cute, elegant | Mei's signature | — |\n| `protour` | Pro Tour | racer | pin | `#f4f6fa` `#d8283a` `#1a2a5a` | sporty | Riptide | 12,000 |\n| `sandstorm` | Sandstorm | sport2, shorts | solid | `#e8c06a` `#1a1a1a` `#ffffff` | sporty, bold | Riptide | 9,000 |\n| `lifeguard` | Lifeguard | onepiece | solid | `#e0302a` `#ffd04a` `#ffffff` | sporty, classic | Riptide | 8,000 |\n| `coralrash` | Coral Rash | rash, long sleeves | stripes | `#ff7a5e` `#ffffff` `#2a3a5a` | sporty | Riptide | 14,000 |\n| `neonrush` | Neon Rush | tankini | gradient | `#7cff5a` `#ff4fb8` `#1a1a1a` | bold, sporty | Riptide, Day 2+ | 16,000 |\n| `monaco` | Monaco | halter | stripes | `#1d2f6a` `#ffffff` `#d8283a` | classic, elegant | Coral Couture | 22,000 |\n| `polkapop` | Polka Pop | sport2, brief | dots | `#e8283a` `#ffffff` `#ffd04a` | cute | Coral Couture | 18,000 |\n| `tropicana` | Tropicana | sarong | palms | `#2f8f4e` `#ffe0a0` `#ff8a1e` | elegant | Coral Couture | 26,000 |\n| `mermaid` | Mermaid | onepiece | scales | `#1fb7b0` `#7a5fd8` `#e8f8ff` | cute, elegant | Coral Couture, Day 3+ | 30,000 |\n| `sunsetblvd` | Sunset Boulevard | tankini | gradient | `#ff9e5e` `#7a3fa0` `#ffd36a` | bold, elegant | Coral Couture | 28,000 |\n| `midnight` | Midnight | onepiece | solid | `#16141c` `#ffd36a` `#ffd36a` | elegant, bold | Coral Couture, Day 4+ | 35,000 |\n| `gingham` | Gingham Picnic | tankini | check | `#6aa8e8` `#ffffff` `#e8283a` | cute, classic | Coral Couture | 15,000 |\n| `fortunagold` | Fortuna Gold | racer | lame | `#ffd36a` `#fff3c0` `#1a1a1a` | bold | win the Final | — |\n| `jackpot` | Jackpot | sport2, shorts | sevens | `#1a1a2a` `#ffd36a` `#e8283a` | bold, cute | casino prize counter | 300 chips |\n| `pinstripe` | Pepper's Pinstripe | racer | pin | `#121216` `#f4f4f4` `#ffd36a` | classic, elegant | Pepper's gift on Day 4 (see §5.5) | — |\n\n**5.2.2 Accessories (10).** One per anchor: head, face, hair, neck, wrists.\n\n| id | Name | Anchor | Look | Tastes | Where | S$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| `ribbon` | Ribbon | hair | a bow in the wearer's accent color | classic, cute | Rin and Mei start with it; Coral Couture | 2,000 |\n| `sweatband` | Sweatband | head (`band`) | terry band | sporty | Riptide; Lola starts with it | 3,000 |\n| `sportshades` | Sport Shades | face | wraparound lenses `#20262e`, frame `#e8eef2`; **sunglasses** | sporty | Riptide; Ingrid starts with them | 6,000 |\n| `heartshades` | Heart Shades | face | two pink hearts; **sunglasses** | cute, bold | Coral Couture | 7,500 |\n| `aviators` | Gold Aviators | face | like Sonny's; **sunglasses** | bold | Coral Couture, Day 3+ | 15,000 |\n| `visor` | Sun Visor | head (`visor`) | white with a colored brim | sporty | Riptide | 4,000 |\n| `sunhat` | Straw Sun Hat | head (`sunhat`) | wide straw brim, ribbon band | elegant, classic | Coral Couture | 9,000 |\n| `hibiscus` | Hibiscus | hair | a red flower behind the ear | cute, elegant | Sundries; Amara starts with it | 2,500 |\n| `shellnecklace` | Shell Necklace | neck | white shell dots | cute, classic | Sundries | 4,500 |\n| `wristbands` | Wristbands | wrists | 2-px bands | sporty | Riptide; Tess starts with them | 3,500 |\n\n**5.2.3 Gifts (25).** Stock and daily deals work as for every shop item (§4.12). Icons are `E.shapeSprite` of a store\nshape where one exists (`kenney-food:coconut`, `kenney-food:ice-cream`, `kenney-holiday:present-a-cube` for the\nwrapping), otherwise a 12×12 `E.sprite`.\n\n| Category | Items (S$) | Shop |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| food and drink | `mango_smoothie` Mango Smoothie 800 · `bubble_tea` Bubble Tea 900 · `matcha_icecream` Matcha Ice Cream 700 · `mochi_box` Mochi Box 1,500 · `bbq_skewers` BBQ Skewers 1,200 · `hot_sauce` Hot Sauce Sampler 2,000 · `iced_coffee` Iced Coffee 600 · `coconut` Fresh Coconut 400 | Sundries & Smiles |\n| goods | `plush_seal` Plush Seal 3,000 · `snow_globe` Snow Globe 2,500 · `puzzle_cube` Puzzle Cube 2,200 · `portable_speaker` Portable Speaker 9,000 · `matcha_kit` Matcha Kit 4,500 · `calligraphy_set` Calligraphy Set 6,000 · `knitting_kit` Knitting Kit 2,800 · `maracas` Maracas 1,400 · `luchador_mask` Luchador Mask 5,000 (Day 2+) | Sundries & Smiles |\n| books | `beach_paperback` Beach Paperback 1,200 · `fashion_mag` Fashion Magazine 800 | Sundries & Smiles |\n| sports | `energy_drink` Energy Drink 500 · `surf_wax` Surf Wax Deluxe 1,600 · `sunscreen` Sunscreen SPF 100 1,000 · `foam_finger` Foam Finger 900 | Riptide Sports |\n| fashion | `glitter_sandals` Glitter Sandals 5,500 · `gold_hoops` Gold Hoop Earrings 12,000 | Coral Couture |\n\n### 5.3 Tastes and starting affinity\n\n**Gift tastes.** L = love (+3), + = like (+2), · = neutral, − = dislike (−3). Each fighter has 2 loves, at least 3 likes\nand at least 3 dislikes; the data test checks it.\n\n| Gift | Rin | Lola | Ingrid | Amara | Tess | Mei |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| mango_smoothie | · | + | · | + | + | · |\n| bubble_tea | · | · | · | · | · | + |\n| matcha_icecream | + | · | + | · | · | + |\n| mochi_box | + | · | · | · | · | L |\n| bbq_skewers | · | + | · | · | L | − |\n| hot_sauce | − | L | − | · | + | − |\n| iced_coffee | · | · | + | · | · | · |\n| coconut | · | · | · | · | + | · |\n| plush_seal | L | · | + | · | · | + |\n| snow_globe | · | · | L | − | · | · |\n| puzzle_cube | + | − | · | · | · | L |\n| portable_speaker | − | + | · | L | + | · |\n| matcha_kit | L | − | · | · | · | + |\n| calligraphy_set | + | · | · | · | − | · |\n| knitting_kit | · | · | L | − | · | − |\n| maracas | · | + | · | + | · | · |\n| luchador_mask | · | L | · | · | + | · |\n| beach_paperback | + | − | + | · | · | · |\n| fashion_mag | · | · | − | + | − | + |\n| energy_drink | − | · | · | − | + | − |\n| surf_wax | · | · | · | · | L | · |\n| sunscreen | · | · | + | · | + | · |\n| foam_finger | − | + | · | · | + | · |\n| glitter_sandals | · | · | − | + | − | + |\n| gold_hoops | · | + | · | L | · | · |\n\n**Weather tastes** (for mood):\n\n| Fighter | Likes | Dislikes |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Ingrid | cloudy, rain | — |\n| Amara | sunny | rain |\n| Tess | sunny | — |\n| others | neutral | neutral |\n\n**Starting affinity.** One symmetric value per pair. It is also used to pair NPCs into teams.\n\n| | Rin | Lola | Ingrid | Amara | Tess | Mei |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Rin** | — | 20 | 35 | 25 | 30 | 40 |\n| **Lola** | 20 | — | 25 | 40 | 45 | 20 |\n| **Ingrid** | 35 | 25 | — | 20 | 35 | 25 |\n| **Amara** | 25 | 40 | 20 | — | 30 | 40 |\n| **Tess** | 30 | 45 | 35 | 30 | — | 25 |\n| **Mei** | 40 | 20 | 25 | 40 | 25 | — |\n\nEvery fighter except Ingrid starts with someone at 40 or more, who is willing to team up at once. Ingrid (\"The\nGlacier\") has to earn a partner; Pepper's tutorial gives everyone a starter partner anyway: the highest-affinity NPC.\n\n### 5.4 Locations and schedules\n\n**Locations.**\n\n| Location | Open | Map (tiles) | Features | NPC spots |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **Sunset Courts** | Morning, Afternoon (final and party override) | the 44×28 court map (§4.3) | Court A, bleachers, Tiki Tok Bar (Kai), umbrellas and loungers, lifeguard tower, DJ booth (Sonny in the mornings), surf rack, sandcastle, changing hut, Match Board | 3 bar stools, 3 loungers, 2 on the shoreline, 1 practice pair bumping a ball |\n| **Lagoon Pool** | Morning, Afternoon | 30×22 | a free-form pool, the Pool Hop deck and 32 pads, cabana bar, loungers, flamingo float, palms, tiki torches, changing hut | 2 swimming, 3 loungers, 2 sitting on the pool edge, 2 cabana stools |\n| **Fortuna Promenade** | Morning, Afternoon | 36×16 boardwalk | 3 shopfronts with doors, ice-cream cart, benches, lamps, planters, the railing over the sea | 2 benches, 3 window-shopping, 1 at the ice-cream cart |\n| **Your Villa** | always | 14×10 interior plus a balcony | bed (Rest / Sleep), closet (Wardrobe), desk (Journal: Save, Friends, Stats), album frame, mailbox (letters), a balcony view by time of day | 1 visitor spot (night events) |\n| **Casino Fortuna** | Night | 30×20 | cashier, 6 slots, blackjack (Pepper), roulette (Kai), VIP lounge (Sonny), prize counter, chandeliers, neon | 3 at slots, 2 at the roulette rail, 2 at the bar |\n| **Dock** | story only | 24×14 | seaplane, planks, crates, flags | the arrival lineup |\n\n**Schedule weights.** Daytime columns are Beach / Pool / Promenade / away; night is Casino / away.\n\n| NPC | Morning | Afternoon | Night |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Rin | 4 / 2 / 3 / 1 | 4 / 3 / 2 / 1 | 3 / 7 |\n| Lola | 5 / 2 / 2 / 1 | 5 / 2 / 2 / 1 | 6 / 4 |\n| Ingrid | 3 / 4 / 2 / 1 | 2 / 5 / 2 / 1 | 2 / 8 |\n| Amara | 3 / 2 / 4 / 1 | 3 / 3 / 3 / 1 | 7 / 3 |\n| Tess | 6 / 2 / 1 / 1 | 5 / 3 / 1 / 1 | 4 / 6 |\n| Mei | 2 / 3 / 4 / 1 | 3 / 2 / 4 / 1 | 8 / 2 |\n\n- **Rain** multiplies Beach × .2, Pool × .5, Promenade × 1.5 (it's covered) and away × 1.5.\n- **NPC teams** are formed at day start. Of the NPCs who aren't your partner, choose the pairing with the largest sum of\n  pair affinities plus ±10 noise from the `world` rng, preferring not to repeat yesterday's pairs. With 5 free NPCs, one\n  stays solo and can be invited.\n\n**Mailbox letters** (a simple letter screen with a portrait):\n\n| When | Letter |\n| --- | --- |\n| D1 night | Pepper's welcome (the rules again) |\n| D2 morning | Sonny's flyer: \"Free chips for champions!\" |\n| D3 morning | a note from your highest-affinity friend |\n| D4 morning | Pepper's warning |\n| D5 morning | Sonny's \"FINAL HYPE\" poster |\n\n### 5.5 Story beats and events\n\nData lives in `05-data-text.js`; triggers live in `30-vacation.js`.\n\n| When | Event | What happens | Effects |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| New Vacation | **The Invitation** | The letter on parchment with Sonny's gold seal; \"Who opened it?\" leads to character select (6 cards with portraits, epithets, style, stats as bars, tastes) | — |\n| D1 Morning | **Arrival** (Dock) | The seaplane lands and your fighter steps off; the other five are already there, each with one line. Sonny's grand welcome reveals the \"tournament\" is volleyball and a vacation. Pepper hands out keys and explains the slots, Sonny Dollars and the Cup in five days. | flags |\n| D1 Morning | **Welcome Match** (the tutorial) | \"Allow me to demonstrate!\" You and your starter partner (Pepper assigns the highest-affinity NPC) play Sonny & Pepper (\"five percent effort\"), first to 5, with Pepper's coaching (§5.5.1). Sonny loses comically and falls on his face. | partner set; S$10,000 |\n| D1 Night | Casino opening | If you go: Sonny gives 20 free chips and explains the games | chips |\n| D2 Night | Villa visit | If you rest in the villa and someone has affinity ≥ 50, she knocks with a snack: a 3-line chat with one choice (±4) | affinity |\n| D3 Afternoon | Rain shower | Sonny on the PA: \"LIQUID SUNSHINE, PEOPLE!\"; a rain match (wet ball: pass scatter × 1.2) | — |\n| D3 Night | **The Overheard Call** | At the casino: Sonny on the phone in the VIP lounge, \"…Yeah, I put the island on the Cup. What could go wrong?\" Pepper sees you hear it. Choice: \"Your secret's safe\" (kind) or \"Everyone's going to hear about this\" (cheeky). If you're not at the casino, you get a rumor letter instead. | flag `kind` |\n| D4 Morning | **Pepper's Letter** | \"The Final is tomorrow. Mr. Fortuna's serve is… dazzling. Eyewear is advised. — P.\" If you were kind on Day 3 and visited the casino at least once, it comes with the Pinstripe suit. | hint, suit |\n| D4 Afternoon | **Semifinal** | The NPC pair with the best record challenges you; it's marked SEMIFINAL on the Match Board. Win: seeded (you serve first in the Final), S$30,000. Lose: unseeded. | flags |\n| D5 Afternoon | **THE FORTUNA CUP FINAL** | The beach in banners, a bigger crowd; Sonny & Pepper in match gear as \"THE HOUSE\"; first to 11; the specials of §4.8.6 | win: S$100,000, Fortuna Gold |\n| D5 Night | **Farewell Party** | The beach at night: torches, fireworks, everyone dancing. Each fighter says goodbye with a line for her affinity stage. A group postcard is taken automatically. | album |\n| Ending A (Final won) | **The House Folds** | Sonny must hand over the island, but Pepper produces his IOUs: she owns it now. Sonny paddles off on the flamingo float: \"I'LL BE BACK… NEXT SUMMER!\" Pepper: \"Breakfast is at eight. The island is under new management.\" | — |\n| Ending B (Final lost) | **The House Always Wins** | Sonny gloats, then bets the island on one spin of a giant roulette wheel at the party \"to make it interesting\". Pepper calls red. It lands red. Same flamingo exit. Pepper: \"The house always wins. I am the house.\" | — |\n| After either | Credits | The postcard slideshow plus the party photo, with credits | — |\n| Then | **Vacation Results** | A report card: money earned, W–L, best friend (portrait), suits collected x/21, gifts given, best Pool Hop, casino net, postcards. A title: \"Island Icon\" (won the final and 3 Best Friends), \"Fortuna Champion\" (won the final), \"Social Butterfly\" (3+ Good Friends), otherwise \"Beach Bum\". Unlocks New Vacation+ and every suit for Beach Match. | unlocks |\n\n**5.5.1 The tutorial script** (Welcome Match, first to 5). Pepper's tips are non-modal callouts (Shell tutorial cards or a\nUI-kit panel) shown at the right moment, with the current device's glyphs:\n\n1. **Receive:** \"The ring shows where the ball comes down. Stand in it. Press ✕ as the ball reaches you.\"\n   (Auto-receive covers the first 2 receives if you miss.)\n2. **Set:** \"Your partner passed it to you. ✕ again as it drops, to set her up.\"\n3. **Spike:** \"She set you. You'll jump on your own. ✕ at the top. Push the stick, or point the mouse, to aim.\"\n4. **Serve:** \"✕ to toss, ✕ again at the top of the toss. □ tosses for a jump serve.\"\n5. **Block:** \"When they spike near the net, □ to block.\"\n6. **Dive:** \"Out of reach? ○ dives.\"\n7. **Call:** \"△ calls 'Mine!' or 'Yours!'. Your partner listens.\"\n8. **Chemistry:** \"The better you two get along, the better she plays. Chat. Bring gifts. Win.\"\n\nNew Vacation+ offers \"Skip the Welcome Match\".\n\n### 5.6 Opponents and difficulty\n\n**Day skill base** (before stats, difficulty and `T.aiSkillMul`):\n\n| Match | Base |\n| --- | --- |\n| tutorial | Sonny .20, Pepper .35 (Pepper never hits hard) |\n| Day 1 | .40 |\n| Day 2 | .50 |\n| Day 3 | .58 |\n| Day 4 | .66 |\n| Day 4 semifinal | .74 |\n| Final | Sonny .70, Pepper .85, plus the specials |\n\n- The Match Board lists the pairs present, each with stars (skill) and its record.\n- Off-screen NPC results (§4.10) decide which pair has the best record, and so who plays the semifinal.\n\n### 5.7 Writing\n\n**Style.**\n\n- Short: at most 2 lines of about 36 characters per page.\n- Upbeat and a little cheesy; each fighter's voice stays consistent.\n- **Sonny** speaks in ALL-CAPS bursts, with nicknames (\"CHAMP\", \"SUNSHINE\") and casino metaphors.\n- **Pepper** is dry, exact and faintly sarcastic, and never uses an exclamation mark.\n- Jokes come from fighting backgrounds and vacation mishaps. **No innuendo.**\n\n**How many lines** (the data test checks the counts):\n\n| Speaker | Lines needed |\n| --- | --- |\n| each fighter | greet ×3 (by stage); chat ×6 (2 each for affinity 0–39, 40–79, 80+); gift love ×2, like ×2, neutral ×1, refuse ×2; suit accepted ×1, suit refused ×1; invite accept ×2, decline ×2; leaving her old team ×1; pre-match taunt ×2; match win ×2, loss ×2; partner barks ×2; villa visit ×1 (with a choice); party farewell ×2 (low, high); ending ×1 |\n| Sonny | about 40 PA and commentary lines, plus story |\n| Pepper | about 25 (tutorial tips, quips, letters) |\n| Kai, Odette, Bo | about 8 each (shop quips) |\n\n**Sample lines.** They set the tone; reuse them.\n\n| Speaker | Line |\n| --- | --- |\n| Sonny, arrival | \"WELCOME, FIGHTERS, TO ISLA FORTUNA! The tournament of the century is… drumroll… BEACH VOLLEYBALL!\" / \"And a VACATION! You're welcome!\" |\n| Pepper, arrival | \"Villa keys. Sunscreen is in the minibar. The Cup is in five days. Mr. Fortuna is not taking questions.\" / \"Please don't feed him.\" |\n| Rin | greet: \"Good morning. The sand is… adequate.\" · chat: \"I practice my swing at dawn. The sea doesn't judge.\" · love (plush seal): \"…It's so round. I will name him Admiral.\" · refuse (energy drink): \"My heart rate is fine as it is. Thank you.\" |\n| Lola | greet: \"¡Hola, compañera! Ready to bring the THUNDER?\" · love (hot sauce): \"THIS! This is the fuel of champions!\" · refuse (paperback): \"A book? On vacation? Ay, you're funny.\" |\n| Ingrid | greet: \"It is thirty-one degrees. I am melting. Hello.\" · love (snow globe): \"Snow. Tiny, perfect snow. I may cry.\" · refuse (sandals): \"Glitter gets everywhere. Everywhere.\" |\n| Amara | greet: \"Hey hey! You hear that? The ocean's got rhythm!\" · love (speaker): \"Okay. The party starts NOW.\" · refuse (snow globe): \"Snow? Babe, we're in paradise.\" |\n| Tess | greet: \"G'day! Waves are pumping, sun's out. Life's good, yeah?\" · love (surf wax): \"Ohhh, the good stuff! My board says thanks.\" · refuse (calligraphy): \"Mate, I can barely write my own name.\" |\n| Mei | greet: \"Hehe. Bet you can't beat me at anything today.\" · love (puzzle cube): \"Solved it. Twice. Got another?\" · refuse (skewers): \"I don't eat things on sticks that used to have faces.\" |\n| Invites | Tess, accepting: \"Partners? Too right!\" · Ingrid, declining: \"I prefer to know someone before I trust them with my spikes.\" |\n| Results | Lola wins: \"¡VICTORIA! Somebody ring the bell!\" · Rin loses: \"I will reflect on this. Deeply.\" |\n| Sonny, commentary | \"WHAT A SPIKE! Somebody call a lifeguard!\" · \"ACE! That serve had TAXES on it!\" · \"BLOCKED! The wall is CLOSED for business!\" · \"Long rally, folks. I'm getting a tan just WATCHING.\" · \"MATCH POINT! I can't look! …I'm looking.\" |\n| Pepper, in the final | \"Statistically, that was unwise.\" · \"The house has noticed.\" |\n\n---\n\n## 6. UI/UX and controls\n\n### 6.1 Screen flow\n\n```\nboot → title ──(10 s idle)──► attract ──(any input)──► title\ntitle → menu ─ New Vacation → invitation → character select → arrival → Welcome Match → map\n             ─ Continue / Load → map (at the saved slot)\n             ─ Beach Match → setup and join (1–4) → match → results → setup / title\n             ─ Album · How to Play · Settings (engine) · About & Credits\nmap ⇄ location (Beach / Pool / Promenade / Villa)\n      inside: talk · gift · team up · challenge → match; shops · wardrobe · journal · album · letters · Pool Hop\nmap (night) → casino (cashier / slots / blackjack / roulette) or villa → day end → map (next day)\nDay 5: Final → party → ending A or B → credits → vacation results → title\nAI Hub session: boot → hub card → match → end overlay (no title, no menus)\nPause (gameplay scenes): Resume · How to Play · Take a Postcard · Dev Mode · Settings · Controls · Full screen · Quit to title\n```\n\n### 6.2 Controls\n\n**Matches:**\n\n| Action | DualSense | Xbox | Keyboard | Mouse |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Move | L stick, d-pad | L stick, d-pad | WASD, arrows | — |\n| Bump · set · spike · serve (timed) | ✕ | A | Space, J | Left |\n| Shot / tip · block · jump serve · free ball | □ | X | E, K | Right |\n| Dive | ○ | B | Shift, L | — |\n| Call Mine / Yours / Auto | △ | Y | Q, I | Middle |\n| Aim | L stick at contact | L stick | WASD at contact | the cursor on their court |\n| Camera | R3 | RS click | V | — |\n| Pause | Options | Menu | Esc, P | — |\n\n**Everywhere else:**\n\n| Context | Controls |\n| --- | --- |\n| Exploration | Move: stick / WASD · Run: hold ○ or R2 / Shift · Interact: ✕ / E, Space, Enter / click a person or thing · Gift bag: □ / G · Island map: △ / M, Tab · Postcard: Create / C · Pause: Options / Esc |\n| Menus | Navigate: d-pad, stick / arrows, WASD / hover · Select: ✕ / Enter, Space / click · Back: ○ / Backspace / right click · Tabs: L1, R1 / Q, E / wheel · Option: □ / F · Special: △ / R |\n| Pool Hop | the four face buttons ✕ ○ □ △ (A B X Y; J, L, K, I or Space, Shift, E, Q); two at once on double pads |\n| Casino | the on-screen prompts (§4.16), plus blackjack H, S, D, P and slot stops J, K, L |\n| Beach Match, split keyboard | P1: WASD with F hit, G dive, H shot, R call · P2: arrows with `.` hit, `/` dive, `,` shot, L call |\n\n### 6.3 Prompt rules\n\n- Every screen has the bottom prompt bar. During a rally, at most 3 context prompts.\n- Glyphs follow the last device at once, per player.\n- PlayStation symbols are the default for any controller; Settings → Button symbols switches to Xbox (A B X Y).\n- Keyboard prompts show keycaps and mouse prompts show the mouse icon. Never show controller glyphs to a keyboard\n  player, or keys to a pad player.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Build order and milestones\n\n**Every milestone ends with:**\n\n- `npm test` green;\n- a fresh build of `GAME.html` that runs from `file://` with no console errors;\n- its screenshots reviewed.\n\nGrey-box art may appear inside a milestone only if that same milestone replaces it. Nothing shipped carries placeholder\nart, text or TODOs.\n\n| # | Milestone | Build | Tests and acceptance |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| **M0** | Foundation | Fetch the sources (§3.1), copy the engine and tools, `npm install`, `npx playwright install chromium`. `tools/build.mjs`; the `test/run.mjs` skeleton and vm loader (§9.1). `00-core`, `01-tuning`, `10-input` (action maps, glyph icons, prompt bar, touch-only gate), `11-ui` (Panel, Button, List, PromptBar, Slider), `99-main`, and real boot, title and menu scenes. Engine patches 1, 2, 6, 7. | rng reproducibility; glyph per device (PS ✕ / Xbox A / keycap); UI focus by taps and by `input.feed('move')` hover; title → menu. **Accept:** GAME.html shows the title with ✕ on a pad and keycaps on a keyboard; Settings shows Button symbols. |\n| **M1** | Volleyball core (the most important) | `20-ball`, `21-rules`, `22-players`, `23-ai`, `24-match` (phases, Broadcast camera, basic HUD); the court map with sand, lines and net; human controls with the judge and ring; AI vs AI; 1P with an AI partner vs AI. **Dev panel v1** with the Ball, Timing, Players and AI sliders and Reset, because tuning needs it now. | ball, rules, judge, ai and match suites (§9.3). **Accept:** a full 1P match to 7 is fun with the default numbers; filmstrips of the ring and of a rally look right. |\n| **M2** | Characters and court art | Engine patch 5 (athletic build, swim cuts and patterns, hair, hats, extras, poses, bare feet); `13-rigs`; `15-anim` (every volleyball move, IK overlay, high-fives, celebrations); cut the mocap set and wire it; `14-world-art` (court surroundings, backdrops for day, sunset and night, bleachers and crowd, net art, DJ booth, scoreboard); the Serve Cam view; `tools/rigsheet.mjs`. | every suit, hair and accessory builds a rig and draws without errors (browser suite); rig sheet and filmstrips reviewed. **Accept:** match screenshots meet the Look target in both cameras; no character in default colors. |\n| **M3** | Presentation, audio, exhibition, local multiplayer | `12-audio` (patches 3 and 4, SFX, voices, the `spike` and `sunrise` songs, jingles); commentary; judgement popups; celebrations; replay; results; `52-exhibition` with 1–4 joins and per-player prompts; final title and menu art and music. | 4 local players (`addPlayer` pads plus the keyboard halves) each control one fighter; songs parse with no unknown tokens; voices are no-ops headless and play in the browser. **Accept:** a Beach Match end to end with 2 keyboard halves and 2 pads. |\n| **M4** | Vacation core | `30-vacation` (state, calendar, weather, schedules, moods, affinity, partners, money, saves); `31-map`; `32-location` (Beach, Pool, Promenade, Villa with real maps, props and NPC spots); talk menu, gifts, team-up, Match Board challenges, day end; `34-story` wiring with the invitation, character select, arrival, Welcome Match and its coaching. | vacation suite; New Vacation → tutorial → map; save and load in the middle of a day. **Accept:** Days 1–2 fully playable. |\n| **M5** | Shops, wardrobe, journal, postcards | `33-shop` (3 shops, deals, try-on), wardrobe and partner page, suit gifts to NPCs, the Journal (Friends with known likes, Stats, Save), letters, `42-photo` (photo mode, album, title backdrop, PNG export). | shop suite; photo specs saved, restored and re-rendered (browser); album replace and delete. |\n| **M6** | Minigames | `40-poolhop` (song `lagoon`, judging on the music clock, wobble and double pads); `41-casino` (floor, cashier, prize counter, slots, blackjack, roulette; song `neon`). | poolhop and casino suites (RTP, rules, payouts). |\n| **M7** | Story to the end | Every event of §5.5 (D1 casino opening, D2 villa visit, D3 rain and the overheard call, D4 letter and semifinal, D5 final with its specials, party, endings A and B, credits slideshow, results, New Vacation+); every dialogue line in §5.7's counts; How to Play pages; About & Credits pages (filled at M10); the remaining songs `house`, `island`, `lagoon`, `boutique`, `neon`, `siesta`, `farewell`. | story suite; data counts; the full playthrough (§9.3) to both endings. |\n| **M8** | AI Hub online | `25-netplay`; session game options; the card; host and client sync; server mode; time-up, leave and end; `test/lib/fakehub.mjs`. | netcode suite (Node, with latency, jitter and loss); hub suite (the harness's four scenarios). |\n| **M9** | Attract, dev mode, touch-only, polish | `51-attract` with the full playlist; every dev tool and slider; the touch-only gate; every game setting; a juice pass (particles, shake and flash under the comfort settings); lighting per time of day; an art pass on every screen; a mix pass on all sound. | attract, dev and touch tests; the full playthrough again. **Accept:** the screenshot review list (§9.5) passes at 1280×720 and 1920×1080. |\n| **M10** | Ship | Final build. `npm test` all green, including browser and hub. `tools/check.mjs GAME.html`: act on every look note. Fill in About & Credits (§10). Write and validate `exit-interview.json`. Make sure nothing dev-only is bundled; report the final size. | everything in §11 is true. |\n\n---\n\n## 8. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risking |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Volleyball feel**: floaty, unfair, endless or one-touch rallies | timing, physics and AI all interact | Closed-form ball: exact and testable. Every feel number is a TUNING slider from M1. An AI-vs-AI statistics test: rallies average 3–8 touches, serve faults < 12%, 1.5–4 points a minute. Filmstrips and real play each milestone. Difficulty presets. |\n| **Swimsuit and athletic rigs** look wrong in some views or facings | the Humanoid draw method is big; characters are about 50 px tall | Spike it in M2's first hours with one cut and one pattern. The rig sheet covers every view and facing. Patterns use 1-px features. Fallback if editing `draw` stalls: overdraw the suit inside the `r.actor` callback from projected joints (`rig.worldOffset(J.x)`), with no engine edit. |\n| **Animation doesn't meet the ball** at contact | sim and animation could drift apart | Drive animation from the plan: the jump starts at t* − rise and the IK targets the ball's position at t*. A filmstrip check per move. |\n| **Netcode** under latency, jitter and loss | a timing game, online | Deterministic launches on the shared hub clock; client-judged touches the host validates; snapshots only for positions. Node fake-hub tests with 150 ± 50 ms and 5% loss run before the real harness. |\n| **Hub rule violations**: pause, quit, storage, dialogs, Create+Options | engine defaults | Session-specific game options (no menu, corner or autoPause), patch 6, and the harness's automatic checks inside the one test command. |\n| **Scope**: many systems | the breadth of the plan | The match comes first and every milestone ships something playable. Content is data. Reuse: one location scene, one Match class for every mode, one UI kit. |\n| **UI density on a TV** | inventories and stats invite tables | The rules in §4.2 are review items; at most 8 focusables; screenshot reviews at 1920×1080 and 1280×720. |\n| **Voices** harsh or out of sync | home-made synthesis | The per-letter hook; the dev Voice Lab; soft envelopes and a lowpass; Voices at .8 by default. |\n| **Music** quality | hand-written step notation | The instrument patch; the chord plans in §4.24.1; layered tracks; a listening pass; loops of at least 16 bars. |\n| **Mocap on the athletic build** | the clips were measured on other proportions | Check every clip in the rig sheet; `mocapMask: 'upper'`; a procedural fallback for any clip that fails. |\n| **Determinism** breaking tests or the netcode | a stray `Math.random` | rng streams only. Tests seed `Math.random`, and a test greps `src/` for `Math.random(` and fails. |\n| **Touch-only misdetected** on hybrid devices | touchscreen laptops | Require coarse-only pointers and no key or pad input yet; the notice goes on the first key or pad press. |\n| **No Chromium, or a full /tmp** | the machine is shared | `TMPDIR=DEV/.tmp`; `CHROMIUM_PATH` for `check.mjs`; ask the user before skipping a browser check, and never report one as passed if it was skipped. |\n\n---\n\n## 9. Testing\n\n### 9.1 One command\n\n`npm test`, which runs `node test/run.mjs`:\n\n- It runs every suite and prints **only failures** (`FAIL suite › case: detail`), then **one line**:\n  `N passed, M failed (core, data, ball, rules, judge, ai, match, vacation, shop, story, poolhop, casino, ui, attract,\n  dev, netcode, playthrough, browser, hub) in 42 s`. A failure exits with code 1.\n- Flags: `--only=ball,rules`, `--skip-browser`, `--skip-hub`, `--seed=n`.\n- As TASK.md says, rerun a suite only after changing the code it covers (`--only`). Run everything before a milestone\n  ends.\n- **The headless loader** (`test/lib/load.mjs`) builds `build/game.js` first if any src file is newer. It makes a fresh\n  `vm` context with stand-ins: `window`, `addEventListener`, `location`, `matchMedia: () => ({ matches: false })`,\n  `navigator: { maxTouchPoints: 0 }`, and `AIHub` either absent or the fake. It loads the engine, the mocap scripts and\n  `build/game.js`, seeds `Math.random` with `E.rng(seed)`, and returns `{ E, game, G }`. It drives play with\n  `game.advance(seconds)`, `input.tap` and `input.hold`, and reads `game.debug.snapshot()`. Copy the pattern from the\n  handoff's `game/test.mjs` and `kits/test.mjs`.\n\n### 9.2 The debug handle (`game.debug`)\n\n- **`snapshot()`** returns: `{ scene, day, slot, money, chips, partner, affinity, mood, flags, match: { phase, score,\n  serving, touches, ball, players: [{ id, x, y, z, act }] }, ui: { screen, focus }, attract, dev }`.\n- **`tools`**: `goto(scene, data)`, `newVacation(char, seed)`, `setDay(d, slot)`, `give(id, n)`, `money(n)`,\n  `affinity(id, v)`, `partner(id)`, `match(opts)`, `forcePoint(side)`, `perfectPlayer(on)`, `cpuControl(on)`,\n  `predict()` (each player's next t*, P* and kind), `step(n)`, `poolBot(on)`, `slotsForce(symbols)`, `deal(cards)`,\n  `rouletteForce(n)`.\n- The dev panel calls the same tools.\n\n### 9.3 Suites: what each proves\n\n| Suite | Cases |\n| --- | --- |\n| core | rng streams independent and reproducible; event bus; scene wrapper and overlays; TUNING reset; save migration |\n| data | unique ids; a taste for every gift and fighter; ≥ 2 loves, ≥ 3 likes and ≥ 3 dislikes each; every shop item exists with a price; every cut and pattern is known; every NPC spot is on walkable floor; schedule weights are valid; every story speaker exists and has a voice and portrait; line counts per §5.7; every line fits 2 lines of the box (`E.font.width`); no \"TODO\", \"TBD\", \"lorem\" or \"placeholder\" anywhere in `src/`; no `Math.random(` in `src/` |\n| ball | closed form vs stepped 1/120 s integration within .01 units over 3 s; `aim()` lands within .5 units; `timeAtHeight`; net clear / tape / net / antenna for constructed launches; in and out exactly at the line (r tolerance) |\n| rules | rally scoring, win by 2, the cap; 4 touches; double touch; a block counts as a touch; serve rotation alternates within a team; every fault scores for the right side; the match-point flag |\n| judge | boundaries at ±perfect, great and ok (inclusive); assist multipliers; first press only; reach, stretch and whiff; auto-receive |\n| ai | calls respected in assignment; formation by phase; attack zones avoid defenders (statistically); spectacle mode ends rallies within 3–9 touches |\n| match | AI vs AI over 20 seeds: it finishes; no phase stuck over 15 s; the ball never NaN or off the map; rally stats in range. A perfect bot beats Easy; an idle human loses 0–7. Golden Glare hides the ring, but not for a sunglasses wearer; Lucky Seven fires once; an ace triggers a replay; result stats add up to the score; same seed, same score |\n| vacation | slots used correctly; night places; weather table; schedules (same seed, same places; pairs together; a pair at the beach every daytime slot); moods; affinity math; gifts (the accept/refuse table, one per slot, a refused gift returns); invite thresholds; partner break-up; prize money; day-end drift; autosave and load mid-slot |\n| shop | buy, insufficient funds, caps; deals deterministic; equip and unequip; NPC suit acceptance by taste |\n| story | every event fires at its slot under its conditions; endings A and B; New Vacation+ carries the right things over |\n| poolhop | a perfect bot clears under time with all PERFECT; a wrong-button bot falls and recovers; double pads need both buttons; payout formula |\n| casino | slots: payout per line, and RTP 89–95% over 200k seeded spins; blackjack: S17 and H17, 3:2 blackjack, double, split aces, reshuffle; roulette: payouts for every bet type, wheel order, results uniform over 37k spins (loose chi-square); cashier rounding |\n| ui | focus moves spatially; hover via `input.feed('move', x, y)` focuses; click activates; right click goes back; prompts change with `lastDevice` and the glyph setting (✕, then A, then keycaps) |\n| attract | 9.9 s idle stays on the title, 10.0 s starts the attract; a key, pad, mouse or touch returns to the title with the input consumed; it plays a match, then the montage beats in order |\n| dev | the pause menu lists Dev Mode; opening it freezes time; moving a slider changes `G.T` and the behavior (gravity changes flight time); Reset all restores the defaults; jump tools land in the right scenes |\n| netcode | Node fake hub at 150 ± 50 ms latency and 5% loss, 1 to 4 players: host and clients agree on every launch and score; claims inside the window are accepted and outside it rejected; the host waits for late claims; a leaver becomes a CPU; time-up gives the right standings; a server host with no player runs and finishes; messages per second within limits; unreliable messages under 1,200 bytes |\n| playthrough | New Vacation as each fighter (6 fast runs): Day 1 tutorial won by a bot; D1 afternoon beach match; D1 night casino slots, blackjack and roulette; D2 morning buy a suit and give a gift; D2 afternoon Pool Hop; D2 night villa rest with a visit; D3 morning Promenade gifts; D3 afternoon rain match; D3 night the overheard call; D4 morning the letter and a postcard; D4 afternoon semifinal; D4 night rest; D5 morning shopping; D5 afternoon the final (won in 3 runs, lost in 3); D5 night party; ending; credits; results; title. Assert state at each step and no errors |\n| browser | Playwright on `file://GAME.html` at 1280×720. A 30 s tour (title → menu → Beach Match quick start → a few points → pause → Dev Mode open and close → quit) with no console errors; the title has pixels; the attract starts after 10 s idle; an emulated touch-only device (`hasTouch`, `isMobile`; if Chromium still reports a fine pointer, stub `matchMedia` in `page.addInitScript`) shows \"Controller or keyboard required\" and no touch buttons; `tools/check.mjs GAME.html` passes; screenshots saved |\n| hub | see below |\n\n**The hub suite** (Playwright with a local server):\n\n- Copy `harness.html`, `bridge.js` and `round.js` with `GAME.html` into `DEV/test-output/hub-serve/`.\n- Start `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` there and read the port it prints. Confirm the served page's title\n  is ours before trusting a result.\n- Run four URLs: `harness.html?game=GAME.html&players=4&latency=150&jitter=50&loss=5&auto=1`, the same with\n  `&scenario=host-leave`, `&players=2&scenario=server`, and `&players=1&auto=1`.\n- Each passes when `document.body.dataset.complete === 'true'` and `window.__hubCheck.pass === true`. On failure print\n  the failing checks.\n- Stop the server **by its own PID** at the end.\n\n### 9.4 Art and animation checks\n\nThese are screenshots and filmstrips, outside the pass/fail count:\n\n- the rig sheet;\n- filmstrips (`tools/filmstrip.mjs --seed 1`) of the bump, set, spike, block, float and jump serves, dive, high-five,\n  every celebration, and a Pool Hop hop and slip;\n- every screen at 1280×720, at 1920×1080, and in a 4:3 window.\n\n### 9.5 Screenshot review list\n\n- **Front end:** title; menu; attract (the match and each montage beat); character select; invitation; arrival; tutorial\n  callouts.\n- **Travel and places:** island map (morning, night, rain); each location by day and by night; talk menu; a gift\n  reaction; shop with try-on; wardrobe; the Journal's Friends page.\n- **Minigames:** Pool Hop; casino floor; a slots jackpot; blackjack; roulette.\n- **Photos:** photo mode; album.\n- **Matches:** Broadcast and Serve Cam at day, sunset, night and in rain; the final with banners.\n- **Story ends:** party; both endings; credits; results.\n- **Multiplayer:** the Beach Match join screen with 4 players; the hub card.\n- **System:** every dev panel tab; the pause menu; Settings with Button symbols; the touch-only title.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Packaging, About screen and exit interview\n\n**Build `GAME.html`:** one file that works offline from `file://`. Check that:\n\n- it opens with no console errors;\n- the AI Hub client is the first script after `<meta charset>`, and the hub meta tags are present;\n- there are no external requests (`check.mjs` lists any);\n- `DEV/.src`, `DEV/hub` and the tests are not in it.\n\n**About & Credits** (the pages of §4.20). Fill them at M10, truthfully; write \"unknown\" for anything you can't confirm.\n\n1. **Credits.**\n   - *Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball* is an original parody-tribute inspired by *Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach\n     Volleyball* (Team Ninja / Tecmo, Xbox, 2003). No assets from it are used.\n   - Design, code, art, music and writing: the builder (name the model).\n   - Engine: my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (MIT, github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge), modified (see Engine Feedback).\n   - Motion clips via the engine's mocap sets: Quaternius Universal Animation Library (CC0), Mesh2Motion (CC0), the CMU\n     Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (free for all uses).\n   - Store shapes, if used: Kenney (CC0).\n   - The AI Hub session client and its version.\n2. **Source Information:** TASK.md's 14 fields in its order: Date (2026-11-03 17:47:49), Source, Plan (`PLAN.md`), Genre\n   and Perspective, Tech, Art Direction, Animation, Audio, Online, Testing, Research, Environment, Model, Usage.\n   For Research, add your own to what this plan did: it read the engine handoff (API card, guide, index, asset card,\n   the sports kit, the Humanoid, Dialog and audio source), the AI Hub protocol, client example and harness checks, and\n   the engine repository's motion-capture catalogs. The source game was described from general knowledge, with no web\n   research.\n3. **Testing Feedback:** the four answers.\n4. **Engine Feedback:** the six answers, including the list of engine patches.\n5. **Prompt Feedback:** the four answers.\n\nPut the same text in the final chat reply.\n\n**`exit-interview.json`:** exactly TASK.md's shape, every value filled in, plain text. Suggested `aiHub` values:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball\",\n  \"tagline\": \"Stay ahead. Stay alive. Stay tanned.\",\n  \"description\": \"A five-day island vacation of 2-on-2 beach volleyball, friendships, swimsuit shopping, pool hopping and casino nights, ending with a match for the island against its owner.\",\n  \"type\": \"Game\",\n  \"genre\": \"Sports\",\n  \"source\": \"Dead or Alive Xtreme Beach Volleyball\",\n  \"series\": \"Dead or Alive\",\n  \"players\": \"1–4\",\n  \"controls\": \"Stick/WASD move · Cross/Space/click hit on time · Square/E shot and block · Circle/Shift dive · Triangle/Q call\",\n  \"tags\": [\"sports\", \"versus\", \"co-op\", \"pixel art\", \"comedy\", \"arcade\"]\n}\n```\n\nCheck that it parses: `node -e \"JSON.parse(require('fs').readFileSync('exit-interview.json', 'utf8'))\"`.\n\n**Working rules** (from TASK.md):\n\n- Keep every dev file in `DEV/`, and don't read other agents' folders.\n- Prefer `file://` and the engine's headless tools.\n- Start a server only for the hub harness, bound to 127.0.0.1 on a port the OS picks, and confirm the page is ours.\n- Stop only processes you started, by PID (never pkill, killall, or fuser -k).\n- Use no subagents or workflows to review, judge or audit.\n\n---\n\n## 11. Definition of done\n\n- [ ] Every item of §0's feature checklist works in `GAME.html`. No TODO, placeholder or stub text or art anywhere; the\n      data suite's grep passes.\n- [ ] A vacation plays from the invitation to the results through both endings, with save, load and Continue.\n- [ ] Beach Match works with 1–4 local players (pads and a split keyboard).\n- [ ] The AI Hub harness passes all four scenarios, and the game is unaffected outside a session.\n- [ ] The attract mode starts after 10 s idle on the title or menu, shows matches and every montage beat, and any input\n      exits it.\n- [ ] Dev Mode opens from the pause menu, with its tools and live sliders, and Reset to defaults works.\n- [ ] PlayStation glyphs by default and Xbox (A B X Y) in Settings; native keyboard and mouse with hover focus on every\n      screen; prompts follow the last device.\n- [ ] Touch-only devices show \"Controller or keyboard required\" with a Settings button and no touch controls, while the\n      attract runs.\n- [ ] Every sound is synthesized in code: music, effects, and gibberish voices for every speaker.\n- [ ] `npm test` prints only failures and one count line, and the final run is green.\n- [ ] About & Credits holds the Source Information and the Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback; `exit-interview.json`\n      parses.\n","numLines":545,"startLine":1649,"totalLines":2193}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01LgsyxLxPkEQHViZkffDavt","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
