{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xo4F5fd5THHNDVxrkq6576","type":"tool_result","content":"beat final location [ 'photo' ] active true t 0\n0 location true true\n1 location true false\n2 location true false\n3 location true false\n4 location true false\n5 location true false\nlocation true","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf","uuid":"3feb5495-b5bb-485c-b5ad-28195d8ec41a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:11:31.224Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"beat final location [ 'photo' ] active true t 0\n0 location true true\n1 location true false\n2 location true false\n3 location true false\n4 location true false\n5 location true false\nlocation true","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-215911__x5b1962/agent.out","hunks":[{"oldStart":2378,"oldLines":3,"newStart":2378,"newLines":4,"lines":[" {\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01VTgsPfsguLtnLQXajDxdSm\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"empty fields: 0 | testing 4 engine 6 prompt 4 tags 6\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\",\"uuid\":\"42c3cf0b-c9bf-4651-a2cd-779af6f519e2\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:11:06.840Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"empty fields: 0 | testing 4 engine 6 prompt 4 tags 6\",\"stderr\":\"\",\"interrupted\":false,\"isImage\":false,\"noOutputExpected\":false},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01VTgsPfsguLtnLQXajDxdSm\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CghUG2WM1UG5m6Lei6T8C\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"thinking\",\"thinking\":\"\",\"signature\":\"\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":464,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":862732,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":464},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\",\"uuid\":\"92820260-f074-4987-a70a-5765fba92e26\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:11:14.742Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CghUG26HtsCEpu7YVu5Rm\",\"thinking_duration_ms\":6573,\"thinking_display\":\"updates\"}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CghUG2WM1UG5m6Lei6T8C\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"I've closed the remaining gaps: the final release build passed 341 of 341 checks, including the AI Hub harness's four scenarios in Chromium.\\n\\n**What I checked against each point:**\\n- **Builder's Eye and Patterns:** I listed the individual checks, and they all pass.\\n  - The Builder's Eye cursor steps a cell at a time and rises a level.\\n  - A Pattern starts from its scroll, turns 90°, and is laid down using the scroll up.\\n  - The Quilters' Hall Pattern has 129 build cells.\\n  - Residents build cells from the Town Chest.\\n  - Finishing the Pattern forms the Quilters' Hall room.\\n  - The scripted playthrough builds the Hall the same way.\\n- **Quilting Bee win:** the round ends as a win after the raid. The earlier failure was in the test: it left the raid running unattended for a minute. Losing when the Banner falls, the +3 score per barn block, kill scoring and the standings also pass.\\n- **Awards:** I added the check that was missing. The Knot Cutter award goes to the player with the most kills, and Master Quilter is checked too.\\n- **TODO, FIXME, placeholder, stub:** none in the sources, tests or tools. The one match in the built HTML is a comment inside the engine's own build-stamp code, not game code.\\n- **Exit interview:** `exit-interview.json` parses and has no empty fields. The testing answers now give numbers I counted from this session, and the HTML was rebuilt so the About screen matches. Usage stays \\\"unknown\\\", which TASK.md allows when it can't be confirmed.\\n\\nThe game file is `DragonQuiltBuilders-DragonQuestBuilders-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-215911.html`, with `exit-interview.json` beside it in the work folder.\\n\\n## Source Information\\n- **Date:** 2026-11-03 21:59:11\\n- **Source:** Dragon Quest Builders\\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\\n- **Genre and Perspective:** a sandbox action RPG (block building, crafting, town building, real-time combat, a siege and bosses), seen in third-person isometric 2.5D over a true voxel world. The camera turns in 90° steps and zooms; a three-quarter view is a setting.\\n- **Tech:**\\n  - my-3D2dge v0.85.2, lightly modified, plus my own voxel world, renderer, physics and pathfinding, in plain ES2020 JavaScript on Canvas 2D and Web Audio.\\n  - AI Hub Session Protocol v1 (client session.js 1.4.0).\\n  - Node 18+ for the headless tests and Playwright 1.63.0 for the browser checks.\\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native pixel style with an original patchwork-quilt look. Every block is a stitched fabric patch, the menus are felt panels with running-stitch borders, and the logo is patchwork.\\n- **Animation:** the engine's procedural rigs and moves, plus new moves (place, eat, stir, chop), poses, tools drawn on the rig, boss wind-ups, swinging doors, a fluttering banner, portal swirls and an unravel effect.\\n- **Audio:** all in code: 14 original songs on a leitmotif (the town waltz gains layers as the town levels up), 12 jingles, about 50 synthesized sound effects, and Animalese voices for each character with their own Voices volume setting.\\n- **Online:** AI Hub shared-world sessions for the Quilting Bee co-op round: the game's own card, a host-run world, standings, awards, time-up, leave, end and server mode. The same round plays solo with bots outside the hub.\\n- **Testing:** headless scripted tests in 19 suites (341 checks), including a full playthrough and a fake multi-copy hub with latency and loss; Playwright screenshots; the hub harness's four scenarios.\\n- **Research:** no web research on the source game. I read the engine's documentation and source sections, and the AI Hub protocol README.\\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown\\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\\n- **Usage:** unknown\\n\\n## Testing Feedback\\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** 41: 31 bugs in the game and its AI player, and 10 mistakes in the tests themselves.\\n   - **Rendering:** x-ray silhouettes were missing behind walls; the deep starting hollow hid the player; the version label showed \\\"?\\\"; the Knot Wall towered at full height.\\n   - **Building and mining:** the Hall room failed on uneven ground; damaged blocks healed between hits; stair lips blocked walking; the deep-water rule was wrong; Spin Stitch couldn't charge; room hints pointed at the tops of walls.\\n   - **Siege and boss:** Gnarlgrim could walk into the Rift's void; monsters spawning beyond the Rift got stuck; \\\"survive 3 waves\\\" only counted after the boss; the ballista's aim arc was too narrow, its bolts hit walls and fell short, and any hit knocked the player off it; skipping the finale never showed the results.\\n   - **Quests:** M12 needed a long walk back to the Professor to hand it in.\\n   - **Saves and co-op:** saves stored every plant in the world; co-op clients never saw monsters.\\n   - **Attract mode:** it silenced all audio, left a cutscene running, collided with a prop, and left its builder seated on a ballista.\\n   - **AI player:** seven faults, including out-of-reach targets, chasing monsters across the map, and a talk loop that never yielded.\\n2. **How many were critical or game breaking?** 8: the Hall softlock, blocks healing between hits, the boss falling into the void, the ballista dismount, the missing results screen, invisible monsters for co-op clients, the hidden player at the start, and silenced audio after the attract mode.\\n3. **Most helpful test:** the scripted playthrough from New Game to Chapter Clear. It found the block-healing, ballista, siege and finale bugs that no single-system check caught.\\n4. **Least helpful test:** the world-generation determinism check, which never failed.\\n\\n## Engine Feedback\\n1. **What I liked most:** the views are exact linear projections, so a voxel renderer plugged straight into the engine's depth-sorted queue, x-ray, lighting and particles. The rigs, dialog, menus, saves and settings came free.\\n2. **Did I get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. Wall items need a screen box for the x-ray pass, which I only found in the source. The default isometric view's block height isn't a whole number of pixels, so I made my own views.\\n3. **Most important thing I built myself:** the voxel world: storage, a renderer with cutaway and water, body physics with stairs, and pathfinding.\\n4. **Hardest part of the engine:** depth-sorting real 3D blocks in a 2D painter's queue designed for heightmap walls.\\n5. **What I changed in the engine, and why** (each change marked `// DQB:`):\\n   - A mouse-wheel accessor that works while the camera wheel is off, so the wheel can cycle the hotbar.\\n   - A right-stick flick for 90° camera turns.\\n   - A per-letter dialog hook for the voices.\\n   - A separate Voices audio bus.\\n   - Three tools drawn on the character rig: a darning stick, a cobble club and the Seam Ripper.\\n6. **One thing I would change:** a built-in voxel map type with its own depth-lift hook and occluder boxes.\\n\\n## Prompt Feedback\\n1. **What I liked most:** the clear definition of done and the detailed plan. The controller-first, 10-foot rules made UI decisions easy.\\n2. **What was confusing:** the plan's file names used another model and timestamp than TASK.md's.\\n3. **Hardest thing to do:** proving the whole chapter completes through real triggers, while also building netcode and an attract mode.\\n4. **What I would change:** a smaller slice or staged delivery. The scope is very large for one pass.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":464,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":862732,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":464},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\",\"uuid\":\"e6e49550-3830-4b9a-a5ab-1d901e4240ab\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:11:28.113Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CghUG26HtsCEpu7YVu5Rm\"}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"text\",\"text\":\"Stop hook feedback:\\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: Not satisfied on transcript evidence. The HTML is built and exit-interview.json parses with no empty fields, and the final reply contains the four sections. But TASK.md requires every feature implemented, and the transcript does not verify that. Specific gaps: the Quilting Bee's 'Knot Cutter' award was never verified by a passing run; its earlier 'won' check was changed to pass, not confirmed; the playthrough's first full pass never ran clean (later passes were only checked in part); the M13 siege and M14 boss steps were fixed by changing the test and game together, with no clean end-to-end pass recorded after the last change; and TASK.md's 'Usage' field is unknown with no attempt to estimate it. The grep for TODO/placeholder/stub was run on src, tests and tools, but the claim that none remain depends on a single search whose output was not shown in full.\"}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"b7d7e0cb-a26c-4fe8-90f7-7d5024813af2\",\"uuid\":\"22eebef5-4654-4773-8725-3a905dce23a6\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T07:11:30.301Z\",\"isSynthetic\":true}"]}]},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145/.tmp/att.mjs","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":7,"lines":["+import { load } from '../test/lib/load.mjs';","+const { G, game } = load(); game.advance(1);","+G.go('title', null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(.5); G.attract.reset(); game.advance(11);","+for (let s = 0; s < 120; s++) game.advance(1);","+console.log('beat', G.attract.BEATS[G.attract.beat].id, game.sceneName, G.overlay.list.map(o => o.kind), 'active', G.attract.active, 't', G.attract.t);","+game.input.tap('confirm'); for (let k = 0; k < 6; k++) { game.advance(1/120); console.log(k, game.sceneName, G.attract.active, game.input.anyPressed()); }","+game.advance(1); console.log(game.sceneName, G.attract.active);"]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145/test/suites/09-ui.test.mjs","hunks":[{"oldStart":12,"oldLines":7,"newStart":12,"newLines":7,"lines":["   G.go('menu', null, { fade: 0 }); game.advance(.2); const m = G.SCENES.menu;","   I.tap('down'); game.advance(.05); t('the d-pad moves the focus', m.focus.i === 1, m.focus.i);","   const L = m.layout(), it = L[3]; I.feed('move', it.x + 5, it.y + 5); game.advance(.05); t('hover moves the focus', m.focus.i === 3, m.focus.i);","-  I.feed('down', it.x + 5, it.y + 5); I.feed('up', it.x + 5, it.y + 5); game.advance(.2); t('a click activates', game.sceneName === G.SCENES.menu.items()[3].id || game.sceneName !== 'menu', game.sceneName);","+  I.feed('down', it.x + 5, it.y + 5); game.advance(1 / 120); I.feed('up', it.x + 5, it.y + 5); game.advance(.4); t('a click activates', game.sceneName === G.SCENES.menu.items()[3].id || game.sceneName !== 'menu', game.sceneName);","   t('pause actions list Dev Mode', G.pauseItems().filter(Boolean).some(a => a[0] === 'Dev Mode') && G.pauseItems().filter(Boolean).some(a => a[0] === 'How to Play'));","   t('no errors', game.errors.length === 0, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));"," };"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-215911__x5b1962/agent.out","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145/.tmp/att.mjs","/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145/test/suites/09-ui.test.mjs"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Xo4F5fd5THHNDVxrkq6576","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
