{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghUzxMWLVPLguqh9DmxH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019jbB9RtQkTh8qfQpLx5AbQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145; cat > ENGINE-CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2)\n\n`tools/patch-engine.mjs` applies every change to a pristine copy of the handoff engine and writes\n`engine/my-3d2dge.js`. Each patched spot carries an `AOA:` comment. Each change has a headless test.\n\n| # | Change | Why | Test |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1 | `✕ ○ □ △ ◀ ▶` added to the 5x7 font `G57` | `input.label()` returns PlayStation symbols the font could not draw; steppers need arrows | ui suite (glyphs) |\n| 2 | `glyphs` setting moved to the Game group, PlayStation by default, options PlayStation / Xbox; applied to every player | TASK.md: PlayStation glyphs by default with a Settings option for Xbox | ui suite |\n| 3 | `Dialog`: a function `voice` is called for every newly shown letter | Animalese voices letter by letter, in sync with the text | story / location dialogs |\n| 4a | A voice bus under the master, `audio.voiceVolume`, `audio.bus(name)` | the Voices volume setting | dev Voice Lab |\n| 4b | Music and sfx voices accept `wave` = a name in `audio.instruments` (PeriodicWave tables), `decay` (pluck envelope), `cutoff` (lowpass), `detune` (a second oscillator) | steel drum, marimba, pluck, bell, organ and pad for the tropical score | data suite builds every song |\n| 5 | Humanoid: `o.swim.shorts` draws swim shorts on the thighs; `rig.swimDraw(g, P)` is called inside the torso plate with its projected corners | swimsuit cuts and patterns without rewriting the HD draw | data suite dresses every suit |\n| 6 | `input.reserveCombo = [8, 9]`: Options (button 9) is ignored while Create (button 8) is held | an AI Hub rule (Create + Options opens the hub's bar) | hub harness |\n\nTouch-off mode (plan patch 7) needed no engine change: the game never asks for touch buttons and turns the touch stick\noff on touch-only devices, which keeps the corner's menu button.\nEOF\ncat > README-DEV.md <<'EOF'\n# Ahead or Alive: Xtreme Beach Volleyball — development\n\n- `node tools/patch-engine.mjs` — rebuild `engine/my-3d2dge.js` from the pristine handoff engine in `.src/` (see ENGINE-CHANGES.md).\n- `node tools/build.mjs` — concatenate `src/*.js` into `build/game.js` (one IIFE), write `build/dev.html` and the\n  deliverable `../AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145.html`.\n- `node test/run.mjs` — every suite; prints only failures and one count line. Flags: `--only=match,casino`,\n  `--skip-browser`, `--skip-hub`. The hub suite serves `test-output/hub-serve/` on 127.0.0.1 at a port the OS picks and\n  stops that server by its own PID.\n- `node tools/shots.mjs title map match …` — screenshots into `test-output/` (Playwright, file://).\n- `node tools/check.mjs <html>` — the engine's checker (errors, look notes).\n\nConventions: gameplay randomness only through `G.rng(stream)` (a test greps for `Math.random(`); every tuning number is\nin `G.TUNING` and read live from `G.T`; every scene goes through `G.wrapScene`; `game.debug.tools` drives the dev panel\nand the tests.\nEOF\nls","description":"Write engine changes and dev readme"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1724,"cache_read_input_tokens":703265,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1724},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_t