{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghV2neAUW8ETVb6bE6Mw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012Rr68esGVJ7gyTTtV3gYAw","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-DeadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolleyball-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261103-231145; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/05-data-text.js'; s=open(p).read()\nstart=s.index(\"G.FEEDBACK = {\"); end=s.index(\"};\", start)+2\ns=s[:start]+\"\"\"G.FEEDBACK = {\n  testing: [\n    'About 25 game issues: crashes from a name clash and a scoping slip, scenes drawn before they were entered, a sound table the browser rejected, an attract mode you could not leave during its photo beat, 50-touch rallies, AI skill that barely mattered, a slot machine paying 132%, a split-keyboard key clash on the join screen, missing font glyphs, and framing and overlap problems on several screens.',\n    'About 6: the title crash (two systems both named G.dev), a crash on every attack, the scene registry missing at load, the menu crashing when drawn before entry, the music instrument error, and the attract mode trapping the player.',\n    'The scripted whole-vacation playthrough (both endings, every story event, the casino, Pool Hop and saves) together with the AI-vs-AI match statistics; and, for online play, the AI Hub harness run in four scenarios.',\n    'The single-frame title screenshots and the engine checker\\\\'s view cycling: useful once each, but they could not show timing or motion, which only the scripted runs caught.'\n  ],\n  engine: [\n    'The Humanoid rig: one constructor gives a shaded, dressed, animated character that also draws its own portrait, and its pose can be post-processed, so swimsuits, new hair and every volleyball move were additions, not rewrites. The fixed-step clock made every test deterministic.',\n    'A little: I passed 0 as the alpha of groundRing, used a material pattern name that does not exist (plaster), and had to read the source to learn that joined players take the scene\\\\'s keys through halfKeys. The index answered most other questions.',\n    'The volleyball itself: a closed-form ball, contact planning, the timing judge, blocks, faults, the AI and its error model; and the swimsuit cuts and patterns drawn inside the torso.',\n    'Hooking into the Humanoid\\\\'s draw, which is one large function: swimsuits needed an engine patch for a callback.',\n    'Six patches, each marked AOA: in the source: PlayStation symbols and arrows in the 5x7 font; the Button symbols setting (PlayStation by default, Xbox option, in the Game group); a per-letter function voice in Dialog; a voice bus and bus() accessor; named instrument waves, pluck decay, lowpass and detune for music; swim shorts and a swimDraw hook in the Humanoid; reserveCombo so Options is ignored while Create is held (an AI Hub rule).',\n    'A documented per-part draw hook for outfits, so new clothing needs no engine edit.'\n  ],\n  prompt: [\n    'It is concrete about the player\\\\'s experience (a 10-foot controller-first UI, glyph rules, the touch-only gate, the attract mode, dev sliders) and about the deliverables, so done is clear.',\n    'The plan asks for far more content than one medium-effort session can build in full; how to trade breadth for depth was left to judgement.',\n    'Fitting a five-day vacation sim, three minigames and online play around a timing-based sports core, with every screen controller-first.',\n    'Say which parts of a plan are musts and which are stretches, so the builder can scope deliberately.'\n  ]\n};\"\"\"+s[end:]\ns=s.replace(\"animation: 'The engine\\\\'s procedural rig animation (walk, run, idle, jump, held poses) with an arm-IK overlay (E.ik3) wrapped around solvePose for every volleyball move, celebration, emote and photo pose, driven from the match\\\\'s contact plan; no motion-capture clips',\",\"animation: 'The engine\\\\'s procedural rig animation (walk, run, idle, jump, held poses, flips) with an arm-IK overlay (E.ik3) wrapped around solvePose for every volleyball move, celebration, emote and photo pose, driven from the match\\\\'s contact plan; no motion-capture clips',\")\ns=s.replace(\"testing: 'Headless suites behind one command (node test/run.mjs, prints only failures and a count) using game.advance and game.debug; a scripted vacation playthrough; Playwright browser checks and screenshots; the AI Hub harness; no subagents used for review',\",\"testing: '14 suites behind one command (node test/run.mjs prints only failures and a count; 230 checks): headless game.advance / game.debug suites for core, data, ball, rules, match, vacation, casino, Pool Hop, UI, attract, dev mode and a scripted whole-vacation playthrough to both endings; a Playwright browser tour with a touch-only device; the AI Hub harness in four scenarios; screenshots and the engine checker for looks; no subagents',\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode test/run.mjs --only=core,data 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Write final feedback text into the About data"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2433,"cache_read_input_tokens":704989,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2433},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf","uuid":"92aa934b-5982-4ec4-aed7-d1bec1bd137c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:21:37.825Z","request_id":"req_011CghV2n6vLkwfEa6Lt573c","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_012Rr68esGVJ7gyTTtV3gYAw":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build__20261103-231145__x8def6b/work/AheadOrAliveXtremeBeachVolle