{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CghVS98rCF3D11mWZAWxD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I audited the source against TASK.md and found one real gap: saving was never connected in the shipped game. The save hooks were only set up inside the tests, so in the real game, saving to a slot, the autosave, Continue and Load had nothing to save or restore. That's fixed: saves are set up when the game starts, and a new test checks that after an autosave the menu offers Continue and loads the vacation, without the test setting anything up itself. The game is rebuilt and the full test command passes all 232 checks, including the AI Hub harness and the browser run.\n\n**The audit**\n- **Stub search:** no TODO, TBD, FIXME, placeholder, lorem, \"not implemented\", \"coming soon\" or \"stub\" text in the source. The only hits were time-of-day names like `todOverride`. No function has an empty body.\n- **TASK.md features:**\n\n| TASK.md feature | Where it lives | Tested by |\n|---|---|---|\n| The game: volleyball, vacation, places, shops, Pool Hop, casino, album, credits | its own module and scene each | the match, vacation, casino, Pool Hop and playthrough suites |\n| Save and load | the vacation module, set up at boot | the vacation suite (new test) |\n| Dev mode with live sliders and reset | the dev and tuning modules | the dev suite; the browser tour opens it from the pause menu |\n| Attract mode after 10 s idle | the attract module | the attract suite, headless and in the browser |\n| Multiplayer, online and on one machine | the hub module and the Beach Match join screen | the hub harness in four scenarios; the playthrough |\n| PlayStation glyphs by default, Xbox option, keyboard and mouse prompts | the input module and the Button symbols setting | the UI suite |\n| Touch-only \"Controller or keyboard required\" screen, attract still runs | the title and attract modules | the browser suite, on an emulated touch device |\n| About & Credits with the four sections | the text data | the About page and the exit interview are built from the same text |\n| All audio in code, gibberish voices | the audio and music modules | no audio files in the build |\n\n**About the gaps the review raised**\n- **The island map:** it does have every landmark the plan names: the volcano, the lagoon pool, the courts, the Promenade, the villas, the casino, the Dock with Sonny's seaplane, and the lighthouse. My earlier description undersold it.\n- **Postcards:** each one is saved as a full record of the shot (place, camera, people, poses, filter, frame) plus a small picture. What's missing is rebuilding the album view live from that record, which the plan wanted; TASK.md doesn't require it.\n- **Long AI rallies:** they occasionally run to about 20 touches. That's a balance choice, not a missing feature.\n- **Motion-capture clips:** I didn't use them. TASK.md asks for the engine's native animation system as the base, and that is what the game uses.\n\nThe About page and `exit-interview.json` now count about 26 issues, 7 of them critical (the save bug added to each), and 232 checks. The exit interview still parses with every field filled. The Source Information, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback in my previous reply still stand; only Testing Feedback changes:\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 26 game issues. The new one is saves that were never connected in the real game (only the tests set them up). The rest are as listed before: crashes from a name clash and a scoping slip, a scene drawn before it was set up, a sound table the browser rejected, an attract mode you couldn't leave, 50-touch rallies, AI skill that barely mattered, a slot machine paying 132%, a split-keyboard key clash, missing font characters, and framing and overlap problems.\n2. **How many would be considered critical issues / game breaking?** About 7: saving, autosave and Continue doing nothing; the title crash; a crash on every attack; the scene list missing at load; the menu crashing when drawn before it was set up; the music instrument error; and the attract mode trapping the player.\n3. **What was the most helpful test you ran?** The scripted whole-vacation playthrough with the AI-vs-AI match statistics; for online play, the AI Hub harness in four scenarios; and this final source audit, which found the save bug.\n4. **What was the least helpful test you ran?** Single-frame screenshots and the engine checker's view cycling. Each was useful once, but neither shows timing or motion."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":686,"cache_read_input_tokens":721680,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":686},"output_tokens":677,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7b48fecc-086c-4274-afae-e17752649adf","uuid":"11252917-7b0e-4ff7-8559-52462ca2f47b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T07:26:46.947Z","request_id":"req_011CghVS8qzL5M5dCQrc7z8n"}
